HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/hunter/taming-the-beast-alliance"] = [==[guide: Taming the Beast (Alliance)
id: forever/class/hunter/taming-the-beast-alliance
level: 10-10
map: 1429
section Elayaa Easewind
tip At 10, Elayaa Easewind, a hunter trainer on Zephras Isle, may send you on to Valanaar with Taming the Beast. It is only a pointer: skip it if you are already in Valanaar.
level 10
accept 94007
section Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar
tip Quel'ana Quickgale stands with the trainers by Valanaar's west gate, Quel'dora Quickgale beside her.
turnin 94007
accept 94978
section Windsong Crawler
tip Windsong Crawlers live only by water: the nearest scuttle along the shore south-west of Valanaar, among the crabs. How the rod works: target a living crawler, use the Taming Rod and stand still for the whole channel while it hits you; moving, fighting back or anyone else's help breaks it and costs one of the rod's few charges. Killing one does not count. Keep each rod: it goes back to Quel'ana.
objective 94978.1 kill
turnin 94978
accept 94979
section Ornery Galestrider
tip Dismiss the crawler first (right-click the pet portrait, Dismiss Pet). Ornery Galestriders graze in the Gustberry Lowlands, the fields a short walk west and south-west of Valanaar.
objective 94979.1 kill
turnin 94979
accept 94013
section Vuldren Alpha
tip Dismiss the galestrider. Vuldren Alphas hunt in the same Gustberry Lowlands, a little further south.
objective 94013.1 kill
turnin 94013
accept 94050
turnin 94050
section Grif Wildheart in Kharanos
tip At 10 go to Grif Wildheart, the hunter trainer at the smithy in Kharanos. The Hunter's Path from Olmin Burningbeard in Ironforge, Tristane Shadowstone north-west of Kharanos or Einris Brightspear in Stormwind also leads here, for a little experience; it is only a pointer. In Elwynn at 10 instead? Josephine Carson's chain in Goldshire teaches the same.
level 10 when !turnedin 94792
accept 6064 when !turnedin 94792
section Large Crag Boar
tip Large Crag Boars (level 6-7) root around the fields west, south and north-west of Kharanos and respawn every 3 minutes. How the rod works: target a living beast, use the Taming Rod and stand still for the whole channel while it hits you. Moving, fighting back, being out of range or anyone else's help breaks it and costs one of the rod's few charges; if they run out, destroy the rod, abandon the quest and take it again from Grif. The boars use Rushing Charge from 25 yards, so start with the rod, not Auto Shot. Keep each rod: it goes back to Grif.
objective 6064.1 kill when !turnedin 94792
turnin 6064 when !turnedin 94792
accept 6084 when !turnedin 94792
section Snow Leopard
tip Dismiss the boar first (right-click the pet portrait, Dismiss Pet): a released practice pet can turn on you. Snow Leopards (level 7-8) prowl the slopes south-east of Kharanos, more north-west and west of it; the smaller Juvenile Snow Leopards do not count.
objective 6084.1 kill when !turnedin 94792
turnin 6084 when !turnedin 94792
accept 6085 when !turnedin 94792
section Ice Claw Bear
tip Dismiss the leopard. Ice Claw Bears (level 7-8) roam the hills around Kharanos, many south-east of it and more north-west toward Anvilmar; their Ice Claw hits hard, so start at full health.
objective 6085.1 kill when !turnedin 94792
turnin 6085 when !turnedin 94792
accept 6086 when !turnedin 94792
section Belia Thundergranite in Ironforge
tip Belia Thundergranite, the pet trainer, stands in the Hall of Arms in Ironforge's Military Ward, by the hunter trainers.
turnin 6086 when !turnedin 94792
section Dazalar in Dolanaar
tip At 10 go to Dazalar, the hunter trainer in Dolanaar. The Hunter's Path from Ayanna Everstride at Aldrassil, Jocaste in Darnassus, Einris Brightspear in Stormwind, Olmin Burningbeard in Ironforge or Grif Wildheart in Kharanos also leads here, for a little experience; it is only a pointer. In Elwynn at 10 instead? Josephine Carson's chain in Goldshire teaches the same.
level 10 when !turnedin 94792
accept 6063 when !turnedin 94792
section Webwood Lurker
tip Webwood Lurkers (level 5-6) creep through the woods just north-east, south-west and east of Dolanaar. How the rod works: target a living beast, use the Taming Rod and stand still for the whole channel while it hits you; moving, attacking it or anyone else's help breaks it and costs one of the rod's few charges (out of charges: destroy the rod, abandon the quest, take it again). Their Web roots you but does not break the channel if you keep still. Keep each rod: it goes back to Dazalar.
objective 6063.1 kill when !turnedin 94792
turnin 6063 when !turnedin 94792
accept 6101 when !turnedin 94792
section Nightsaber Stalker
tip Dismiss the spider first (right-click the pet portrait, Dismiss Pet): a released practice pet can turn on you. Nightsaber Stalkers (level 7-8) lie on the hillside south of Lake Al'Ameth, south of Dolanaar; the plain Nightsabers by the village do not count.
objective 6101.1 kill when !turnedin 94792
turnin 6101 when !turnedin 94792
accept 6102 when !turnedin 94792
section Strigid Screecher
tip Dismiss the cat. Strigid Screechers (level 7-8), owls, perch in the woods south, south-west and west of Dolanaar.
objective 6102.1 kill when !turnedin 94792
turnin 6102 when !turnedin 94792
accept 6103 when !turnedin 94792
section Jocaste in Darnassus
tip Take the road west from Dolanaar to Darnassus. Jocaste stands inside the Cenarion Enclave with the hunter trainers; Silvaria, the pet trainer, is up the ramp next to her.
turnin 6103 when !turnedin 94792
section Josephine Carson in Goldshire
tip At 10 go to Josephine Carson, the hunter trainer who stands with the other trainers by the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire; Isaac Chan, the pet trainer, is beside her. Skyborne: this is for one who left Zephras Isle without taming; it teaches the same.
level 10
accept 94792
section Rockhide Boar
tip Rockhide Boars (level 7-8) graze in three herds south and south-east of Goldshire, toward the Maclure Vineyards. How the rod works: target a living beast, use the Taming Rod and stand still for the whole channel while it hits you. Moving, fighting back, a heal from someone else or anyone else hitting the beast breaks it and costs one of the rod's few charges; if they run out, destroy the rod, abandon the quest and take it again. The boars use Rushing Charge, so start with the rod, not Auto Shot. Killing a boar does not count. Keep each rod: it goes back to Josephine. A Dwarf or Night Elf who took Josephine's rod instead of their home trainer's is led through Goldshire from here.
objective 94792.1 kill when !turnedin 6063
turnin 94792 when !turnedin 6063
accept 94863 when !turnedin 6063
section Gray Forest Wolf
tip Dismiss the boar first (right-click the pet portrait, Dismiss Pet): a released practice pet can turn on you. Gray Forest Wolves (level 7-8) run in the woods east of Goldshire, east of Crystal Lake.
objective 94863.1 kill when !turnedin 6063
turnin 94863 when !turnedin 6063
accept 94864 when !turnedin 6063
section Young Forest Bear
tip Dismiss the wolf. Young Forest Bears (level 8-9) roam the woods just south of Goldshire, with more south-west and south-east of town.
objective 94864.1 kill when !turnedin 6063
turnin 94864 when !turnedin 6063
accept 94793 when !turnedin 6063
turnin 94793 when !turnedin 6063
section Your first pet
tip Tame Beast works like the rod: a beast of your level or lower, a channel you must not move during, the beast hitting you all the while. A pet keeps the level you tame it at and levels up with you; it can never be above your level, so tame one close to yours. Each family has its own ability on Forever (a boar's Charge, for example). For levelling, a cat hits hardest (Claw and Bite) and a boar takes more punishment.
note Near Goldshire there are no cats: Prowlers (wolves, level 9-10) roam eastern Elwynn, Longsnouts (boars, 10-11) its far south-west by the Westfall border; at 12-13, Young Goretusks (boars) graze the fields of northern Westfall. only Human
note Near Kharanos: Snow Leopards (cats, level 7-8) prowl all over Dun Morogh, Scarred Crag Boars (9-10) its east toward Loch Modan; at 10-11, Mountain Boars roam western Loch Modan. only Dwarf
note Near Dolanaar: Elder Nightsabers (cats, level 8-9) and Feral Nightsabers (cats, 10-11) prowl the woods of north-western Teldrassil. only NightElf
note Near Valanaar: Vuldren Alphas (level 10), the beast of your last practice tame, hunt the Gustberry Lowlands; Shriekling Matriarchs (raptors, level 9) nest just west of Valanaar; Shadowgale Urseras (bears, 10-11) roam the north of Zephras Isle. only Skyborne
note Feed Pet: open your spellbook, cast Feed Pet and click a food your pet's family eats (the pet's tooltip lists them: cats eat meat and fish, boars almost anything). Raw meat looted from beasts counts. To buy: Toddrick the butcher in Goldshire, Jaeana in Darnassus and the innkeepers on Zephras Isle sell meat; the innkeepers of Kharanos and Dolanaar sell bread. Food near the pet's level makes it happiest; much lower food gives about half. You cannot feed in combat.
note Happiness: the face on the pet frame. An unhappy pet does three quarters of its damage, a happy one a quarter more. Happiness drains slowly, faster when the pet dies; a pet left unhappy too long can run away.
note Loyalty grows with time and kills. Each loyalty rank raises the training points you spend in Beast Training (pet level times loyalty rank minus one).
note Beast Training (spellbook, General tab) teaches your current pet the abilities you know. To learn a new ability or rank: leave your pet with a stable master (Erma in Goldshire, Shelby Stoneflint in Kharanos, Seriadne in Dolanaar, Genn Fairweather on Zephras Isle), tame a beast that has it (its pet spellbook tab shows what it knows), use the ability in fights until the game says you learned it, then take your own pet back and teach it with Beast Training. A pet holds four active abilities at most.
note Pet trainers sell Growl ranks and resistances. Alliance: Isaac Chan in Goldshire, Karrina Mekenda by the hunter trainers in Stormwind's Dwarven District, Peria Lamenur in Kharanos, Belia Thundergranite in Ironforge's Hall of Arms, Keldas in Dolanaar, Silvaria in Darnassus' Cenarion Enclave, Quel'dora Quickgale in Valanaar.
note Call Pet, Dismiss Pet and Revive Pet are in your spellbook now; Mend Pet comes from your trainer at 12. A dead pet needs Revive Pet; one that is away more than about 100 yards is dismissed and comes back with Call Pet.]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/hunter/taming-the-beast-horde", title = "Taming the Beast (Horde)", faction = "Horde", race = "Orc, Troll, Tauren, Skyborne", class = "Hunter", levels = "10-10", zone = "Durotar", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/hunter/taming-the-beast-horde"] = [==[guide: Taming the Beast (Horde)
id: forever/class/hunter/taming-the-beast-horde
level: 10-10
map: 1411
section Thotar in Razor Hill
tip At 10 go to Thotar, the hunter trainer inside the barracks in Razor Hill. If Sian'dur in Orgrimmar, Kali Remik in Sen'jin Village or Kary Thunderhorn in Thunder Bluff hands you The Hunter's Path, take it and hand it to Thotar for a little experience; it is only a pointer, and you can take the first rod without it.
level 10
accept 6062
section Dire Mottled Boar
tip Dire Mottled Boars (level 6-7) roam just north and west of Razor Hill. How the rod works: target a living beast, use the Taming Rod from inside its range and stand still for the whole channel while the beast hits you. Moving, fighting back, a heal from someone else or anyone else hitting the beast breaks it and costs one of the rod's few charges; if they run out, destroy the rod, abandon the quest and take it again from Thotar. The boars charge from 20 yards, so start with the rod, not Auto Shot. The tamed boar becomes your pet for practice. Keep each rod: it goes back to Thotar.
objective 6062.1 kill
turnin 6062
accept 6083
section Surf Crawler
tip First dismiss the boar (right-click your pet's portrait, Dismiss Pet): a released practice pet can turn on you. Surf Crawlers (level 7-8) walk the beaches around Sen'jin Village and the Echo Isles; the small Pygmy Surf Crawlers do not count. A crawler runs for help at 15% health, so do not hurt it.
objective 6083.1 kill
turnin 6083
accept 6082
section Armored Scorpid
tip Dismiss the crawler. Armored Scorpids (level 7-8) crawl the dry plains west and south-west of Razor Hill, some just south of the road west out of town; Track Beasts shows them. Their hits can break the channel: start at full health and keep still.
objective 6082.1 kill
turnin 6082
accept 6081
section Ormak Grimshot in Orgrimmar
tip Follow the road north to Orgrimmar's gate. Ormak Grimshot stands with the hunter trainers in the Valley of Honor, up the ramp at the city's east side; Xao'tsu, the pet trainer, is a few steps north of him.
turnin 6081
section Yaw Sharpmane at Bloodhoof
tip At 10 go to Yaw Sharpmane, who stands at the north edge of Bloodhoof Village. The Hunter's Path from Kary Thunderhorn in Thunder Bluff, Sian'dur in Orgrimmar or Thotar in Razor Hill also leads here, for a little experience; it is only a pointer.
level 10
accept 6061
section Adult Plainstrider
tip Adult Plainstriders (level 6-7) walk the plains south-west and north-west of Bloodhoof Village. How the rod works: target a living beast, use the Taming Rod and stand still for the whole channel while it hits you; moving, fighting back or anyone else's help breaks it and costs one of the rod's few charges (out of charges: destroy the rod, abandon the quest, take it again). A plainstrider flees at 25% health, so do not damage it first. Keep each rod: it goes back to Yaw.
objective 6061.1 kill
turnin 6061
accept 6087
section Prairie Stalker
tip Dismiss the plainstrider first (right-click the pet portrait, Dismiss Pet): a released practice pet may attack you. Prairie Stalkers (level 7-8) roam the grass north of Bloodhoof Village.
objective 6087.1 kill
turnin 6087
accept 6088
section Swoop
tip Dismiss the stalker. Swoops (level 7-9) glide over the plains north-west and north-east of Bloodhoof; the Taloned Swoops do not count. A Swoop's knockdown breaks the channel, but it lands only once per channel: start the rod just after it has used it.
objective 6088.1 kill
turnin 6088
accept 6089
section Holt Thunderhorn in Thunder Bluff
tip Head north to Thunder Bluff and take a lift up. Holt Thunderhorn stands with the hunter trainers on Hunter Rise; Hesuwa Thunderhorn, the pet trainer, is nearby.
turnin 6089
section Elayaa Easewind
tip At 10, Elayaa Easewind, a hunter trainer on Zephras Isle, may send you on to Valanaar with Taming the Beast. It is only a pointer: skip it if you are already in Valanaar.
level 10
accept 94007
section Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar
tip Quel'ana Quickgale stands with the trainers by Valanaar's west gate, Quel'dora Quickgale beside her.
turnin 94007
accept 94978
section Windsong Crawler
tip Windsong Crawlers live only by water: the nearest scuttle along the shore south-west of Valanaar, among the crabs. How the rod works: target a living crawler, use the Taming Rod and stand still for the whole channel while it hits you; moving, fighting back or anyone else's help breaks it and costs a charge. Killing one does not count.
objective 94978.1 kill
turnin 94978
accept 94979
section Ornery Galestrider
tip Dismiss the crawler first (right-click the pet portrait, Dismiss Pet). Ornery Galestriders graze in the Gustberry Lowlands, the fields a short walk west and south-west of Valanaar.
objective 94979.1 kill
turnin 94979
accept 94013
section Vuldren Alpha
tip Dismiss the galestrider. Vuldren Alphas hunt in the same Gustberry Lowlands, a little further south.
objective 94013.1 kill
turnin 94013
accept 94050
turnin 94050
section Your first pet
tip Tame Beast works like the rod: a beast of your level or lower, a channel you must not move during, the beast hitting you all the while. A pet keeps the level you tame it at and levels up with you; it can never be above your level, so tame one close to yours. Each family has its own ability on Forever (a boar's Charge, for example). For levelling, a cat hits hardest (Claw and Bite) and a boar takes more punishment.
note Near Razor Hill: Durotar Tigers (cats, level 7-8) roam the south of Durotar, from Sen'jin Village down the coast; Venomtail Scorpids (9-10) the north-west toward Orgrimmar; at 11-12, Savannah Huntresses (cats) prowl the plains around the Crossroads in the Barrens. only Orc,Troll
note Near Bloodhoof: Flatland Prowlers (cats, level 9) and Prairie Wolf Alphas (wolves, 9-10) roam the plains of northern Mulgore; at 11-12, Savannah Huntresses (cats) prowl around the Crossroads in the Barrens. only Tauren
note Near Valanaar: Vuldren Alphas (level 10), the beast of your last practice tame, hunt the Gustberry Lowlands; Shriekling Matriarchs (raptors, level 9) nest just west of Valanaar; Shadowgale Urseras (bears, 10-11) roam the north of Zephras Isle. only Skyborne
note Feed Pet: open your spellbook, cast Feed Pet and click a food your pet's family eats (the pet's tooltip lists them: cats eat meat and fish, boars almost anything). Raw meat looted from beasts counts. To buy: Grimtak the butcher and Innkeeper Grosk in Razor Hill sell meat, Kaga Mistrunner in Thunder Bluff and the innkeepers on Zephras Isle too; Bloodhoof's innkeeper and bakers sell bread. Food near the pet's level makes it happiest; much lower food gives about half. You cannot feed in combat.
note Happiness: the face on the pet frame. An unhappy pet does three quarters of its damage, a happy one a quarter more. Happiness drains slowly, faster when the pet dies; a pet left unhappy too long can run away.
note Loyalty grows with time and kills. Each loyalty rank raises the training points you spend in Beast Training (pet level times loyalty rank minus one).
note Beast Training (spellbook, General tab) teaches your current pet the abilities you know. To learn a new ability or rank: leave your pet with a stable master (Shoja'my in Razor Hill, Seikwa at Bloodhoof, Genn Fairweather on Zephras Isle, Xon'cha in Orgrimmar), tame a beast that has it (its pet spellbook tab shows what it knows), use the ability in fights until the game says you learned it, then take your own pet back and teach it with Beast Training. A pet holds four active abilities at most.
note Pet trainers sell Growl ranks and resistances. Horde: Harruk in Razor Hill, Reban Freerunner at Bloodhoof, Xao'tsu in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, Hesuwa Thunderhorn on Thunder Bluff's Hunter Rise, Quel'dora Quickgale in Valanaar, later Grokor in Stonard and Zudd at Grom'gol.
note Call Pet, Dismiss Pet and Revive Pet are in your spellbook now; Mend Pet comes from your trainer at 12. A dead pet needs Revive Pet; one that is away more than about 100 yards is dismissed and comes back with Call Pet.]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/hunter/the-hunters-charm", title = "The Hunter's Charm", class = "Hunter", levels = "50-52", zone = "Azshara", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/hunter/the-hunters-charm"] = [==[guide: The Hunter's Charm
id: forever/class/hunter/the-hunters-charm
level: 50-52
map: 1447
section The Hunter's Charm (Alliance)
tip At 50 any Alliance hunter trainer offers it: Ulfir Ironbeard in Stormwind's Dwarven District, Olmin Burningbeard in Ironforge's Hall of Arms or Dorion in Darnassus' Cenarion Enclave.
level 50
accept 8151
section The Hunter's Charm (Horde)
tip At 50 any Horde hunter trainer offers it: Ormak Grimshot in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor or Holt Thunderhorn on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff.
level 50
accept 8151
section Ogtinc
tip Ogtinc lives on a raised spot on the cliffs at the north-east rim of the Ruins of Eldarath, west-central Azshara. Keep to the high ridges around the ruins: the pit below does not lead up to him. Alliance: fly to Talrendis Point; Horde: fly to Valormok, a short ride west of him.
getfp Talrendis Point only Alliance
getfp Valormok only Horde
turnin 8151
accept 8153
section Courser Antlers
tip You need two Perfect Courser Antlers. Mosshoof Coursers (level 52-53, deer) graze all over Azshara and drop one about one kill in twelve, so expect two dozen kills. Good herds: north of the Thalassian Base Camp in the north, and the hills north-east and south-east of Valormok; the Lake Mennar area also has elite giants and dragonkin. They Enrage at 30% health. Coursers share spawn points with the Thunderhead hippogryphs: if none are around, kill the hippogryphs and coursers may spawn instead. Respawn is about five and a half minutes.
objective 8153.1 collect
section Ogtinc
turnin 8153
accept 8231
section Wavethrashing
tip You need six Wavethrasher Scales. Wavethrashers (three-headed sea beasts) live along Azshara's coasts, mostly underwater: the Young Wavethrashers (level 51-52) of the north-east shore drop a scale about one kill in three, the Wavethrashers (52-53) of the east coast by the Tower of Eldara about as often (a few walk the beach there), the Great Wavethrashers (53-54) of the south-east shore about one in seven. Track Beasts does not show them; fight them where you can breathe, and bring water breathing if you can. Elite sharks swim the deeper water.
objective 8231.1 collect
section Ogtinc
turnin 8231
accept 8232
section Morphaz in the Sunken Temple
tip Morphaz is an elite green drake (level 52) inside the Sunken Temple, a five-player dungeon: needs a group of five. The temple stands in the Pool of Tears in eastern Swamp of Sorrows: climb its outer steps, dive into the flooded hall and follow the stairs down to the entrance. Horde: fly to Stonard; Alliance: fly to Nethergarde Keep or Darkshire and ride on. He is not there when you arrive: first kill the six troll guardians on the platforms around the upper ring, which opens the way down to Jammal'an the Prophet in the Pit of Sacrifice. Jammal'an's death brings out two drakes, Weaver and Dreamscythe (pull them one at a time); when both are dead, Morphaz and Hazzas appear together and cannot be split. Clear the dragonkin around the pit first, because they call for help. Morphaz uses Acid Breath and Wing Flap. The tooth always drops. Warriors in the group may want the same run for the voodoo feathers of the balcony trolls.
objective 8232.1 collect @ 69.0 54.0 map=1435
section The Green Drake
tip In Classic Ogtinc let you choose the Devilsaur Eye, the Devilsaur Tooth or the Hunting Spear here. Forever's change notes say the choice is gone, though its quest page still lists three unnamed rewards: look at the reward window before you hand in.
turnin 8232]==]
