HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/mage/celestial-orb"] = [==[guide: Celestial Orb and Stave
id: forever/class/mage/celestial-orb
level: 35-40
map: 1445
section Return to the Marsh (Stormwind)
tip Jennea Cannon at the top of the Wizard's Sanctum, Stormwind's Mage Quarter, sends you back to Tabetha; Bink in Ironforge gives the same quest.
level 35
accept 1953
section Return to the Marsh (Orgrimmar)
tip Deino, one of Orgrimmar's mage trainers in Darkbriar Lodge, sends you back to Tabetha; Anastasia Hartwell in the Undercity and Ursyn Ghull in Thunder Bluff give the same quest.
level 35
accept 1953
section Tabetha
tip Tabetha's cottage is deep in the marsh west of Theramore, just north of the Stonemaul Ruins; come in from the west road, the elites roam its east side.
turnin 1953
accept 1954
section The Infernal Orb
tip The Burning Blade Summoners (level 38-39, not elite) work the Mannoroc Coven in southern Desolace, east of Shadowprey Village, and every one carries an Infernal Orb. They cast Shadow Bolt from 40 yards, keep an imp at their side and run for help at low health; Nether Maidens patrol the pillared ruin beside them, so pull with care. Horde mages: one more summoner stands alone in western Mulgore, south-west of Thunder Bluff.
objective 1954.1 collect
section The Exorcism
tip Back at Tabetha's. Hand in the orb now; The Exorcism waits for level 38. Kill the critters around the cottage first: they join the fight. Accepting The Exorcism starts a 3 minute timer, and Tabetha calls the Demon of the Orb out in her garden: a level 40 elite that resists many spells, roots and slows. Grouping up is encouraged: a mage of 40 may need help or potions, at about 45 it is soloable. You can pull it from range from the dock. The timer keeps running after it dies, so hand the quest in straight away. If time runs out, abandon the quest and take it again; she calls the demon again.
turnin 1954
level 38
accept 1955
objective 1955.1 kill
turnin 1955
accept 1956
section Power in Uldaman
tip Uldaman is a dungeon in the northern Badlands: a group of five, from level 40 here. Go in by the rear entrance, a cave in Dustwind Gulch south-east of the main entrance (elite dragons fly nearby): the Obsidian Sentinel (level 42 elite) stands just past the first door. At 80, 60, 40 and 20 percent it breaks off an Obsidian Shard, an elite too; while a shard lives, both reflect targeted spells, so use area spells and your wand on them. A solo trick: step out through the nearby zone line each time a shard appears; the Sentinel heals but keeps shrinking. It always drops the power source, and takes 2 hours to come back.
level 40
objective 1956.1 collect @ 49.1 13.7 map=1418
section Mana Surges
tip Back to Tabetha. Accepting Mana Surges opens a rift beside her cottage and starts a 10 minute timer: twelve Mana Surges (level 40, Shock and Lightning Bolt) come out about four at a time. Attacking one does not pull the rest. Standing at the edge of the field draws them all; the tree south-west of it is out of their reach but in your spell range. Kill twelve and hand in before the timer runs out.
turnin 1956
accept 1957
objective 1957.1 kill
turnin 1957
accept 1958
turnin 1958
section Tabetha's Task (optional)
tip At 40 the mage trainers who send you to Tabetha (Jennea Cannon, Bink, Anastasia Hartwell, Deino) also have Tabetha's Task, a quest any class can do. Tabetha then wants the Tiara of the Deep from Hydromancer Velratha, a level 46 elite naga in Zul'Farrak, the troll dungeon in north-western Tanaris: a group of five, level 44-54. The reward window shows the Spellshifter Rod and the Gemshale Pauldrons.
level 40
accept 2861
turnin 2861
accept 2846
section Tiara of the Deep in Zul'Farrak
tip Zul'Farrak, the troll dungeon in north-western Tanaris, needs a group of five; the guide waits for level 44. Hydromancer Velratha is one of the bosses by the sacred pool, and the tiara always drops.
level 44 when onquest 2846
