HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/mage/destroy-morphaz", title = "Destroy Morphaz", class = "Mage", levels = "50-54", zone = "Azshara", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/mage/destroy-morphaz"] = [==[guide: Destroy Morphaz
id: forever/class/mage/destroy-morphaz
level: 50-54
map: 1447
section Magecraft (Stormwind)
tip Maginor Dumas, the Master Mage, stands in the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind's Mage Quarter; Dink in Ironforge gives the same quest.
level 50
accept 8250
section Magecraft (Orgrimmar)
tip Uthel'nay, one of Orgrimmar's mage trainers in Darkbriar Lodge, gives it; so do Pierce Shackleton in the Undercity and Archmage Shymm in Thunder Bluff.
level 50
accept 8250
section Sanath Lim-yo
tip Fly to Talrendis Point (Alliance) or Valormok (Horde). Sanath Lim-yo camps below his master's tower, a short way east of Valormok: from the fork of Azshara's main road at the Ruins of Eldarath, head straight north to the cliffs. Get off your mount before he teleports you up, or the teleport may not take you. A trail with no enemies climbs to Archmage Xylem at the top of the tower; an attendant at the top sends you back down, as often as you like.
turnin 8250
accept 8251
section Glittering Dust
tip The blood elves hold the Thalassian Base Camp on the hills of north-eastern Azshara. Blood Elf Surveyors (51-52, Fire Nova up close) and Reclaimers (52-53, Fireball, and they heal and Renew each other) each drop the dust about one time in four; they spot you from far off, so pull at the edges. They come back after 5 1/2 minutes.
objective 8251.1 collect
section Archmage Xylem
tip Back to Sanath Lim-yo, who teleports you up to the tower.
turnin 8251
accept 8252
section Enchanted Coral
tip The Spitelash Sirens (level 50-52) walk the ruins and beaches around the Ruins of Eldarath and the bay east of Valormok, often three together, and a few stand inside the Temple of Zin-Malor; each drops a coral about one time in four. The Spitelash Screamers look almost the same but never drop it. Killing the other naga there makes more Sirens appear in their spots. Lingering Highborne ghosts wander the ruins: watch your back.
objective 8252.1 collect
section Archmage Xylem again
tip Back to Sanath Lim-yo and up to the tower.
turnin 8252
accept 8253
section Morphaz
tip The Temple of Atal'Hakkar, the Sunken Temple, lies in the Pool of Tears: climb the steps into the sunken building, swim down through it and follow the passage down to the portal. A group of five, level 50-54. Morphaz is not waiting when you arrive. First kill the six troll guardians (elites of 50-52) on the platforms around the upper ring; that opens the way down (the left-hand ramp from the entrance) to Jammal'an the Prophet and Ogom the Wretched in the Pit of Sacrifice. Once Jammal'an dies, two green drakes, Weaver and Dreamscythe, come out and patrol the pit: pull them one at a time. When both are dead, Morphaz (level 52 elite, Acid Breath and Wing Flap) and Hazzas appear together and cannot be split, so fight both. The shard always drops. Hunters, Priests and Rogues of 50 need Morphaz too: a group of them shares one clear.
objective 8253.1 collect @ 69.9 53.6 map=1435
section The Arcane Shard
tip Back to Azshara, Sanath Lim-yo and the tower. Look at the reward window before you hand in: Classic offered the Arcane Crystal Pendant, the Fire Ruby or the Glacial Spike, and Forever's notes say the choice may be gone.
turnin 8253]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/mage/ju-ju-heaps", title = "Ley or Arcane Staff or Orb (Horde)", faction = "Horde", class = "Mage", levels = "10-12", zone = "Durotar", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/mage/ju-ju-heaps"] = [==[guide: Ley or Arcane Staff or Orb (Horde)
id: forever/class/mage/ju-ju-heaps
level: 10-12
map: 1411
section Un'thuwa
tip Un'thuwa, the troll mage trainer, stands in Sen'jin Village on the Durotar coast south of Razor Hill. Orcs coming from Orgrimmar can take Speak with Un'thuwa from Uthel'nay in the Valley of Spirits first; it is only a pointer and Un'thuwa gives Ju-Ju Heaps without it. Taking it shuts out the Undercity's Balnir Farmstead.
level 10
accept 1884
section Cain Firesong (Brill)
tip At 10 Cain Firesong, the Brill mage trainer upstairs in the Gallows' End Tavern, sends you to Anastasia Hartwell in the Undercity. Taking it shuts out Ju-Ju Heaps; if Speak with Un'thuwa (from Orgrimmar or Thunder Bluff) is in your log, abandon it first or Cain cannot give you this one. (A Troll who took this one in Brill follows the Balnir steps; an Undead who took Ju-Ju Heaps in Sen'jin, the Echo Isles steps.)
level 10
accept 1881
section The Ju-Ju Heaps
tip Wade across the shallows south-east of Sen'jin to the main Echo Isle, where Zalazane (level 10) holds his camp with Hexed and Voodoo Trolls (level 8). The heaps you can click are the skull piles inside the raised huts around his camp, one hut holding two, more in the huts to the north; the skulls lying on the ground outside cannot be clicked. Destroy four. There are seven and each comes back 30 seconds after it is destroyed.
objective 1884.1 interact when onquest 1884
section Back to Un'thuwa
tip The orb is an off-hand for a one-hand weapon; the staff is a two-hander.
turnin 1884 when onquest 1884
section Anastasia Hartwell
tip Walk south from Brill to the Ruins of Lordaeron and take the lift down into the Undercity. Anastasia stands in the Magic Quarter, the north-east ring of the city.
turnin 1881 when onquest 1881
accept 1882 when onquest 1881
section The Balnir Farmstead
tip The Balnir Farmstead lies south-east of Brill, south of the road east to the Bulwark. The snapdragons grow in the farm's garden and look more like bushes than flowers; any of them will do and you need no Herbalism. They come back within seconds.
objective 1882.1 collect when onquest 1882
section Back to Anastasia
turnin 1882 when onquest 1882]==]
