section Danitha Morr
tip At 18 Danitha Morr, inside Bandarion Keep on the bluffs north-west of the Solliden Farmstead, sends you south to the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.
level 18
accept 91858
section The Sepulcher
tip Trevan Rol stands in the lower part of the Sepulcher, below the surface; Deathguard Baldren keeps watch near the town's entrance.
turnin 91858
accept 91859
turnin 91859
accept 91860
section The pyre on Fenris Isle
tip Fenris Isle lies in the lake north-east of the Sepulcher. The gnolls' pyre, with the Charred Remains, is on its shore: click the remains to hand in, and click them again for the next quest. The body is a tauren's, not the elf's.
turnin 91860
accept 91861
section Fenris Keep
tip Lumina Windsinger is caged in the basement of Fenris Keep, at the north end of the isle. The Rot Hide gnolls (level 18-19) fill the keep: they pull in big groups across floors and players report very fast respawns, so clear a path and keep moving. Any of them can carry the Fenris Isle Key (often the first kill); the rare Rot Hide Bruiser (22) and Snarlmane (23) can too. If her cage is empty, another player is escorting her: wait for her to come back.
turnin 91861
accept 91862
objective 91862.1 collect
section Free Lumina
tip Hand in the key first: starting the escort before that gives the key quest no credit. Then open the cage: Lumina walks out through the keep and its courtyard while the gnolls attack, then runs for the dock and makes her own way back to the Sepulcher. Stay close and keep her alive; if she dies, take the quest again when she is back in her cage.
turnin 91862
accept 96204
section Back to the Sepulcher
tip Lumina waits beside Trevan Rol in the Sepulcher (a different Lumina from the one you escorted). For The Debt, click through every line of her story.
turnin 96204
accept 95034
objective 95034.1 talk
turnin 95034
section A Moon-Kissed Blade
tip At 20 Lumina asks for a blade that can kill Old Fire-Eye. Talk to Trevan Rol beside her for his Weapon Notes, which list the parts, and keep them: he wants them back with the parts. Three parts, in any order: two from dungeons (a group of five each) and a gem from elite naga outside a third.
level 20
accept 95036
section The Enchanted Silver Ingot
tip Shadowfang Keep is the dungeon in south Silverpine, for a group of five in the low to mid 20s. The ingot sits on the table next to Archmage Arugal at the very end. A friend's cleared instance works: walk in and run to the table.
goto 44.8 67.8 Shadowfang Keep map=1421
objective 95036.3 collect @ 44.8 67.8 map=1421
section Whitestone Oak Lumber
tip The Deadmines lies under Moonbrook in Westfall, Alliance land: a group of five at about 17-24. From the Undercity take the zeppelin to Grom'gol in Stranglethorn Vale and go north through Duskwood into Westfall. The way in is the Moonbrook mine. The Goblin Woodcarvers (elite, level 18-19) in Sneed's mast room drop the lumber every time.
goto 42.5 71.7 The Deadmines, in the Moonbrook mine map=1436
objective 95036.2 collect @ 42.5 71.7 map=1436
section Ulric Frostveil
tip Ulric Frostveil waits at Zoram'gar Outpost on Ashenvale's west coast: take the zeppelin from Grom'gol (or the Undercity) to Orgrimmar, then go north through the Barrens into Ashenvale and west along the road. Andruk, the outpost's wind rider master, saves you the walk next time. Take Ulric's quest before you hunt the naga: the Kor Gem only drops while you have it.
accept 95042
section The Corrupted Kor Gem
tip The naga stand in the flooded ruins and passages around the Blackfathom Deeps entrance, just north of Zoram'gar: you do not need to enter the instance (its first naga drop the gem too). Tide Priestesses (level 20-21), Oracles (21-22) and Sea Witches (23-24) drop the Corrupted Kor Gem, one in two. All are elite: grouping up is encouraged. Players solo them one at a time, with difficulty; a group of three makes it easy. They heal themselves, run for help at low health, and the Sea Witches cast Frost Nova up close. Some players report no drop while in a raid group.
objective 95042.1 collect
section The Purified Kor Gem
tip Back to Ulric at Zoram'gar: he cleanses the gem. Keep the Purified Kor Gem for Trevan.
turnin 95042
section Trevan Rol
tip Bring the lumber, the ingot and the gem to Trevan in the Sepulcher. He gives you a Bundle of Blacksmithing Materials for a smith in Tarren Mill: keep it in your bags.
turnin 95036
accept 95111
section Ott
tip Ott, the weaponsmith, stands just south of Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad Foothills. Accepting Ott's Masterwork starts the forging: step back and wait near him until he is done.
turnin 95111
accept 95125
complete 95125
turnin 95125
accept 95126
section The Moonsilver Blade
tip Back to Trevan Rol in the Sepulcher's lower part: he hands you the Moonsilver Blade, a two-handed sword.
turnin 95126
section Two-Handed Swords
tip The blade is a two-handed sword, and you need the skill to hit a level 25 elite with it. Archibald, the weapon master in the Undercity's War Quarter, teaches Two-Handed Swords for a small fee; then swing it on easy mobs until the skill is near its cap (five points per level).
train
section Old Fire-Eye
tip Equip the Moonsilver Blade. Old Fire-Eye, the great worgen, roams the woods south of the Sepulcher toward the gates of Gilneas. He is elite (level 25): the guide waits for level 22 first, and grouping up is encouraged; players have killed him from 22 up, one needed a second, another soloed him at 25. A purple shield guards him until your first swing with the blade lands: a message tells you it broke.
accept 95140
level 22
objective 95140.1 kill @ 47.91 85.33 map=1421
section Wolfsbane
tip Back to Lumina in the Sepulcher with the Moonsilver Blade (the quest asks for it): she takes it and blesses it with the magic of her people into Wolfsbane.
turnin 95140]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/paladin/tome-of-divinity", title = "Redemption (Alliance)", faction = "Alliance", race = "Human, Dwarf", class = "Paladin", levels = "12-14", zone = "Stormwind City", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/paladin/tome-of-divinity"] = [==[guide: Redemption (Alliance)
id: forever/class/paladin/tome-of-divinity
level: 12-14
map: 1453
section The summons (Human)
tip At 12 Brother Wilhelm, the paladin trainer in Goldshire, sends you to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. The errand is optional, a little XP: Brandur Ironhammer in Ironforge gives the same one (taking one closes the other), and Duthorian starts the chain without it.
level 12
accept 2998
section The summons (Dwarf)
tip At 12 Brandur Ironhammer, the paladin trainer in Ironforge's Mystic Ward, sends you upstairs to Tiza Battleforge. The errand is optional, a little XP: Azar Stronghammer in Kharanos and Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind give the same one (taking one closes the others), and Tiza starts the chain without it.
level 12
accept 2999
section Duthorian Rall
turnin 2998 when onquest 2998
section Duthorian Rall
turnin 3681 when onquest 3681
section The Tome of Divinity
tip Duthorian Rall stands inside the Cathedral of Light. He hands you the Tome of Divinity: right-click it in your bags to start the next quest. If the book says the quest is already done, destroy it and ask Duthorian for a new copy. Bring 10 Linen Cloth for the next step if you have it.
turnin 1641
accept 1642
turnin 1642
accept 1643
section Stephanie Turner
tip Stephanie Turner stands at a corner in the middle of the Trade District, outside a general goods store. She wants 10 Linen Cloth: humanoids drop it (Riverpaw gnolls in Westfall about every other kill, Defias and kobolds a little less), or buy it at the Auction House a few steps away in the Trade District.
turnin 1643
accept 1644
objective 1644.1 collect
turnin 1644
accept 1780
section The Symbol of Life
tip Back to the Cathedral. Duthorian gives you the Symbol of Life; Gazin Tenorm lies wounded by the altar of the same hall. Keep the symbol: you need it on Henze Faulk. If you lose it, Duthorian gives you another (The Symbol of Life).
turnin 1780
accept 1781
turnin 1781
accept 1786
section Henze Faulk
tip Henze Faulk lies dead on Heroes' Vigil, the island in Stone Cairn Lake in eastern Elwynn, on top of one of the mounds around the stone circle. Target his body and use the Symbol of Life to raise him, then speak to him. If another paladin just raised him, his body is back within about three minutes. The Defias Rogue Wizards on the island (level 9-10) cast Frostbolt from far off: they stand apart, so pull one at a time.
objective 1786.1 use @ 72.6 51.41 map=1429
turnin 1786
accept 1787
section The Defias Script
tip The Defias Rogue Wizards around the big stone tablet east of Henze carry the Defias Script: about one kill in two drops it, but some players need many kills. They respawn in three minutes.
objective 1787.1 collect @ 74.16 52.0 map=1429
section Redemption
tip Back to the Cathedral of Light: Gazin takes the script, Duthorian teaches you Redemption.
turnin 1787
accept 1788
turnin 1788
section Tiza Battleforge
turnin 2997 when onquest 2997
section Tiza Battleforge
turnin 2999 when onquest 2999
section Tiza Battleforge
turnin 3000 when onquest 3000
section The Tome of Divinity
tip Tiza Battleforge stands upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries, in the Mystic Ward: take the ramp at the back of the hall. She hands you the Tome of Divinity: right-click it in your bags to start the next quest. If the book says the quest is already done, destroy it and ask Tiza for a new copy. Bring 10 Linen Cloth for the next step if you have it.
turnin 1645
accept 1646
turnin 1646
accept 1647
section John Turner
tip John Turner walks the outer ring of the Commons, past the front gate, the bank and the Auction House. He wants 10 Linen Cloth: humanoids drop it (Kogan Forgestone in Kharanos every time, Dark Iron Ambushers about two kills in five), or buy it at the Auction House on his ring.
turnin 1647
accept 1648
objective 1648.1 collect
turnin 1648
accept 1778
section The Symbol of Life
tip Back upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries. Tiza gives you the Symbol of Life; her husband Muiredon Battleforge rests on the same floor. Keep the symbol: you need it on Narm Faulk. If you lose it, Tiza gives you another (The Symbol of Life).
turnin 1778
accept 1779
turnin 1779
accept 1783
section Narm Faulk
tip Narm Faulk lies dead in Dun Morogh, not Loch Modan: east past Kharanos, north-east of Ironband's compound, on the smallest of three little hills between Helm's Bed Lake and the Dark Iron camp. Target his body and use the Symbol of Life to raise him, then speak to him. If another paladin just raised him, his body is back within about three minutes.
objective 1783.1 use @ 78.32 58.09 map=1426
turnin 1783
accept 1784
section The Dark Iron Script
tip The Dark Iron Spies (level 9-11, twelve of them) sneak around the little house below the lake, just south of Narm; you see them from his hill. About one kill in two drops the Dark Iron Script. They run for help at low health: finish them or step back. They respawn in three minutes.
objective 1784.1 collect @ 77.53 61.18 map=1426
section Redemption
tip Back up to the Hall of Mysteries: Muiredon takes the script, Tiza teaches you Redemption.
turnin 1784
accept 1785
turnin 1785]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/paladin/tyrs-watch", title = "Tyr's Watch and Redemption (Forsaken)", faction = "Horde", race = "Undead", class = "Paladin", levels = "1-13", zone = "Tirisfal Glades", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/paladin/tyrs-watch"] = [==[guide: Tyr's Watch and Redemption (Forsaken)
id: forever/class/paladin/tyrs-watch
level: 1-13
map: 1420
section Aramis Hammerhand
tip Shadow Priest Sarvis gives you a Consecrated Scroll after The Mindless Ones: read it, then bring it to Aramis Hammerhand by the church. He asks you to heal five Injured Deathguard lying around Deathknell. Holy Light hurts a Forsaken paladin a little each time: watch your health.
accept 98601 when level<9
turnin 98601 when level<9
level 2 when level<9
accept 90902 when level<9
complete 90902 @ 31.6 65.8 map=1420 when level<9
turnin 90902 when level<9
section Coming to Terms
tip At 4 Aramis sends you after a Frightened Paladin who fled into the hills west of the church, just south of the bat cave. Talk to her to offer aid: she turns on you, and you have to put her down (level 3, easy).
level 4 when level<9
accept 91208 when level<9
accept 91209 when level<9
objective 91208.1 kill when level<9
turnin 91208 when level<9
section Shari Stilwell
tip Follow the road east out of Deathknell to Brill. Shari Stilwell, the paladin trainer, stands in town; she trains you from here on.
turnin 91209 when level<9
train when level<9
section A Second Home
tip At 8 Shari Stilwell in Brill sends you to the order's keep on the west coast. The Tarnished in Shadowvale and the crypt under it hit hard at 8-9: come at 10 or later.
level 8
accept 91282
section Bandarion Keep
tip {area:16602} stands on the bluffs north-west of the Solliden Farmstead (the road west starts near 29,46). Breton Samuels waits at the gate. Hilda the Breaker, the keep's trainer, and Ephram Barbaro, its stable master, stand at the forest's edge just south of him. They only have work for you from level 10 and after A Righteous Cause from Leonid at the keep, the end of Hadric Harlson's chain that starts south-east of Brill; take their quests when you see them.
turnin 91282
accept 91285
accept 99152
accept 99153
section Murlocs at the Gates
tip The Vile Fin murlocs (level 9-11) lurk on the bluffs along the road east of the keep and in the camps around the lake to the south-west, on the way down to Shadowvale.
objective 91285.1 kill
objective 91285.2 kill
section Touring the Grounds
tip Breton gives you a weapon, then sends you round the keep to speak with four of its people: Hilda the Breaker just south of the gate, Ander Solliden, the lookout, who walks the road south-east of the keep, then Jorin Croge and Danitha Morr inside the keep. Pick the conversation option with each.
turnin 91285
accept 91294
objective 91294.1 talk
objective 91294.3 talk
objective 91294.2 talk
objective 91294.4 talk
section Danitha Morr
tip Danitha Morr leads the order from inside the keep; Jorin Croge stands beside it. The Tarnished need level 9.
turnin 91294
level 9
accept 91317
accept 91316
section Shadowvale
tip The Tarnished (level 8-9) hold the ruined village of Shadowvale in the Whispering Forest, south-west of the keep. Commander Rudolph Gelhardt (level 10) stands on the upper floor of a house, with Drudges below him: clear the ground floor first.
objective 91317.2 kill
objective 91317.3 kill
objective 91317.1 collect
section The crypt under Shadowvale
tip The cellar is under the village, not on the surface: the way down is inside a burned-out house, where the arrow points. Twelve Lumber Piles (stacked beams) lie in the cellar, each good for one Sturdy Lumber. Whispering Horror, an elite (level 11-13), sits at the far end: leave it alone.
objective 91316.1 collect @ 12.9 65.7 map=1420
section Hilda's bones
tip The Shadowvale Lurchers and Mystics (level 8-10) in the crypt drop the Faintly Glowing Bones: about one in two from Lurchers, more from one kind of Mystic, less from the other.
objective 99152.1 collect @ 9.89 66.36 map=1420 when onquest 99152
section Ephram's crystal
tip The Glowing Crystal Fragment, a green crystal, lies on the floor in the left-hand part of the crypt.
objective 99153.1 collect @ 9.8 69.3 map=1420 when onquest 99153
section Back to the keep
tip Danitha hands you Rudolph Gelhardt's head for Sylvanas: keep it in your bags, it is what you hand in.
turnin 91316
turnin 91317
accept 95803
section Hilda the Breaker
tip Hilda and Ephram wait at the forest's edge south of the gate.
turnin 99152 when onquest 99152
section Ephram Barbaro
tip Ephram waits at the forest's edge south of the gate, a few steps west of Hilda.
turnin 99153 when onquest 99153
section A Lesson in Divinity
tip Danitha offers the first Lesson in Divinity at level 12. Bring 10 Linen Cloth if you have it: the Undercity asks for it next.
level 12
accept 94427
section The Undercity
tip Walk south from Brill to the Ruins of Lordaeron and down into the Undercity. Lady Sylvanas Windrunner holds court in the Royal Quarter; Tanis Alderwood begs in the Trade Quarter.
turnin 95803
turnin 94427
accept 94434
section Linen Cloth
tip Tanis needs 10 Linen Cloth. Humanoids drop it: the Scarlet Zealots and Friars of the glades about three kills in ten. The Undercity Auction House sells it too.
objective 94434.1 collect
section Tanis Alderwood
turnin 94434
accept 94435
section The Symbol of Life
tip Back to {area:16602}. Danitha gives you the Symbol of Life; Deathguard Billmuth waits downstairs in the keep. If you lose the symbol, Danitha gives you another.
turnin 94435
accept 94436
turnin 94436
accept 94438
section Deathguard Falgan
tip Venomweb Vale is at the far east end of the glades, a long walk. Falgan lies dead among the Scarlet Crusaders there: target his body and use the Symbol of Life, then talk to him at once, as he does not stay alive long. If he is already up (another player), just talk to him; if he died again, raise him again.
turnin 94438
accept 94440
section The Scarlet attack plans
tip The Scarlet Zealots (level 8-9), Friars (9-10) and Tarnished around Venomweb Vale carry the attack plans. They run for help at low health and respawn in five minutes.
objective 94440.1 collect
section Redemption
tip Back to {area:16602}, across the whole glades: Billmuth downstairs takes the plans, then Danitha, back upstairs in the keep, teaches you Redemption.
turnin 94440
accept 94441
turnin 94441]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/paladin/verigans-fist", title = "Verigan's Fist", faction = "Alliance", race = "Human, Dwarf", class = "Paladin", levels = "20-30", zone = "Stormwind City", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/paladin/verigans-fist"] = [==[guide: Verigan's Fist
id: forever/class/paladin/verigans-fist
level: 20-30
map: 1453
section The Tome of Valor (Ironforge)
tip At 20 Tiza Battleforge, upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries in the Mystic Ward, gives you the Tome of Valor. Right-click it: it sends you to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. Take the Deeprun Tram from Ironforge to Stormwind.
level 20
turnin 1794
section The Tome of Valor
tip Duthorian Rall stands in the Cathedral of Light. Humans get the Tome of Valor from him. Right-click the book to start its quest and hand it straight back to him.
level 20
turnin 1793 only Human
accept 1649
turnin 1649
accept 1650
section Daphne Stilwell
tip Daphne Stilwell's farmhouse stands on the south-west coast of Westfall, south of Moonbrook: take the path that runs south beside the Deadmines' back exit. When you take her quest, she walks from her orchard to the house and three waves of Defias Raiders (level 17-18) attack: three, then four, then five. Fight close to her so they do not swarm her, and heal her when she drops. You get time to eat and drink between waves, and she heals to full. If you or Daphne die, the quest fails: abandon it and take it again from her (she is back five minutes after dying). Players find it hard alone before about 24.
turnin 1650
accept 1651
complete 1651
turnin 1651
accept 1652
section Duthorian Rall
tip Back to the Cathedral of Light: Duthorian gives you the Bastion of Stormwind shield and teaches you Sense Undead.
turnin 1652
accept 1653
section Jordan Stilwell
tip Jordan Stilwell works outside the gates of Ironforge, not inside. He gives you Jordan's Weapon Notes: four parts, in any order. Keep the notes.
turnin 1653
accept 1654
section Bailor Stonehand
tip Bailor Stonehand is downstairs in the house of Thelsamar that has a tailoring merchant outside. His quest only opens once you hold Jordan's.
accept 1655
section Bailor's Ore
tip The crate of ore sits outdoors in the middle of the Mo'grosh ogre camp in north-east Loch Modan, beside a big tree and a broken wagon, between the caves. The camp holds about fifteen Mo'grosh ogres, elite (level 18-19), who knock you down and come back after five minutes: grouping up is encouraged; at 20-22 it needs a group of about three. The crate is back two seconds after each loot, so every paladin in the group gets one.
objective 1655.1 collect
section Back to Bailor
tip Bailor turns the ore into Jordan's Refined Ore Shipment, the part Jordan wants.
turnin 1655
objective 1654.2 collect
section Whitestone Oak Lumber
tip The Deadmines is a group of five under Moonbrook; the instance portal is at the bottom of the Moonbrook mine. The Goblin Woodcarvers (elite, level 18-19) in the mast room with Sneed drop the lumber every time.
goto 42.5 71.7 The Deadmines, in the Moonbrook mine map=1436
objective 1654.1 collect @ 42.5 71.7 map=1436
section Jordan's Smithing Hammer
tip Shadowfang Keep is a dungeon for a group of five in the low to mid 20s, in southern Silverpine Forest, Horde land: a long trip for the Alliance, through the Wetlands, Arathi and Hillsbrad. The hammer lies on a crate across from the horses in the stables, early in the dungeon, at the far end of the courtyard before the ramp up; it is back five minutes after someone takes it.
goto 44.8 67.8 Shadowfang Keep map=1421
objective 1654.3 collect @ 44.8 67.8 map=1421
section Thundris Windweaver
tip Thundris Windweaver is in Auberdine. Take his quest before you hunt naga: the Kor Gem never drops without it.
accept 1442
section The Corrupted Kor Gem
tip The Blackfathom naga in the flooded passages around the Blackfathom Deeps entrance, on Ashenvale's north-west coast, drop the Corrupted Kor Gem: Tide Priestesses (level 20-21), Oracles (21-22) and Sea Witches (23-24), one in two. You do not need to enter the instance. All are elite: grouping up is encouraged; players solo them one at a time, with difficulty. They heal themselves, run for help at low health, satyrs stand near some, and the Sea Witches cast Frost Nova up close. Some players report no drop while in a raid group.
objective 1442.1 collect
section The Purified Kor Gem
tip Back to Thundris in Auberdine: he purifies the gem.
turnin 1442
objective 1654.4 collect
section Verigan's Fist
tip Bring the four parts to Jordan Stilwell outside Ironforge. Accept his last quest and wait by him while he forges the mace at his anvil.
turnin 1654
accept 1806
turnin 1806]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/priest/benediction", title = "Benediction and Anathema", class = "Priest", levels = "60-60", zone = "Eastern Plaguelands", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/priest/benediction"] = [==[guide: Benediction and Anathema
id: forever/class/priest/benediction
level: 60-60
map: 1423
section The Eye of Divinity
tip The Eye of Divinity comes from the Cache of the Firelord, the chest that appears when Majordomo Executus yields in Molten Core, a 40-player raid (it is in the cache about half the time). Molten Core's portal is at the bottom of Blackrock Depths; once you have done Attunement to the Core (a Core Fragment from beside that portal), Lothos Riftwaker inside Blackrock Mountain ports you straight in. Nothing in this chain starts without the Eye: Eris is invisible until you equip it.
section Eris Havenfire
tip Equip The Eye of Divinity, then find Eris Havenfire, a ghost on the hillside in the north-west of the Eastern Plaguelands, west of Stratholme's gate (if she does not show, take the Eye off and put it back on). A Warning is only talk; The Balance of Light and Shadow starts the moment you accept it, so prepare first: full mana, Major Mana Potions, Demonic or Dark Runes, mana food or Nightfin Soup, and a stack of Oil of Immolation or Stratholme Holy Water for the skeletons.
level 60
accept 7621
turnin 7621
accept 7622
section The Balance of Light and Shadow
tip Save 50 peasants before 15 die (the Death Post by the path counts the dead). They walk from the cave towards Eris in waves, catch diseases and draw skeletons and skeleton archers. Cure the purple-glowing diseases first (Abolish Disease), keep Renew on the hurt ones, Flash Heal the nearly dead, and kill skeletons as they spawn: one Holy Nova of rank 3 or more kills them, oil takes two ticks while they hit you. Shield yourself at the start of each wave; friendly nameplates make the hurt peasants easy to pick out. Friends may buff you before you accept and may heal or cure peasants, but they must not heal or buff you, attack a skeleton or bring a pet once it starts, or a demon appears and kills everyone. Fail, and Eris is gone for a while (players report anything from 15 minutes to two hours); talk to her again when she is back.
complete 7622
section Benediction
turnin 7622
section The Eye of Shadow
tip The splinter needs The Eye of Shadow as well. Lord Kazzak, a world boss in the Blasted Lands (a raid), always drops it; Manahounds and Doomguard Commanders there drop it rarely (about 3% and 2%), the Hederine of Winterspring hardly ever. It can be traded: check the Auction House first.
section Benediction
tip With the Splinter of Nordrassil, The Eye of Divinity and The Eye of Shadow in your bags, use the splinter wherever you are: it becomes Benediction. Use Benediction to turn it into Anathema, the shadow staff, and back (a 30-minute cooldown).]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/priest/blood-of-morphaz", title = "Blood of Morphaz", class = "Priest", levels = "50-52", zone = "Azshara", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/priest/blood-of-morphaz"] = [==[guide: Blood of Morphaz
id: forever/class/priest/blood-of-morphaz
level: 50-52
map: 1447
section Cenarion Aid: High Priest Rohan
tip At 50 in Ironforge, High Priest Rohan in the Hall of Mysteries (Mystic Ward) offers Cenarion Aid. Before you leave a city, buy an Ichor of Undeath at the Auction House (a few silver): the third quest asks for one and it drops rarely.
level 50 when !onquest 8254
accept 8254 when !onquest 8254
section Cenarion Aid: Brother Joshua
tip At 50, Brother Joshua at the altar of Stormwind's Cathedral of Light offers Cenarion Aid (High Priest Rohan in Ironforge has it too). Before you leave, buy an Ichor of Undeath at the Auction House in the Trade District (a few silver): the third quest asks for one and it drops rarely.
level 50 when !onquest 8254
accept 8254 when !onquest 8254
section Cenarion Aid: Ur'kyo
tip At 50, Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits offers Cenarion Aid. Before you leave, buy an Ichor of Undeath at the Auction House (a few silver): the third quest asks for one and it drops rarely.
level 50
accept 8254
section Ogtinc
tip Ogtinc, a furbolg, lives on the clifftop north-east of the Ruins of Eldarath. Alliance: fly to Talrendis Point; Horde: fly to Valormok. Ride east and leave the road at the fork before the ruins, then follow the northern cliff edge east to him: the naga ruins and the beach below are walled in by cliffs with no way up.
getfp Talrendis Point only Alliance
getfp Valormok only Horde
turnin 8254
accept 8255
section Of Coursers We Know
tip Mosshoof Coursers (level 52-53, not elite) graze all over Azshara, thickest north-east of Ogtinc and south of the mountains; about one in three drops a Healthy Courser Gland, so plan on a dozen kills for four. They enrage at 30% health: finish them fast. Killing them costs no Cenarion Circle reputation. Keep any Ichor of Undeath you loot.
objective 8255.1 collect
section Ogtinc
turnin 8255
accept 8256
section The Ichor of Undeath
tip Carrying an Ichor of Undeath already? It counts at once. Otherwise any undead may drop one, rarely: the Lingering Highborne (level 48) in the Ruins of Eldarath below Ogtinc's cliff drop it about one kill in ten, the highborne ghosts on Azshara's border with Ashenvale (level 45-46) a little less, the Anguished and Suffering Highborne in Winterspring (54-55) about one in eight. The Auction House is usually quicker.
objective 8256.1 collect
section Ogtinc
turnin 8256
accept 8257
section Morphaz in the Sunken Temple
tip Morphaz is a level 52 elite green dragon inside the Sunken Temple, a five-player dungeon: bring a group of five (a level 60 group clears it with ease). Horde: fly to Stonard; Alliance: fly to Nethergarde Keep in the Blasted Lands and ride north. The temple stands in the middle of the Pool of Tears: climb the steps on its south side, swim down through the flooded hall and take the stairs to the portal. Inside, Morphaz only appears late: kill the six troll minibosses on the upper balconies, then Jammal'an the Prophet below them; that wakes the drakes Weaver and Dreamscythe in the Pit of Sacrifice, and killing both brings Morphaz and Hazzas. The pair patrols together and cannot be split: pull them into a hallway and have the tank face them away from the group (breath and a knockback). Loot him in a party, not a raid group: the blood always drops.
objective 8257.1 collect @ 69.0 54.0 map=1435
section Greta Mosshoof
tip Greta Mosshoof is at the Emerald Sanctuary in southern Felwood. Horde: fly to Bloodvenom Post and ride south-east; Alliance: fly to Astranaar in Ashenvale and ride north into Felwood. She takes the blood for experience and gold. Look at the reward window before you hand in: Classic let you pick Blessed Prayer Beads, Circle of Hope or Woestave, and Forever's notes say that choice may be gone.
turnin 8257]==]
