HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/priest/priest-robes-horde"] = [==[guide: Priest Robes at 5 (Horde)
id: forever/class/priest/priest-robes-horde
level: 5-6
map: 1411
section In Favor of Spirituality
tip At 5, Ken'jai, the priest trainer in the Den in the middle of the Valley of Trials, sends you to Tai'jin in Razor Hill. Train Lesser Heal (Rank 2) from him while you are here: it opens at level 4 for 1 silver, and the next quest needs exactly that rank.
level 5
accept 5649
section Tai'jin
tip Follow the road out of the Valley of Trials north-east to Razor Hill. Tai'jin is inside the barracks, the first building on the right as you come into town.
turnin 5649
accept 5648
train
section Grunt Kor'ja
tip Grunt Kor'ja kneels behind a group of rocks just off the road, a short walk south of Razor Hill. Cast Lesser Heal (Rank 2) on her first, then Power Word: Fortitude. Rank 1 of Lesser Heal does not count; drag Rank 2 onto your bar from the spellbook. She leaves once both land and is back in about 5 minutes.
objective 5648.1 kill
section Tai'jin
tip Back in the Razor Hill barracks: Tai'jin gives you the Juju Hex Robes.
turnin 5648
section In Favor of Darkness
tip At 5, Dark Cleric Duesten, the priest trainer in the chapel of Deathknell, sends you to Dark Cleric Beryl in Brill. Train Lesser Heal (Rank 2) from him while you are here: it opens at level 4 for 1 silver, and the next quest needs exactly that rank.
level 5
accept 5651
section Dark Cleric Beryl
tip Follow the road east out of Deathknell to Brill. Dark Cleric Beryl is upstairs in the inn, Gallows' End Tavern.
turnin 5651
accept 5650
train
section Deathguard Kel
tip Deathguard Kel kneels, half-dead, beside the north gate of Brill's graveyard, a short walk north of the inn. Cast Lesser Heal (Rank 2) on him first, then Power Word: Fortitude: Fortitude first does not count, nor does Rank 1 of Lesser Heal. If an addon gets in the way, cast both from the spellbook.
objective 5650.1 kill
section Dark Cleric Beryl
tip Back upstairs in the Brill inn: Beryl gives you the Acolyte's Sacrificial Robes.
turnin 5650]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/priest/starshards-and-elunes-grace", title = "Starshards and Elune's Grace", faction = "Alliance", race = "NightElf", class = "Priest", levels = "10-20", zone = "Darnassus", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/priest/starshards-and-elunes-grace"] = [==[guide: Starshards and Elune's Grace
id: forever/class/priest/starshards-and-elunes-grace
level: 10-20
map: 1457
section Starshards: Laurna Morninglight
tip At 10, Laurna Morninglight, the priest trainer in the building at the north edge of Dolanaar, hands you Returning Home, a letter for Priestess Alathea in Darnassus. Dolanaar is on the road west to Darnassus.
level 10 when !onquest 5627,5628,5629,5630,5631,5632,5633
section Starshards: Priestess Josetta
tip At 10 in Elwynn Forest, Priestess Josetta, upstairs in the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, hands you Returning Home, a letter for Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.
level 10 when !onquest 5627,5628,5629,5630,5631,5632,5633
section Starshards: Maxan Anvol
tip At 10 in Dun Morogh, Maxan Anvol, the priest trainer inside the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos, hands you Returning Home, a letter for Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.
level 10 when !onquest 5627,5628,5629,5630,5631,5632,5633
section Starshards: Brother Joshua
tip At 10 in Stormwind, Brother Joshua at the altar of the Cathedral of Light hands you Returning Home, a letter for Priestess Alathea in Darnassus. Nara Meideros in the Park has the same letter.
level 10 when !onquest 5627,5628,5629,5630,5631,5632,5633
section Starshards: Braenna Flintcrag
tip At 10 in Ironforge, Braenna Flintcrag in the Hall of Mysteries (Mystic Ward) hands you Returning Home, a letter for Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.
level 10 when !onquest 5627,5628,5629,5630,5631,5632,5633
section Starshards: Priestess Alathea
tip At 10, go to Priestess Alathea on the upper balcony of the Temple of the Moon, at the south end of Darnassus: take the ramp up from the temple floor; she stands beside Tyrande Whisperwind. Stars of Elune is given and taken back at once and teaches Starshards. No letter needed. Forever made Starshards hit much harder, on a 30-second cooldown.
level 10 when !onquest 5627,5628,5629,5630,5631,5632,5633
accept 5627 when !onquest 5627,5628,5629,5630,5631,5632,5633
turnin 5627 when !onquest 5627,5628,5629,5630,5631,5632,5633
section Starshards: Laurna's letter
tip Take the road west from Dolanaar into Darnassus and go up to the upper balcony of the Temple of the Moon, beside Tyrande Whisperwind: Priestess Alathea takes Returning Home and teaches Starshards.
turnin 5629 when onquest 5629
section Starshards: Josetta's letter
tip Returning Home goes to Priestess Alathea, on the upper balcony of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, beside Tyrande Whisperwind: take the boat from Stormwind Harbor (or Menethil Harbor) to Auberdine, the boat on to Rut'theran Village, then the portal up into Darnassus.
turnin 5628 when onquest 5628
section Starshards: Maxan's letter
tip Returning Home goes to Priestess Alathea, on the upper balcony of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, beside Tyrande Whisperwind: take the boat from Stormwind Harbor (or Menethil Harbor) to Auberdine, the boat on to Rut'theran Village, then the portal up into Darnassus.
turnin 5630 when onquest 5630
section Starshards: Joshua's letter
tip Returning Home goes to Priestess Alathea, on the upper balcony of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, beside Tyrande Whisperwind: take the boat from Stormwind Harbor (or Menethil Harbor) to Auberdine, the boat on to Rut'theran Village, then the portal up into Darnassus.
turnin 5631 when onquest 5631
section Starshards: Nara's letter
tip Returning Home goes to Priestess Alathea, on the upper balcony of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, beside Tyrande Whisperwind: take the boat from Stormwind Harbor (or Menethil Harbor) to Auberdine, the boat on to Rut'theran Village, then the portal up into Darnassus.
turnin 5632 when onquest 5632
section Starshards: Braenna's letter
tip Returning Home goes to Priestess Alathea, on the upper balcony of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, beside Tyrande Whisperwind: take the boat from Stormwind Harbor (or Menethil Harbor) to Auberdine, the boat on to Rut'theran Village, then the portal up into Darnassus.
turnin 5633 when onquest 5633
section Elune's Grace: High Priestess Laurena
tip At 20 in Stormwind, High Priestess Laurena at the altar of the Cathedral of Light hands you an Elune's Grace letter for Priestess Alathea in Darnassus. Nara Meideros in the Park has the same letter.
level 20 when !onquest 5672,5673,5674,5675
section Elune's Grace: High Priest Rohan
tip At 20 in Ironforge, High Priest Rohan in the Hall of Mysteries (Mystic Ward) hands you an Elune's Grace letter for Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.
level 20 when !onquest 5672,5673,5674,5675
section Elune's Grace: Priestess Alathea
tip At 20, Priestess Alathea on the upper balcony of the Temple of the Moon, beside Tyrande Whisperwind, teaches Elune's Grace with a quest she gives and takes back at once. In Forever, Elune's Grace halves the chance for melee and ranged attacks to hit you for 15 seconds or until three attacks miss.
level 20 when !onquest 5672,5673,5674,5675
accept 5672 when !onquest 5672,5673,5674,5675
turnin 5672 when !onquest 5672,5673,5674,5675
section Elune's Grace: Laurena's letter
tip Hand Laurena's letter to Priestess Alathea, on the upper balcony of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, beside Tyrande Whisperwind: the boat from Stormwind Harbor (or Menethil Harbor) to Auberdine, the boat on to Rut'theran Village, then the portal up into Darnassus.
turnin 5673 when onquest 5673
section Elune's Grace: Nara's letter
tip Hand Nara's letter to Priestess Alathea, on the upper balcony of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, beside Tyrande Whisperwind: the boat from Stormwind Harbor (or Menethil Harbor) to Auberdine, the boat on to Rut'theran Village, then the portal up into Darnassus.
turnin 5674 when onquest 5674
section Elune's Grace: Rohan's letter
tip Hand Rohan's letter to Priestess Alathea, on the upper balcony of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, beside Tyrande Whisperwind: the boat from Stormwind Harbor (or Menethil Harbor) to Auberdine, the boat on to Rut'theran Village, then the portal up into Darnassus.
turnin 5675 when onquest 5675]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/priest/touch-of-weakness-and-dark-sacrifice", title = "Touch of Weakness and Dark Sacrifice", faction = "Horde", race = "Undead", class = "Priest", levels = "10-20", zone = "Undercity", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/priest/touch-of-weakness-and-dark-sacrifice"] = [==[guide: Touch of Weakness and Dark Sacrifice
id: forever/class/priest/touch-of-weakness-and-dark-sacrifice
level: 10-20
map: 1458
section Touch of Weakness: Tai'jin
tip At 10 in Durotar, Tai'jin, the priest trainer inside the barracks of Razor Hill, hands you a Touch of Weakness letter for Aelthalyste in the Undercity.
level 10 when !onquest 5658,5660,5661,5662,5663
section Touch of Weakness: Ur'kyo
tip At 10 in Orgrimmar, Ur'kyo in the Valley of Spirits hands you a Touch of Weakness letter for Aelthalyste in the Undercity. The zeppelin to Tirisfal Glades leaves from the tower outside Orgrimmar's front gate.
level 10 when !onquest 5658,5660,5661,5662,5663
section Touch of Weakness: Var'jun
tip At 10 in Mulgore, Var'jun, just south-west of Bloodhoof Village, hands you a Touch of Weakness letter for Aelthalyste in the Undercity.
level 10 when !onquest 5658,5660,5661,5662,5663
section Touch of Weakness: Miles Welsh
tip At 10 in Thunder Bluff, Miles Welsh, the priest trainer in the cave under Spirit Rise, hands you a Touch of Weakness letter for Aelthalyste in the Undercity.
level 10 when !onquest 5658,5660,5661,5662,5663
section Touch of Weakness: Aelthalyste
tip At 10, go to Aelthalyste, the priest trainer in the Undercity's War Quarter: she gives Touch of Weakness and takes it back at once. No letter needed. From Brill, follow the road south to the ruined city of Lordaeron; the Undercity's lifts are at the back of the throne room. Touch of Weakness strikes the next melee attacker for Shadow damage and lowers its melee attack power for 2 minutes.
level 10 when !onquest 5658,5660,5661,5662,5663
accept 5658 when !onquest 5658,5660,5661,5662,5663
turnin 5658 when !onquest 5658,5660,5661,5662,5663
section Touch of Weakness: Tai'jin's letter
tip Hand the letter to Aelthalyste in the Undercity's War Quarter: the zeppelin from the tower outside Orgrimmar lands in Tirisfal Glades, a short walk from the Undercity.
turnin 5660 when onquest 5660
section Touch of Weakness: Var'jun's letter
tip Hand the letter to Aelthalyste in the Undercity's War Quarter: travel to Orgrimmar and take the zeppelin to Tirisfal Glades.
turnin 5661 when onquest 5661
section Touch of Weakness: Ur'kyo's letter
tip Hand the letter to Aelthalyste in the Undercity's War Quarter: the zeppelin from the tower outside Orgrimmar lands in Tirisfal Glades.
turnin 5662 when onquest 5662
section Touch of Weakness: Miles Welsh's letter
tip Hand the letter to Aelthalyste in the Undercity's War Quarter: travel to Orgrimmar and take the zeppelin to Tirisfal Glades.
turnin 5663 when onquest 5663
section Dark Sacrifice: Ur'kyo
tip At 20 in Orgrimmar, Ur'kyo in the Valley of Spirits hands you a Dark Sacrifice letter for Aelthalyste in the Undercity.
level 20 when !onquest 5679,5644,5646
section Dark Sacrifice: Miles Welsh
tip At 20 in Thunder Bluff, Miles Welsh in the cave under Spirit Rise hands you a Dark Sacrifice letter for Aelthalyste in the Undercity.
level 20 when !onquest 5679,5644,5646
section Dark Sacrifice: Aelthalyste
tip At 20, Aelthalyste in the War Quarter teaches Dark Sacrifice with a quest she gives and takes back at once (its text still speaks of Devouring Plague, which every priest now learns from the trainer).
level 20 when !onquest 5679,5644,5646
accept 5679 when !onquest 5679,5644,5646
turnin 5679 when !onquest 5679,5644,5646
section Dark Sacrifice: Ur'kyo's letter
tip Hand the letter to Aelthalyste in the Undercity's War Quarter: the zeppelin from the tower outside Orgrimmar lands in Tirisfal Glades.
turnin 5646 when onquest 5646
section Dark Sacrifice: Miles Welsh's letter
tip Hand the letter to Aelthalyste in the Undercity's War Quarter: travel to Orgrimmar and take the zeppelin to Tirisfal Glades.
turnin 5644 when onquest 5644]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/rogue/blade-of-cunning-alliance", title = "Blade of Cunning (Alliance)", faction = "Alliance", class = "Rogue", levels = "10-12", zone = "Elwynn Forest", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/rogue/blade-of-cunning-alliance"] = [==[guide: Blade of Cunning (Alliance)
id: forever/class/rogue/blade-of-cunning-alliance
level: 10-12
map: 1429
section Seek out SI: 7
tip At 10 Keryn Sylvius, the rogue trainer upstairs in the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, gives you a package for Master Mathias Shaw in Stormwind. Train Pick Pocket if you lack it: this chain needs it.
level 10
accept 2205
section Master Mathias Shaw
tip Head north to Stormwind. Shaw stands upstairs in the SI:7 building in Old Town (the quest says the Barracks; it means SI:7).
turnin 2205
accept 2206
section Defias Dockmaster
tip The Defias Dockmaster (level 10, a goblin) works in the dock house at Jerod's Landing, on the river at Elwynn's southern edge, south of Goldshire. Stealth in and Pick Pocket him from behind: the schedule never drops from his corpse. Do not open with Sap or a fight: he calls in three waves of bodyguards. Keep away from the fireplaces in the house; they burn you out of stealth. He is back 2 to 5 minutes after a death.
objective 2206.1 collect
section Back to Mathias Shaw
turnin 2206
section Road to Salvation
tip At 10 Hogral Bakkan, the rogue trainer in the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos, sends you to Hulfdan Blackbeard in Ironforge.
level 10
accept 2218
section Hulfdan Blackbeard
tip Hulfdan Blackbeard is in the Forlorn Cavern, the rogue quarter in the north of Ironforge: go into the building with a shady dealer outside and down the stairs.
turnin 2218
accept 2238
section Onin MacHammar
tip Head west to Gnomeregan. Beside the road to its entrance stands a wooden spiral tower: Onin waits stealthed on the top platform, next to a level 10 Leper Gnome, so you only see him up close.
turnin 2238
accept 2239
section Back to Hulfdan
turnin 2239
section The Apple Falls
tip At 10 Jannok Breezesong, the rogue trainer in the Dolanaar inn, gives you a rose for Syurna in Darnassus. If you lose the rose, abandon the quest and take it again.
level 10
accept 2241
section Syurna
tip Head west to Darnassus. Syurna is below ground in the Cenarion Enclave: the way down is the opening at the foot of the split tree left of the Arch Druid's tree, near the nightsaber trainer. Her map marker shows above ground.
turnin 2241
accept 2242
section Sethir the Ancient
tip Sethir the Ancient (level 12 satyr) lives out on a great branch north of the Oracle Glade: go through the V-shaped gap in the wall north of the glade and out along the branch. Pick his pocket for the journal; killing him does not give it, and a fight brings out three Minions of Sethir. He walks between the main branch and a side branch: wait stealthed at the far end of the main branch and pick him from behind when he comes back. Then Sprint away. He is back 8 1/2 minutes after a death.
objective 2242.1 collect
section Back to Syurna
turnin 2242]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/rogue/blade-of-cunning-horde", title = "Blade of Cunning (Horde)", faction = "Horde", class = "Rogue", levels = "10-13", zone = "Durotar", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/rogue/blade-of-cunning-horde"] = [==[guide: Blade of Cunning (Horde)
id: forever/class/rogue/blade-of-cunning-horde
level: 10-13
map: 1411
section Therzok
tip At 10 Kaplak, the rogue trainer in Razor Hill, sends you to Therzok in Orgrimmar. It is only a pointer: an Orc already in Orgrimmar can skip it and take The Shattered Hand from Therzok straight away.
level 10
accept 1859
section The Shattered Hand
tip Therzok stands in the Cleft of Shadow, the canyon under the Valley of Strength. Trolls: take The Shattered Hand from him at 10.
level 10
turnin 1859 only Orc
accept 1963
section Tazan
tip Tazan (level 13, not elite) is a troll pirate on the Merchant Coast south of Ratchet: he walks the fenced hill path between the lower pirate camp by the beached ship and the upper camp by a big tree. Fight him at the foot of the hill, away from the camps. He always drops his satchel and is back 4 1/2 minutes after a death; one satchel per kill, so two rogues need two kills. Hand the satchel in unopened: picking its lock now destroys it and you must kill him again.
objective 1963.1 collect
section Back to Therzok
turnin 1963
accept 1858
section Tazan's Key
tip Therzok hands the satchel back: now open it. Gamon (level 12) kneels by the innkeeper in the inn in the Valley of Strength; stealth up and pick his pocket for Tazan's Key (do not kill him: the key almost never drops). Players often kill him, so you may wait up to 5 minutes for him. Then use the key on Tazan's Satchel in your bags. If you have trained Pick Lock, you can pick the satchel's lock instead.
objective 1858.1 use @ 54.0 68.0 map=1454
objective 1858.1 collect @ 54.0 68.0 map=1454
section Therzok's reward
turnin 1858
section Mennet Carkad
tip At 10 Marion Call, the rogue trainer upstairs in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, sends you to Mennet Carkad in the Undercity.
level 10
accept 1885
section The Rogues' Quarter
tip Mennet Carkad stands in the Rogues' Quarter.
turnin 1885
accept 1886
section Astor Hadren
tip Astor Hadren (level 13) walks the road between the Sepulcher and the Undercity, north of the Sepulcher. He looks like a friendly traveller with no quest mark. Talk to him and pick both of his answers: he turns hostile. Kill him for the letter (it always drops). Fight him away from guards, who can take the kill and leave no loot; only one rogue per kill gets the letter. He is back 5 minutes after a death.
objective 1886.1 collect
section Back to Mennet Carkad
turnin 1886
accept 1898
section Andron Gant
tip Andron Gant is in the Apothecarium, in its biggest room, where two huge guards watch a small bridge. His ledger is on the bookshelf in the back room behind him, not the shelf on the wall next to him.
turnin 1898
accept 1899
objective 1899.1 collect
section Mennet and Varimathras
tip Mennet sends the ledger on to Varimathras, the big demon in the middle of the Hall of the Dark Lady in the Royal Quarter, past its elite guards; the way in is the passage off the Apothecarium. If you lose the ledger, take another from Andron's bookshelf.
turnin 1899
accept 1978
turnin 1978]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/rogue/certificate-of-thievery", title = "Certificate of Thievery", faction = "Alliance", class = "Rogue", levels = "16-20", zone = "Stormwind City", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/rogue/certificate-of-thievery"] = [==[guide: Certificate of Thievery
id: forever/class/rogue/certificate-of-thievery
level: 16-20
map: 1453
section SI:7 (Goldshire)
tip At 16 Keryn Sylvius, the rogue trainer upstairs in the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, sends you to Renzik "The Shiv" in Stormwind. Taking it shuts out the other towns' breadcrumbs.
level 16
accept 2300
section To Hulfdan! (Kharanos)
tip At 16 Hogral Bakkan in the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos sends you to Hulfdan Blackbeard in Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern.
level 16
accept 2299
section Hulfdan Blackbeard
tip Hulfdan is in the house with a shady dealer outside, in the Forlorn Cavern, down the stairs. Then fly or take the Deeprun Tram to Stormwind.
turnin 2299
accept 2298
section Erion Shadewhisper (Dolanaar)
tip At 16 Jannok Breezesong in the Dolanaar inn sends you to Erion Shadewhisper in Darnassus.
level 16
accept 2259
section Erion Shadewhisper
tip Erion stands in the Cenarion Enclave. Then the boat from Rut'theran Village to Auberdine, and the boat from Auberdine to Stormwind Harbor.
turnin 2259
accept 2260
section Renzik "The Shiv"
tip Renzik stands upstairs in the SI:7 building in Old Town, behind the rogue trainers. Before you leave: if you lack Pick Lock, Lord Tony Romano in the SI:7 building teaches it; Lockpicking is the test of the next quest.
turnin 2300 only Human,Skyborne
turnin 2298 only Dwarf,Gnome
turnin 2260 only NightElf
accept 2281
section Lucius
tip Head east through Elwynn Forest into Redridge, or fly to Lakeshire. Lucius stands on a crate on one of the Lakeshire docks, south of town; he gives you Thieves' Tools with the job (Gerald Crawley in Lakeshire sells more). Pick Lock does not work without the tools in your bags.
turnin 2281
accept 2282
section Alther's Mill
tip Alther's Mill stands east of Lakeshire, up off the road; Blackrock orcs roam near it. Inside, the Practice Lockboxes come back almost at once: pick them until Lucius's Lockbox opens for you (about 25 Lockpicking). Your Lockpicking cap rises 5 per level, so a low character may stall. Some boxes are trapped (a frost trap, for one); the skill still goes up. On Forever level 20 spiders wander near the boxes: clear them first or bring a friend. The lockbox always holds the token and is back two seconds after use. Practise on while it still gives skill: the next class quest needs about 75.
objective 2282.1 collect
section Back to Lucius
turnin 2282]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/rogue/plundering-the-plunderers", title = "Plundering the Plunderers", faction = "Horde", class = "Rogue", levels = "16-20", zone = "Orgrimmar", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/rogue/plundering-the-plunderers"] = [==[guide: Plundering the Plunderers
id: forever/class/rogue/plundering-the-plunderers
level: 16-20
map: 1454
section To Orgrimmar!
tip At 16 Kaplak, the rogue trainer in Razor Hill, sends you to Shenthul in Orgrimmar.
level 16
accept 2380
section Find the Shattered Hand
tip At 16 Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter sends you to Shenthul in Orgrimmar. Take Fenwick Thatros from him too; it is done in Silverpine Forest at the end of this guide.
level 16
accept 2378
accept 1998
section Shenthul and Zando'zan
tip Undead take the zeppelin from the towers outside the Undercity to Durotar. Shenthul and Zando'zan stand in the Cleft of Shadow, the canyon under the Valley of Strength. Train Pick Lock from Shenthul (or any rogue trainer) now if you lack it: this job is a lockpicking test.
turnin 2380 only Orc,Troll,Skyborne
turnin 2378 only Undead
accept 2379
turnin 2379
accept 2382
section Wrenix the Wretched
tip Fly or walk to Ratchet on the Barrens coast. Wrenix stands in a small shed near the bank, up the hill to the left before the docks. His Gizmotronic Apparatus beside him hands out what the job needs: take an E.C.A.C. and Thieves' Tools (Pick Lock does not work without the tools in your bags).
getfp Ratchet
turnin 2382
accept 2381
vendor
vendor
section Southsea Treasure
tip Follow the coast south from Ratchet to the first beached pirate ship, the Tide Razor, and climb aboard up its bow. On the middle deck the Buccaneer's Strongboxes come back fast: pick them until your Lockpicking is about 30 (a few are trapped with a frost nova or turn you into a rat; picking still works as a rat). Keep picking while they still give skill: the poisons job at 20 ends at a lockbox that needs about 75, and these boxes are the closest practice. Then go down to the bottom hold and pick the lock of The Jewel of the Southsea: it is empty, but opening it calls a giant level 50 Polly into the next room. Stay stealthed, put the E.C.A.C. on your action bar, target Polly and use it: the parrot shrinks to level 18. Kill it for the Southsea Treasure.
objective 2381.1 collect
section Back to Wrenix
turnin 2381
section Fenwick Thatros
tip Take the zeppelin from Orgrimmar to the Undercity and head south into Silverpine. Fenwick Thatros (level 16) stands alone on the old ferry dock on Lordamere Lake, north-east of the Sepulcher. His Uppercut knocks you back, so do not fight him at the dock's edge. He always drops his head and is back 4 1/2 minutes after a death.
objective 1998.1 collect
section Mennet Carkad
tip If you have no Thieves' Tools left, ask Estelle Gendry, the outfitter in the Rogues' Quarter.
turnin 1998
accept 1999
section Ambermill
tip The Kirin Tor keep their reports in walled Ambermill, in south-east Silverpine. Facing the town hall, take the building on the right: the Ambermill Strongbox is in a corner room upstairs (any Lockpicking opens it; the Thieves' Tools must be in your bags). Three casters of level 19-20 guard that floor and see through stealth, one walking in and out of the strongbox room: time it or fight them one at a time.
objective 1999.1 collect
section Back to Mennet
turnin 1999]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/rogue/poisons-alliance", title = "Poisons (Alliance)", faction = "Alliance", class = "Rogue", levels = "20-24", zone = "Stormwind City", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/rogue/poisons-alliance"] = [==[guide: Poisons (Alliance)
id: forever/class/rogue/poisons-alliance
level: 20-24
map: 1453
section Mathias and the Defias
tip At 20 Master Mathias Shaw, upstairs in the SI:7 building in Old Town, sends you to Agent Kearnen in Westfall. This chain is how you learn Poisons on Forever, so do not skip it.
level 20
accept 2360
section Agent Kearnen
tip Kearnen hides stealthed against the west side of a big tree with two small trees in front of it, just north of Klaven Mortwake's Defias tower in the far east of Westfall, by the Duskwood border. Read Kearnen's Journal for the tower's layout if you like.
turnin 2360
accept 2359
section The Defias Tower Key
tip Get the key first. The Malformed Defias Drone (level 23, not elite) starts at the tower entrance and walks a loop around the outside; it is the spiky-haired one trailing yellow sparkles. Stealth up and Pick Pocket it from behind: it always has the key. It hits hard: if stealth breaks, Sprint away. Watch for the pair of Defias Drones that also patrol.
objective 2359.2 collect
section Klaven's journal
tip Sneak up the tower. Defias Tower Patrollers (23) and Sentries (24) guard the floors; an Ambush with a dagger kills them outright if you would rather clear them. Klaven Mortwake, a level 26 elite, waits on the top floor: Sap him, or bring a friend. The Duskwood Chest beside his desk needs Lockpicking of about 70-75 (practise on the boxes at Alther's Mill in Redridge first). A trick: while the Sentries are away, jump from the chair to the lamp to the bookshelf above the chest, step out of stealth and open the chest from there. Opening it poisons you with the Touch of Zanzil, which stops your stealth for a while and lets the drone see you; that is why the key comes first. Then get out.
objective 2359.1 collect @ 70.4 74.0 map=1436
section Master Mathias Shaw
tip Head north through Elwynn to Stormwind; Mathias Shaw is upstairs in SI:7. He teaches Poisons and gives you the Thistle Tea recipe. Poisons are made, not bought: each batch of Instant Poison takes a Dust of Decay and an Empty Vial, which Jasper Fel and Sloan McCoy sell in Old Town next to SI:7. Buy a stack of each, open Poisons from your spellbook to make them, then use a poison on your weapon.
turnin 2359
accept 2607
section Doc Mixilpixil
tip The Touch of Zanzil still sits on you. Doc Mixilpixil works in the cellar of the SI:7 building: the stairs down are under the stairs to the upper floor, behind Jasper Fel. Target him and type /lay (nothing after it) to be examined, then wait. If he does nothing, abandon the quest, take it again and wait until he asks you to lie down.
turnin 2607
accept 2608
complete 2608 @ 80.06 69.9 map=1453
turnin 2608
accept 2609
section The cure's ingredients
tip All four are in Stormwind. Simple Wildflowers: Bernard or Felicia Gump's flower shop by the Trade District canal. A Leaded Vial: many general goods and alchemy vendors (Keldric Boucher, Jasper Fel and others). A Bronze Tube: the Auction House in the Trade District; the engineering suppliers keep only one and are nearly always sold out, and an engineer can make one. The Spool of Light Chartreuse Silk Thread lies on the floor beside the left end of the counter in The Finest Thread, the tailor's shop on the canals; you can only pick it up with this quest. If you skip the cure, an Anti-Venom (First Aid) or a druid's Cure Poison also clears the Touch of Zanzil.
vendor
vendor
objective 2609.4 collect
section Back to Doc Mixilpixil
turnin 2609]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/rogue/poisons-horde", title = "Poisons (Horde)", faction = "Horde", class = "Rogue", levels = "20-26", zone = "Orgrimmar", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/rogue/poisons-horde"] = [==[guide: Poisons (Horde)
id: forever/class/rogue/poisons-horde
level: 20-26
map: 1454
section Lockpicking practice
tip Gallywix's Lockbox at the end of the tower job needs Lockpicking of about 70-75. Train Pick Lock from Gest or Shenthul in the Cleft of Shadow if you lack it, carry Thieves' Tools, and pick the Buccaneer's Strongboxes on the middle deck of the Tide Razor, the beached pirate ship south of Ratchet: they come back fast. Your cap rises 5 per level.
level 20
goto 64.4 45.4 Tide Razor map=1413
section The Shattered Salute
tip Shenthul stands in the Cleft of Shadow, the canyon under the Valley of Strength. Take the quest and wait: he speaks three lines and salutes you. After his third line, target him and type /salute. If it does not count, abandon the quest and take it again. The tower job ahead is built around Ambush, which needs a dagger: if you have none, Kareth, the blade merchant in the Cleft of Shadow, sells a Jambiya.
accept 2460
complete 2460 @ 43.05 53.74 map=1454
turnin 2460
accept 2458
section Taskmaster Fizzule
tip Fly to the Crossroads and head north to the Venture Co. tower above the Sludge Fen. Fizzule stands under a tree east of the tower, outside it, and is hostile until signalled. Target him from about 50 yards and fire the Flare Gun twice, then walk up in front of him and /salute. In any other order he attacks. Lost the Flare Gun? Abandon and retake from Shenthul.
turnin 2458
accept 2478
section Silixiz's Tower Key
tip Keep Fizzule's Whistle in your bags and use it on him every time you come near, or he turns hostile. Foreman Silixiz (level 22) walks by the tower: hug the wall, stealth up behind him and Pick Pocket the key. Killing him does not give it; if his pockets are empty, kill him and wait 4 1/2 minutes for him to come back.
objective 2478.5 collect
section The Venture Co. tower
tip Inside, floor by floor (everything comes back after 4 1/2 minutes): the Mutated Venture Co. Drones (level 25) on the ground floor die to one Ambush with a dagger; the Patrollers on the second floor take half their health from a one-point Rupture; the Lookouts on the open third floor from a one-point Eviscerate. Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix waits on the top floor: a level 23 elite, back 10 minutes after a kill. Open with Ambush (about half his health), then Gouge, Evasion, a healing potion and Thistle Tea; a friend makes it easy. One head per kill. Then pick Gallywix's Lockbox beside him for the cache: it poisons you with the Touch of Zanzil, which weakens your stealth and agility until Serge Hinott cures it.
objective 2478.1 kill
objective 2478.3 kill
objective 2478.2 kill
objective 2478.4 collect
objective 2478.6 collect
section Back to Shenthul
tip Fly back to Orgrimmar (Ratchet or the Crossroads; dying at the tower and taking the spirit healer's way back to the Crossroads is quicker). Keep Silixiz's Tower Key afterwards. Before you leave the Cleft, buy Dust of Decay and Empty Vials from Rekkul: once Hinott teaches Poisons, each batch of Instant Poison takes one of each.
turnin 2478
accept 2479
section Serge Hinott
tip Take the zeppelin from Orgrimmar to the Undercity and follow the road south through Silverpine Forest into Hillsbrad, to Tarren Mill. Serge Hinott works in the building next to the flight path, beside Apothecary Lydon, a wagon outside. If you lost the Sample of Zanzil's Mixture, abandon and retake from Shenthul. Stay beside him for about a minute while he brews the cure; if it never finishes, abandon and retake from him. Then open Poisons from your spellbook to make Instant Poison from Rekkul's dust and vials, and use it on your weapon.
getfp Tarren Mill
turnin 2479
accept 2480
complete 2480
turnin 2480]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/rogue/ravenholdt", title = "Ravenholdt", class = "Rogue", levels = "24-36", zone = "Hillsbrad Foothills", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/rogue/ravenholdt"] = [==[guide: Ravenholdt
id: forever/class/rogue/ravenholdt
level: 24-36
map: 1424
section The Elegant Letter
tip At 24 any capital's rogue trainer (Master Mathias Shaw or Osborne the Night Man in Stormwind, Gest or Ormok in Orgrimmar, and the others) has an Elegant Letter from Ravenholdt for you: ask for it in their talk window. Open it: the quest gives you the Seal of Ravenholdt for Fahrad. Learn Detect Traps from your trainer first if you have not; the way in is a test of it.
level 24
accept 6681
section Ravenholdt Manor
tip Horde fly to Tarren Mill, Alliance to Southshore. The trail to the manor is hard to see: it starts behind the plateau north of Durnholde Keep, east of Tarren Mill, climbs into the hills and bends twice to a small tunnel. A chest sits in the tunnel: do not open it. Cast Detect Traps near it and walk up close; that is the Rite of Cunning (it comes back after 5 minutes). Opening the chest calls Milton, an elite rogue of about level 32. Through the tunnel lies Ravenholdt Manor: Fahrad is upstairs inside. Do not attack anyone at the manor: it costs Ravenholdt reputation.
objective 6681.1 kill
turnin 6681
accept 96779
section Lord Tomas
tip Lord Tomas is inside Durnholde Keep, the Syndicate fortress south of the manor; he can stand in any of fifteen spots in the keep, so search. Quick and quiet, says Myrokos. Pick the pockets of the level 20-21 Syndicate Rogues, Shadow Mages and Watchmen on your way: they carry Syndicate Emblems for the guards' repeatable reputation quest.
objective 96779.1 kill
section Myrokos Silentform
turnin 96779
turnin 6701
section What's the Big Idea?
tip In your mid 30s Myrokos has two more jobs; take both. Barton leads a Syndicate scouting party at Strahnbrad, in the east of the Alterac Mountains, inside one of the houses with stealthed Syndicate around him. Pick his pocket for the report and do not kill him: he does not drop it. If you are lower than him he sees through stealth; Master of Deception helps, or Distract him, Vanish and come in from behind. Pick Pocket can miss several times in a row.
level 34
accept 96781
accept 96783
objective 96781.1 collect @ 62.6 46.9 map=1416
section Covert Extraction
tip Back to Myrokos; the report sends you after the Perenolde heirlooms. Two towers stand among the Ruins of Alterac, in the middle of the Alterac Mountains, held by ogres: the shield lies in the northern tower, the sword in the southern one, which elite ogres ring and watch from far off. Stay stealthed; nothing guards the heirlooms inside.
turnin 96781
accept 96782
objective 96782.2 collect @ 41.35 40.16 map=1416
objective 96782.1 collect @ 38.5 58.0 map=1416
turnin 96782
section A Way In
tip Stromgarde Keep in western Arathi is a Syndicate stronghold; to get in you need a uniform. Northfold Manor, in north-western Arathi, is held by Syndicate Highwaymen, Pathstalkers and Mercenaries (level 30-32): find the Syndicate Footlocker there and take the uniform; that ends A Way In.
turnin 96783 @ 32.3 26.6 map=1417
accept 96784 @ 32.3 26.6 map=1417 only Horde
section Anastasia Miller
tip Stromgarde's Syndicate Prowlers and Conjurors are elite (level 35-36): a rogue of 36 can slip past them, but fighting one alone is hard, so stay hidden or bring a friend. Put on the Syndicate Uniform (Master of Disguise hands it to you at the footlocker) to pass as one of them; stealth or suspicious acts can break it. If the footlocker gave you no uniform, Anastasia hands you one with Ain't No Telling. Anastasia Miller is not inside the keep: she stands on a ledge on the outside of the castle wall. Jump across to it from the roof of the house beside the ledge.
turnin 96784 @ 26.8 64.4 map=1417 only Horde
accept 96785 @ 26.8 64.4 map=1417
section Ain't No Telling
tip She will not talk without something to bargain with. Her stash is upstairs in a house close to the keep: take the Stolen Funds. If it is already open, wait for it to come back.
objective 96785.1 collect @ 29.5 65.1 map=1417
turnin 96785 @ 26.8 64.4 map=1417
accept 96786 @ 26.8 64.4 map=1417
section The Syndicate Sting
tip Falconcrest's men make the handoff at the southern end of Thoradin's Wall, the old wall between Arathi and Hillsbrad. Kill the two guarding the box and take the Intercepted Shipment. Keep the Syndicate Uniform: Myrokos wants it back with the shipment.
objective 96786.1 collect @ 15.5 43.0 map=1417
section Back to Myrokos
turnin 96786]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/rogue/the-azure-key", title = "The Azure Key", class = "Rogue", levels = "50-52", zone = "Alterac Mountains", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/rogue/the-azure-key"] = [==[guide: The Azure Key
id: forever/class/rogue/the-azure-key
level: 50-52
map: 1416
section A Simple Request (Alliance)
tip At 50 Osborne the Night Man in Stormwind's Old Town has it; so do Syurna in Darnassus and Hulfdan Blackbeard in Ironforge.
level 50
accept 8233
section A Simple Request (Horde)
tip At 50 Ormok in the Cleft of Shadow has it; so does Miles Dexter in the Undercity's Rogues' Quarter.
level 50
accept 8233
section Lord Jorach Ravenholdt
tip Ravenholdt Manor hides in the hills east of Tarren Mill. Horde fly to Tarren Mill, Alliance to Southshore. The trail starts behind the plateau north of Durnholde Keep, climbs into the hills and runs through a small tunnel into the Alterac Mountains; Lord Jorach is inside the manor. Do not attack anyone at the manor: lost Ravenholdt reputation makes him refuse to speak to you.
turnin 8233
accept 8234
section Sealed Azure Bag
tip Alliance fly to Talrendis Point, Horde to Valormok. Only the level 50-51 Timbermaw Shamans in the furbolg hills of northern Azshara carry the bag (the level 47-49 furbolgs further south do not): about one kill in thirty drops it. Pick Pocket them instead and you lose no Timbermaw reputation; if you are Unfriendly or better with Timbermaw Hold, mark them At War in your reputation panel first. They cast Lightning Bolt and Lightning Cloud, heal each other and run at low health.
getfp Talrendis Point only Alliance
getfp Valormok only Horde
objective 8234.1 collect
section Archmage Xylem
tip Sanath Lim-yo, camped below the cliffs just east of Valormok, teleports you up (dismount first); a trail leads to Xylem's tower.
turnin 8234
accept 8235
section Encoded Fragments
tip The Forest Oozes (level 52-53, Diseased Slime up close) drop a fragment four times in five: the biggest group, seven of them, is in the Bitter Reaches hills of north-eastern Azshara, four more south-east of Valormok. Pick their pockets before the kill for an extra fragment or two. Killing the Mistwing Ravagers and hippogryphs that share their spots makes more oozes appear.
objective 8235.1 collect
section Back to Xylem
turnin 8235
accept 8236
section Morphaz in the Sunken Temple
tip Morphaz, a level 52 elite green drake, lives deep in the Sunken Temple: a group of five, level 50-54. The temple stands in the Pool of Tears; climb into the sunken building, swim down through it and follow the passage to the portal. Horde: fly to Stonard; Alliance: fly to Nethergarde Keep and ride on. He is not there when you arrive: first kill the six troll guardians (elites of 50-52) on the platforms around the upper ring, which opens the way down (the left-hand ramp from the entrance) to Jammal'an the Prophet in the Pit of Sacrifice. Jammal'an's death brings out two drakes, Weaver and Dreamscythe; when both are dead, Morphaz and Hazzas appear together and fight as a pair. Their Acid Breath is nature damage: nature protection potions help; poisons and Blind do not work on them. The key always drops. Hunters, Priests and Mages of 50 need Morphaz too: one clear serves them all.
objective 8236.1 collect @ 69.9 53.6 map=1435
section Lord Ravenholdt
tip Look at the reward window before you hand in: Classic offered the Duskbat Drape, the Ebon Mask or the Whisperwalk Boots, and Forever's notes say the choice may be gone.
turnin 8236]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/rogue/the-eye-of-bhossca", title = "The Eye of Bhossca", class = "Rogue", levels = "30-35", zone = "Silverpine Forest", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/rogue/the-eye-of-bhossca"] = [==[guide: The Eye of Bhossca
id: forever/class/rogue/the-eye-of-bhossca
level: 30-35
map: 1421
section C's dead drop
tip C's next job comes by letter: once you are level 30 and have done the horn job, visit any capital city and C's letter arrives in the mailbox; only then does the Dead Drop near Pyrewood Village, in southern Silverpine just south of Shadowfang Keep, offer it. The quest data lists a minimum of 25, but players get the letter, and the job, at 30.
level 30
accept 78676
section The Scarlet Monastery
tip The monastery stands in the far north-east of Tirisfal Glades. Go in alone, out of any group. Before entering, take the Scarlet Initiate's Uniform from the Supply Locker in the stables behind the monastery and wear it; stealth and suspicious actions remove it, so put it back on after each wing change. In the Graveyard, in the Chamber of Atonement (the first big room), Pick Pocket a Scarlet Scryer or Scarlet Crier for the Scryer's Key. In the Library, open the Personal Letterbox in the Athenaeum with it and read the Confidential Message. It sends you back to sit on both benches between the two statues in the Graveyard. Watch for the mechanism's messages, then take the Reliquary Key from the stone coffer: an elite stands by the coffer with a patrol behind it, but from beside the northern mausoleum you can turn the camera until the box shows and click it through the wall (an interact key works too). An elite ghost walks near the mausoleum; the broken piece at its edge keeps you out of its path. Then return to the Library for the locked reliquary and the eye. Avoid fighting through the instance.
goto 82.6 33.8 Scarlet Monastery map=1420
note Solo route: Graveyard key, Library letter, Graveyard benches and coffer, then Library reliquary for the eye. Read the letter before the bench puzzle; check the disguise each time you change wings.
section Back to the dead drop
tip Place the eye in the Dead Drop near Pyrewood. Check a capital mailbox for C's payment letter on your next planned city visit, then return here for the reward quest. The payment may not be available immediately; do not repeat the infiltration just because the reward has not appeared.
turnin 78676
accept 78699
turnin 78699]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/rogue/the-horn-of-xelthos", title = "The Horn of Xelthos", class = "Rogue", levels = "23-26", zone = "Silverpine Forest", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/rogue/the-horn-of-xelthos"] = [==[guide: The Horn of Xelthos
id: forever/class/rogue/the-horn-of-xelthos
level: 23-26
map: 1421
section C's dead drop
tip The Dead Drop is a chest in a house just outside Pyrewood Village in southern Silverpine, south of Shadowfang Keep. Open it and read C's note: the job has to be done alone, out of any group.
level 23
accept 78261
section Veenix
tip Veenix, a goblin friendly to both factions, stands among the Venture Co. in the Windshear Crag, east Stonetalon, a short way north-east of Sun Rock Retreat. Horde fly to Sun Rock Retreat; Alliance to Stonetalon Peak. He wants a Venture Co. Work Order before he hands over explosives: the Venture Co. Loggers (level 18) working around him carry them in their pockets. Stealth up behind one and Pick Pocket it; killing them does not give it.
accept 78270
turnin 78270
section Shadowfang Keep
tip Go in alone and use the Breaching Charge at the courtyard gate. Players also report a freed prisoner opening the courtyard door for you: if you die while he is opening it, stay dead until it is open; it stays open once you release. If you know Vanish, bring Flash Powder and check its cooldown before entering; keep it ready for a failed approach. Pickpocket the sister in the dining hall for the Sister's Half-Key, then the brother in the room reached by turning right at the top of the stairs for the Brother's Half-Key (a level 20 rogue without Vanish may need ranks in Master of Deception to reach the second one unseen). Combine them somewhere safe: this breaks stealth. Free a bag slot first: opening the chest with full bags can use up the key without giving the horn. Return to the courtyard stables and use the combined key on the chest for the horn. Stay clear of the nearby elites; the minimum quest level does not guarantee a safe approach.
objective 78261.1 collect @ 44.8 67.8 map=1421
section Back to the dead drop
tip Place the horn in the Dead Drop near Pyrewood. The payment may not appear immediately: check a capital mailbox for C's follow-up letter on your next planned city visit, then return to this chest for the reward quest. Do not repeat the dungeon just because the payment is not yet offered.
turnin 78261
accept 78307
turnin 78307]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/shaman/call-of-air-alliance", title = "Call of Air and the Tempest's Weapons (Alliance)", faction = "Alliance", class = "Shaman", levels = "30-40", zone = "Ironforge", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/shaman/call-of-air-alliance"] = [==[guide: Call of Air and the Tempest's Weapons (Alliance)
id: forever/class/shaman/call-of-air-alliance
level: 30-40
map: 1455
section Eldrun Stormbreaker
tip At 30 Eldrun Stormbreaker, the shaman trainer in Ironforge, sends you to Veyric Thunderhame in Arathi Highlands. Your level 30 air totems (Grounding, Nature Resistance) need the Air Totem he gives.
level 30
accept 94789
section Veyric Thunderhame
tip Veyric Thunderhame camps in the hills just west of Hammerfall, the Horde town in the north-east of Arathi: mind its guards. Fly to Refuge Pointe and head north-east.
turnin 94789
accept 96264
section Charlga Razorflank
tip Razorfen Kraul is a five-player dungeon at the southern edge of the Barrens (the arrow points at its entrance); Charlga Razorflank (level 33 elite) is its last boss. She casts Chain Bolt, Renew on her allies and Purity; the Tattered Note drops only from her.
objective 96264.1 collect @ 42.9 90.2 map=1413
section Veyric Thunderhame
turnin 96264
accept 79358
section Twisted Fire Totems
tip Five Twisted Fire Totems. The Stonevault troggs (Skullthumpers, Bonesnappers and Shamans, level 37-41) south of Angor Fortress in the Badlands carry them; the Shamans drop Fire Nova Totems and a Healing Ward, the Bonesnappers run for help when hurt. Respawn about five minutes.
level 36
objective 79358.3 collect
section Twisted Earth Totems
tip Five Twisted Earth Totems. The Lost Ones (murlocs, level 34-39) north and north-east of Stonard in the Swamp of Sorrows carry them; most run for help when hurt.
level 33
objective 79358.2 collect
section Twisted Water Totems
tip Five Twisted Water Totems. The Mirefin murlocs (level 35-38) north-east of Brackenwall Village in northern Dustwallow Marsh carry them.
level 34
objective 79358.1 collect
section Twisted Air Totems
tip Five Twisted Air Totems. The Maraudine centaurs (level 36-40) north and north-east of Shadowprey Village in western Desolace carry them; the Scouts drop one nearly every other kill. Wranglers Net and Disarm, Windchasers heal, Stormers throw Jumping Lightning: pull one at a time. Respawn about five minutes.
level 36
objective 79358.4 collect
section Veyric Thunderhame
turnin 79358
accept 96135
section The steam pools
tip Veyric hands you the Corrupted Totems. Thousand Needles is far: the boat to Theramore and the road west, or fly to Thalanaar on the Feralas border and head east into the canyon. Place the Corrupted Totems at the steam pools north-west of Freewind Post to call the corrupted elementals and then the Ravaging Tempest; Razormane quilboar join the fight while the ritual runs. A group quest: bring at least one or two friends. The Eye of the Tempest drops about every other kill, and every group member can loot it.
level 38
objective 96135.1 collect
section Veyric Thunderhame
turnin 96135
accept 96016
section Bath'rah the Windwatcher
tip Bath'rah camps in the ruins in the east of Alterac Mountains: from Tarren Mill follow the river east of town north into the hills. Pick your weapon: Lightning's Grasp, Tidebringer's Claw or Rage of the Storm.
turnin 96016]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/shaman/call-of-air-horde", title = "Call of Air and the Tempest's Weapons (Horde)", faction = "Horde", class = "Shaman", levels = "30-40", zone = "Orgrimmar", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/shaman/call-of-air-horde"] = [==[guide: Call of Air and the Tempest's Weapons (Horde)
id: forever/class/shaman/call-of-air-horde
level: 30-40
map: 1454
section Searn Firewarder
tip At 30 Searn Firewarder in the Valley of Wisdom sends you to Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles. Your level 30 air totems (Grounding, Nature Resistance) need the Air Totem she gives.
level 30
accept 1531
section Alaana Stormwalker
tip At 30 Skyborne shamans get their own Call of Air. Alaana Stormwalker waits where the airship from Zephras Isle lands, in northern Mulgore beside Thunder Bluff. Your level 30 air totems need the Air Totem Prate Cloudseer gives. If she has nothing for you, head up to Xanis Flameweaver in Thunder Bluff (next step): the trainers' Call of Air is open to Skyborne and gives the same totem.
level 30
accept 96136
section Xanis Flameweaver
tip At 30 Xanis Flameweaver, a shaman trainer on Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff, sends you to Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles. Your level 30 air totems (Grounding, Nature Resistance) need the Air Totem Prate gives. Already carry Searn Firewarder's Call of Air from Orgrimmar? It goes to Prate too: skip Xanis.
level 30 when !onquest 1531
accept 1532 when !onquest 1531
section Prate Cloudseer
tip Fly to Freewind Post. Prate Cloudseer stands on a ledge above a cave mouth in the canyon wall north-east of the post, not inside the cave: climb the slope beside it. She also gives you an hour of faster attacks and running.
goto 53.5 42.6 Prate Cloudseer map=1441
section 
