HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/shaman/call-of-earth-alliance", title = "Call of Earth (Alliance)", faction = "Alliance", class = "Shaman", levels = "4-5", zone = "Dun Morogh", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/shaman/call-of-earth-alliance"] = [==[guide: Call of Earth (Alliance)
id: forever/class/shaman/call-of-earth-alliance
level: 4-5
map: 1426
section Archaic Rune
tip Teo's Call of Earth needs the Archaic Rune handed in first: Sten Stoutarm, where you entered Coldridge Valley, gives it to Dwarf shamans after his Dwarven Outfitters. Bring it up the road to Teo Hammerstorm inside Anvilmar.
accept 98581 when !turnedin 98581
turnin 98581 when !turnedin 98581
section Teo Hammerstorm
tip Teo Hammerstorm trains shamans inside Anvilmar, the hall at the south end of Coldridge Valley. The quest opens at level 4. Never took it and now 10 or more? Eldrun Stormbreaker in Ironforge or Ingrid Dunwald in Kharanos gives you Call of Earth, a pointer back to Teo: take it for the experience on the way.
level 4
accept 94373
section Iceclaw Bear Pendants
tip The Frostmane Troll Whelps (level 3-4) hold the snowy slopes west and south-west of Anvilmar, and the Frostmane Novices (level 3-4, they throw Frostbolts from range) camp south of it. Both carry the pendants; they respawn in about three minutes.
objective 94373.1 collect
section Teo Hammerstorm
tip Back to Teo inside Anvilmar. He hands you the Earth Sapta: do not drink it yet.
turnin 94373
accept 94374
section Lost the Earth Sapta?
tip Only if the Earth Sapta is gone from your bags (drunk away from the stone, or sold): Teo gives you another.
turnin 94472 when !has 6635
section The Spirit Stone
tip The Spirit Stone stands on a snowy ridge north-west of Anvilmar. The trail is easy to miss: it climbs the hill from the valley floor; at the small camp near the top turn left and the stone comes into view. Stand beside it, drink the Earth Sapta and speak to the Minor Manifestation of Earth before it fades.
turnin 94374
accept 94375
section Teo Hammerstorm
tip Bring the Rough Quartz back to Teo inside Anvilmar. Keep the Earth Totem in your bags for good: every earth totem needs it.
turnin 94375
train]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/shaman/call-of-earth-horde", title = "Call of Earth (Horde)", faction = "Horde", class = "Shaman", levels = "4-5", zone = "Durotar", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/shaman/call-of-earth-horde"] = [==[guide: Call of Earth (Horde)
id: forever/class/shaman/call-of-earth-horde
level: 4-5
map: 1411
section Canaga Earthcaller
tip Canaga Earthcaller stands just outside the Den, the cave in the middle of the Valley of Trials. The quest opens at level 4.
level 4
accept 1516
section Felstalker Hooves
tip Felstalkers (level 3-4) prowl the slope below the Burning Blade Coven, the cave in the north of the valley, and just inside its mouth among the Vile Familiars. Nearly every Felstalker drops a hoof (four kills in five); they respawn in a little over three minutes.
objective 1516.1 collect
section Canaga Earthcaller
tip Back to Canaga outside the Den. She hands you the Earth Sapta: do not drink it yet.
turnin 1516
accept 1517
section Lost the Earth Sapta?
tip Only if the Earth Sapta is gone from your bags (drunk away from the rock, or sold): Canaga gives you another.
turnin 1463 when !has 6635
section Spirit Rock
tip Spirit Rock sits on a ledge in the hills just south of the Den. The Hidden Path up starts at the foot of the hills south-west of the Den, between two idle peons; it climbs south-west into the hills, then bends back east to the rock. Stand right beside the stone and drink the Earth Sapta: the Minor Manifestation of Earth appears for a short while, so speak to it at once (walk almost under it if it does not answer). Coming back, you can drop down the ledge towards the Den instead of walking the path.
turnin 1517
accept 1518
section Canaga Earthcaller
tip Bring the Rough Quartz back to Canaga outside the Den. Keep the Earth Totem she gives you in your bags for good: every earth totem needs it.
turnin 1518
train
section Seer Ravenfeather
tip Seer Ravenfeather stands in Camp Narache. She may show no quest mark over her head: speak to her anyway. The quest opens at level 4.
level 4
accept 1519
section Ritual Salve
tip The Bristleback Shamans (level 3-4) stand among the quilboar huts of Brambleblade Ravine, east of the camp, and throw the odd Lightning Bolt. Four kills in five drop a salve; they respawn in about four minutes.
objective 1519.1 collect
section Seer Ravenfeather
tip Back to the Seer in Camp Narache. She hands you the Earth Sapta: do not drink it yet.
turnin 1519
accept 1520
section Lost the Earth Sapta?
tip Only if the Earth Sapta is gone from your bags: the Seer gives you another.
turnin 1462 when !has 6635
section Kodo Rock
tip Kodo Rock is a small pillar on a low mound due east of Greatmother Hawkwind's well, east of the camp; it only shows from about fifteen yards away, and hostile boars graze around it. Stand beside it and drink the Earth Sapta, then speak to the Minor Manifestation of Earth before it fades (drink again if it does).
turnin 1520
accept 1521
section Seer Ravenfeather
tip Bring the Rough Quartz back to the Seer. Keep the Earth Totem in your bags for good: every earth totem needs it.
turnin 1521
train
section Windshaper Boro
tip Windshaper Boro, the shaman trainer, stands in Thendal Village. The quest opens at level 3.
level 3
accept 92466
section Signet of Akir
tip Any Al'Aketh cultist can carry the Signet of Akir: the Converts (level 2-3) around the standing stones just east of the village, or the Brutes and Neophytes (level 4) in the camp beyond Hanaa Nightwind, south-west of the village. Keep killing until one drops it.
objective 92466.1 collect
section Windshaper Boro
tip Back to Boro in Thendal Village. He hands you the Earth Sapta: do not drink it yet.
turnin 92466
accept 92467
section The Rise of Spirits
tip The Rise of Spirits is the hilltop shrine north-east of Boro: the path up starts on the hill just above the clearing where the flies were. Drink the Earth Sapta beside the shrine and speak to the Minor Manifestation of Earth before it fades.
turnin 92467
accept 92468
section Windshaper Boro
tip Bring the Rough Quartz back to Boro. Keep the Earth Totem in your bags for good: every earth totem needs it.
turnin 92468
train]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/shaman/call-of-fire-alliance", title = "Call of Fire (Alliance)", faction = "Alliance", class = "Shaman", levels = "10-14", zone = "Dun Morogh", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/shaman/call-of-fire-alliance"] = [==[guide: Call of Fire (Alliance)
id: forever/class/shaman/call-of-fire-alliance
level: 10-14
map: 1426
section Call of Fire
tip At 10 Ingrid Dunwald, the shaman trainer in Kharanos, or Eldrun Stormbreaker, the shaman trainer in Ironforge, sends you to Bruegs Kindleborn.
level 10
accept 94449
section Bruegs Kindleborn
tip Follow the road east to the tunnel towards South Gate Outpost. Out of the first tunnel, keep left past Mountaineer Barleybrew and the tower: a slim trail, hard to see but shown on the minimap, winds up the mountain to Bruegs' cave above the farm. He hands you the Torch of the Dormant Flame: keep it until the end of the chain.
turnin 94449
accept 94465
section Braldir Ashmantle
tip From Bruegs' ledge you can drop carefully down the mountain into Loch Modan, or walk back through the tunnel. Braldir Ashmantle keeps the shrine on the peak just south of Thelsamar: a hidden trail along a cliff ledge, marked by stone totems, climbs to it from the road north of the peak.
turnin 94465
accept 94466
section Reagent Pouch
tip The Stonesplinter Seers (level 13-14) stand among the troggs of Stonesplinter Valley in the south of the loch, and in the trogg camps north-east of Thelsamar. They throw Lightning Bolts from 40 yards and run for help when hurt: pull one at a time. Respawn about five minutes.
objective 94466.2 collect
section Fire Tar
tip The Tunnel Rat Geomancers (level 12-13) work only inside the Silver Stream Mine at the north end of the loch, past Thelsamar. They cast Fire Blast behind a Fire Shield and run for help at low health.
objective 94466.1 collect
section Braldir Ashmantle
tip Back up the trail to Braldir. He makes the Fire Sapta from the tar and the pouch: keep it with the torch.
turnin 94466
accept 94467
section Lost the Fire Sapta?
tip Only if the Fire Sapta is gone from your bags: Braldir gives you another.
turnin 94473 when !has 6636
section The Shrine of Eternal Flame
tip Climb on past Braldir to the peak. Drink the Fire Sapta beside the rock statue there to see the Minor Manifestation of Fire (level 12): it waits until you strike, but grows stronger the longer it is left, and it is immune to fire. Open at once with Rockbiter Weapon and Earth Shock. Its Glowing Ember drops every time.
objective 94467.1 use @ 31.9 64.5 map=1432
objective 94467.1 collect
section The Brazier of the Dormant Flame
tip Click the Brazier of the Dormant Flame atop the shrine with the torch in your bags to place the ember, then click it again for the next quest: the lit Torch of Eternal Flame.
turnin 94467
accept 94468
section Bruegs Kindleborn
tip Back through the South Gate tunnel and up the trail to Bruegs' cave. Keep the Fire Totem in your bags for good: every fire totem needs it.
turnin 94468
train]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/shaman/call-of-fire-horde", title = "Call of Fire (Horde)", faction = "Horde", class = "Shaman", levels = "10-13", zone = "The Barrens", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/shaman/call-of-fire-horde"] = [==[guide: Call of Fire (Horde)
id: forever/class/shaman/call-of-fire-horde
level: 10-13
map: 1413
section Swart
tip At 10 Swart, the shaman trainer on the east side of Razor Hill, sends you to Kranal Fiss in the Barrens. Already carry Searn Firewarder's letter from Orgrimmar? It goes to Kranal too: skip Swart.
level 10
accept 2983
section Narm Skychaser
tip At 10 Narm Skychaser, the shaman trainer in Bloodhoof Village, sends you to Kranal Fiss in the Barrens. Already carry Xanis Flameweaver's letter from Thunder Bluff? It goes to Kranal too: skip Narm.
level 10
accept 2984
section Kranal Fiss
tip Kranal Fiss is not in the Crossroads: take the road north from the Crossroads and fork east towards Durotar; past Grol'dom Farm he paces by a tall tower east of the road (from Durotar: over the Southfury bridge, past Far Watch Post). If you reach Ashenvale you went too far.
goto 56.0 19.9 Kranal Fiss map=1413
section 
turnin 2983 when onquest 2983
section 
turnin 1522 when onquest 1522
section 
turnin 2984 when onquest 2984
section 
turnin 1523 when onquest 1523
section Kranal Fiss
tip Kranal hands you the Torch of the Dormant Flame: keep it until the end of the chain.
accept 1524
section Telf Joolam
tip Back east over the bridge, then south along the Durotar bank of the river to where the mountains meet the water. The trail up starts at the foot of the mountain beside a small dark stone carved with symbols, near the quilboar camp; it is narrow, and a slip costs fall damage. Telf Joolam keeps the shrine at the top.
turnin 1524
accept 1525
section Fire Tar
tip The Razormane casters north-east of the Crossroads drop the Fire Tar three times in four: Water Seekers and Thornweavers (level 10-11), Geomancers (level 12-13, they throw Fireballs and run for help when hurt) and Mystics (level 13-14, they heal themselves at low health). Pull them one at a time.
objective 1525.1 collect
section Reagent Pouch
tip The Burning Blade Cultists (level 10-11, they call imps and cast Immolate) live deep in Dustwind Cave north of Razor Hill: climb the ramp just north-east of town and stay on the high ground above the ravines. The orcs at the cave mouth are not cultists; the cultists are further in, off to the left. Three kills in four drop a pouch. Skull Rock by Orgrimmar is the wrong cave.
objective 1525.2 collect
section Telf Joolam
tip Back up the trail to Telf. He makes the Fire Sapta from the tar and the pouch and hands it to you with the torch: keep both.
turnin 1525
accept 1526
section Lost the Fire Sapta?
tip Only if the Fire Sapta is gone from your bags: Telf gives you another.
turnin 1464 when !has 6636
section The Minor Manifestation of Fire
tip Drink the Fire Sapta beside the Shaman Shrine, the big grey stone just below the summit, then climb to the plateau. Of the fire elementals there only the one in the middle can be attacked: it is level 12, immune to fire and grows stronger the longer the fight lasts, so open at once with Rockbiter Weapon and Earth Shock and leave the others alone. Its Glowing Ember drops every time.
objective 1526.1 use @ 38.1 58.5 map=1411
objective 1526.1 collect
section The Brazier of the Dormant Flame
tip Click the Brazier of the Dormant Flame on the plateau with the torch in your bags to place the ember, then click it a second time: the next quest does not open by itself. It gives you the lit Torch of Eternal Flame.
turnin 1526
accept 1527
section Kranal Fiss
tip Down the trail, back over the bridge to Kranal Fiss by his tower. Keep the Fire Totem in your bags for good: every fire totem needs it.
turnin 1527
section Sessaria Skystride
tip At 10 Sessaria Skystride, the shaman trainer beside Ayessa Dawnsinger in Valanaar, hands you the Torch of the Dormant Flame (Aarnor Galestrike offers the same quest). Already left the isle? A Call of Fire sends you back to them: take the skycutter from the cliffs south of Skywatcher Plateau, north of Thunder Bluff. Learn Flame Shock from her now: Kuramaa, later in the chain, only takes fire damage.
level 10
accept 97243
train
section Olariaan Swiftburn
tip The Shrine of Flames hides on the island's outer rim south-west of Valanaar, just south-east of Windfield Orchard: Olariaan Swiftburn keeps it.
turnin 97243
accept 97244
section Skypriest Faladiel
tip Skypriest Faladiel (level 10, a turncoat Windshaper with a single spawn) holds the farm north-east past Valanaar, just south of the Shrine of Akir, on the hill west of the falls north of the East Pylon Watchtower. Kill him and take his heart.
objective 97244.1 collect
section Olariaan Swiftburn
tip Back to Olariaan at the Shrine of Flames.
turnin 97244
accept 97245
section Kuramaa
tip Kuramaa's Stump is the twisted stump on the hilltop by the Shen'dar Highlands Anchor Pylon, west of Valanaar, in the hills south of the Windsong Crawlers' lakes. Knock on it to call Kuramaa (level 10). The spirit shrugs off most magic: only fire hurts it, so keep Flame Shock on it. Take its wooden mask.
objective 97245.1 collect
section The Eternal Flame
tip Back to Olariaan. Accept the last quest, then wait by the Brazier of Offering while he performs the ritual; when the fire spirits light the Eternal Flame, hold the torch to it. From then you have six minutes: carry the flame straight to the Brazier of Eternal Flame beside Sessaria in Valanaar, with no detours or fights. Timer out? Abandon the quest and take it again from Olariaan.
turnin 97245
accept 97257
goto 51.2 85.9 Brazier of Offering map=2521
complete 97257 @ 58.4 78.8 map=2521
section Sessaria Skystride
tip Keep the Fire Totem in your bags for good: every fire totem needs it.
turnin 97257]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/shaman/call-of-water-alliance", title = "Call of Water (Alliance)", faction = "Alliance", class = "Shaman", levels = "20-23", zone = "Ironforge", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/shaman/call-of-water-alliance"] = [==[guide: Call of Water (Alliance)
id: forever/class/shaman/call-of-water-alliance
level: 20-23
map: 1455
section Eldrun Stormbreaker
tip At 20 Eldrun Stormbreaker, the shaman trainer in Ironforge's Mystic Ward, sends you to Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan.
level 20
accept 94494
section Norric Lochthane
tip Norric's burrow hut stands on the north-western shore of the loch, below Stonewrought Dam, north of Thelsamar.
turnin 94494
accept 94495
section Hervdana Saegrund
tip Hervdana's family lives in a cave beneath the southern falls of the Wetlands, east of Dun Algaz: not in a town. Through the Algaz tunnel north of Loch Modan, then east off the road.
turnin 94495
accept 94497
section The brown waterskin
tip Fill the Unfilled Brown Waterskin at the bottom of the waterfalls below Hervdana's cave, where the fresh water meets the brackish. Dark Iron dwarves roam near the falls.
objective 94497.1 collect @ 65.8 76.5 map=1437
section Hervdana Saegrund
turnin 94497
accept 94499
section The red waterskin
tip Stonewatch Falls pour out of Lake Everstill at the east end of Redridge (fly from Ironforge to Lakeshire). Fill the Unfilled Red Waterskin at their foot, where the Murloc Nightcrawlers gather; pull the murlocs off the spot first. If the skin vanishes without counting, abandon the quest and take it again from Hervdana for a new one.
objective 94499.1 collect @ 71.9 60.3 map=1433
section Hervdana Saegrund
turnin 94499
accept 94500
section The blue waterskin
tip Take the boat from Menethil Harbor to Auberdine (it stops in Southshore on the way), then fly or walk south through Darkshore to Astranaar in Ashenvale. Fill the Unfilled Blue Waterskin in the lake around the town, then the boat back to Menethil.
objective 94500.1 collect @ 34.5 48.0 map=1440
section Hervdana Saegrund
turnin 94500
accept 94501
section Norric Lochthane
tip Back to Norric by Stonewrought Dam with the Vial of Purest Water. He hands you the Water Sapta and the Remaining Drops of Purest Water: keep both for Westfall.
turnin 94501
accept 94502
section Lost the Water Sapta?
tip Only if the Water Sapta is gone from your bags: Norric gives you another before you leave for Westfall.
accept 94616 when !has 6637
turnin 94616 when !has 6637
section Stendel's Pond
tip Fly to Sentinel Hill and head south to Moonbrook: Stendel's Pond and the Forgotten Shrine lie just north of it. Drink the Water Sapta by the shrine to see the Corrupt Minor Manifestation of Water (level 22, Frost Shock and Frost Nova; one spawn, back three minutes after a kill), defeat it for its bracers (always dropped), then place them and the Remaining Drops of Purest Water on the Forgotten Shrine (this, not Norric, ends the quest). Click the shrine again: the Minor Manifestation of Water rises beside it; speak to it before you walk off (if it is gone, abandon and take the quest again at the shrine). It gives you the Shard of Water.
objective 94502.1 use @ 45.6 59.9 map=1436
objective 94502.1 collect @ 45.6 59.9 map=1436
turnin 94502
accept 94503
turnin 94503 @ 46.4 59.2 map=1436
accept 94505 @ 46.4 59.2 map=1436
section Norric Lochthane
tip Back to Norric with the Shard of Water. Keep the Water Totem in your bags for good: every water totem needs it.
turnin 94505]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/shaman/call-of-water-horde", title = "Call of Water (Horde)", faction = "Horde", class = "Shaman", levels = "20-23", zone = "Orgrimmar", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/shaman/call-of-water-horde"] = [==[guide: Call of Water (Horde)
id: forever/class/shaman/call-of-water-horde
level: 20-23
map: 1454
section Searn Firewarder
tip At 20 Searn Firewarder in the Valley of Wisdom sends you to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens. (Swart in Razor Hill gives the same letter: carry either.)
level 20
accept 1528
section Xanis Flameweaver
tip At 20 Xanis Flameweaver, a shaman trainer on Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff, sends you to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens. (Narm Skychaser in Bloodhoof Village gives the same letter: carry either.)
level 20
accept 1529
section Islen Waterseer
tip Islen is not in Ratchet: take the small coast road south from Ratchet past the pirate camp and over a low hill; her fishing hut, with a shark strung up outside, stands by the water before the pirate ship. If you reach the ship you went too far.
goto 65.8 43.8 Islen Waterseer map=1413
section 
turnin 1528 when onquest 1528
section 
turnin 1529 when onquest 1529
section 
turnin 2985 when onquest 2985
section 
turnin 2986 when onquest 2986
section Islen Waterseer
accept 1530
section Brine
tip Brine lives in the southern Barrens, south of Camp Taurajo: her hut sits on a hilltop of Blackthorn Ridge with a spinning windmill beside it, and the way up is the ridge by the lone tree. Quilboar camp all around the hill; Stormhides, thunderhawks and hyenas roam the plains on the way.
turnin 1530
accept 1535
section The Quilboar Watering Hole
tip The muddy pond below Brine's hut. Step right into the puddle before you use the Empty Brown Waterskin (too far away and it refuses). Filling it calls a hostile Razormane Pathfinder (level 20): kill it, and watch for the quilboar hunter by the pond, who may start shooting afterwards.
objective 1535.1 use @ 44.3 76.8 map=1413
objective 1535.1 collect
section Brine
turnin 1535
accept 1536
section The Spring Well
tip The Spring Well stands in the middle of Tarren Mill, just outside the church. From the Barrens: the zeppelin from Orgrimmar to Tirisfal Glades, then south past the Undercity and through Silverpine Forest (or fly once you have the Tarren Mill flight path). Hillsbrad is contested: Alliance players may attack. Stand beside the well and use the Empty Red Waterskin.
objective 1536.1 use @ 62.2 20.8 map=1424
objective 1536.1 collect
section Brine
turnin 1536
accept 1534
section The Ruins of Stardust
tip The right fountain stands in a ring of standing stones on the island of the small green lake south of Astranaar, west of Lake Mystral (not the island in Lake Mystral itself). From the Barrens take the road north through the Mor'shan Rampart and on west. Water elementals and walking treants guard the lake and root you in place; an elite Wandering Protector roams Ashenvale and can pass close by. Use the Empty Blue Waterskin beside the fountain.
objective 1534.1 use @ 33.6 67.5 map=1440
objective 1534.1 collect
section Brine
tip Back to Brine. She gives you the Vial of Purest Water for Islen.
turnin 1534
accept 220
section Islen Waterseer
tip Islen hands you the Water Sapta and the Remaining Drops of Purest Water: take everything she offers before you leave for Silverpine, or you will be back for more.
turnin 220
accept 63
section Lost the Water Sapta?
tip Only if the Water Sapta is gone from your bags: Islen gives you another.
turnin 972 when !has 6637
section The Brazier of Everfount
tip Fly to the Sepulcher. The shrine lies in a hollow just south-west of it: go round the back of the crypt to the thick tree between the two hills, hop past it onto the rocks and drop west down the slope to the pool (each drop costs a little health). Drink the Water Sapta beside the tall standing stone by the pool: several water elementals appear, and only the corrupt one near the middle can be attacked (Tab picks it). The Corrupt Minor Manifestation of Water is level 22 and casts Frost Shock and Frost Nova; if someone just killed it, it is back in about three minutes. Its bracers always drop.
objective 63.1 use @ 38.3 44.6 map=1421
objective 63.1 collect
section The Minor Manifestation of Water
tip Click the Brazier of Everfount to place the bracers and the drops. A few seconds later the pure Minor Manifestation of Water rises on the stone in the middle of the pool: speak to it while the Sapta Sight lasts (drink again by the stone if it has worn off). It gives you the Shard of Water for Islen. Gone before you could speak to it? Back at Islen ask for Call of Water (a fresh Water Sapta for Tiev Mordune, who stands just west of the shrine): hand it to Tiev, stay close while he calls the spirit back, then speak to it.
turnin 63
accept 100
turnin 100
accept 96
section Islen Waterseer
tip Back to Islen south of Ratchet. Keep the Water Totem in your bags for good: every water totem needs it.
turnin 96]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/shaman/darkreaver", title = "The Darkreaver Menace", faction = "Horde", class = "Shaman", levels = "58-60", zone = "Orgrimmar", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/shaman/darkreaver"] = [==[guide: The Darkreaver Menace
id: forever/class/shaman/darkreaver
level: 58-60
map: 1454
section Sagorne Creststrider
tip At 58 Sagorne Creststrider, the shaman trainer in the Valley of Wisdom, asks for two rare diamonds; every Horde shaman goes to him. Skyborne: Forever's quest page lists this quest for Orcs, Tauren and Trolls only: ask before you buy the diamonds.
accept 7667
section Two diamonds
tip Both diamonds are rare: the auction house is the quick way. Miners find the Azerothian Diamond in about one Thorium vein in a hundred (the Small Thorium Veins north of Morgan's Vigil in the Burning Steppes respawn every five minutes). The Pristine Black Diamond drops from high-level elites at about one in a hundred, best from the rare elite Revanchion (about one in nine).
objective 7667.1 collect
objective 7667.2 collect
section Sagorne Creststrider
tip The Darkreaver Menace needs level 60.
turnin 7667
level 60
accept 8258
section The Great Ossuary
tip A five-player dungeon event: Scholomance lies under Caer Darrow, the island town in the south-east of the Western Plaguelands. In the Great Ossuary's basement, first clear every mob in the room, then use the Divination Scryer at its centre: four waves of spirits follow, each closing with an Aspect mini-boss (the first wave weak and slow, the rest elite). Fight in a corner so nothing else joins, and drink between waves: it is long. Then Death Knight Darkreaver (level 62 elite) appears: he Cleaves, casts Shadow Bolt and Blood Leech, and Dominates a player's mind against the group. His head always drops.
objective 8258.1 collect @ 68.9 75.2 map=1422
section Sagorne Creststrider
turnin 8258]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/shaman/spirit-totem", title = "Spirit Totem and Da Voodoo", faction = "Horde", class = "Shaman", levels = "50-52", zone = "Orgrimmar", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/shaman/spirit-totem"] = [==[guide: Spirit Totem and Da Voodoo
id: forever/class/shaman/spirit-totem
level: 50-52
map: 1454
section Sagorne Creststrider
tip At 50 Sagorne Creststrider, the shaman trainer in the Valley of Wisdom, asks for the four elements for Bath'rah the Windwatcher.
level 50
accept 8410
section Beram Skychaser
tip At 50 Beram Skychaser, a shaman trainer on Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff, asks for the four elements for Bath'rah the Windwatcher. Skyborne: Forever's quest page lists Elemental Mastery and Spirit Totem for Orcs, Tauren and Trolls only; if Beram has nothing for you, Bath'rah's own Mastering the Elements is open to every Horde race, but Spirit Totem after it may still turn you away.
level 50
accept 8410
section The four elements
tip One each of Elemental Air, Fire, Earth and Water; all four trade, so the auction house is quickest. To farm them, Arathi Highlands has the exiles near Refuge Pointe (level 38-39, about one kill in eight to ten, respawn under seven minutes): Thundering Exiles south-east of it (air), Rumbling Exiles south-west (earth), Burning Exiles far to the north-west (fire), and the Summoned Guardian far to the south-west (water, about one in seven). Water comes easier from the Patches of Elemental Water in Azshara (two in five) or Seeker Aqualon by Lakeshire in Redridge.
objective 8410.1 collect
objective 8410.2 collect
objective 8410.3 collect
objective 8410.4 collect
section Bath'rah the Windwatcher
tip Bath'rah camps in the ruins of the east of Alterac Mountains: from Tarren Mill follow the river east of town north into the hills.
turnin 8410
accept 8412
section Spider eye and bear claw
tip Eight of each. Fly or ride to the Bulwark and on to the west edge of the Western Plaguelands, north-west of Chillwind Camp: the Venom Mist Lurkers (level 50-51, they poison) give the Bloodshot Spider Eye and the Diseased Black Bears (level 51-52, Infected Wound) the Thick Black Claw, one kill in five each; the two Carrion Vultures there drop either. The bigger Diseased Grizzlies and Plague Lurkers further east almost never drop them. A few bears and lurkers also roam south-east of Brill in Tirisfal.
objective 8412.1 collect
objective 8412.2 collect
section Bath'rah the Windwatcher
turnin 8412
accept 8413
section The Sunken Temple
tip A five-player dungeon: needs a group of five, about level 50-55. Fly to Stonard and ride east. The Sunken Temple (Temple of Atal'Hakkar) stands in the middle of the Pool of Tears: climb the stairs on the ruin's south side, dive into the flooded hall, swim down through it and follow the stairs and passages down to the portal. Two feathers of each colour, one from each of six elite troll mini-bosses (level 51-52) on the balconies around the temple's great round room, every kill, and each player on the quest loots their own: Gasher and Zul'Lor the Amber, Hukku and Mijan the Blue, Zolo and Loro the Green. Mijan heals the others (Renew, a Healing Ward): kill him first; Hukku summons guardians and throws Shadow Bolt Volleys.
objective 8413.1 collect @ 69.9 53.6 map=1435
objective 8413.2 collect @ 69.9 53.6 map=1435
objective 8413.3 collect @ 69.9 53.6 map=1435
section Bath'rah the Windwatcher
turnin 8413]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/dread-mage-hat", title = "Dread Mage Hat", faction = "Alliance", race = "Human, Gnome", class = "Warlock", levels = "25-30", zone = "Stormwind City", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/dread-mage-hat"] = [==[guide: Dread Mage Hat
id: forever/class/warlock/dread-mage-hat
level: 25-30
map: 1453
section Zardeth of the Black Claw
tip At 25 Zardeth of the Black Claw, in the cellar of the Slaughtered Lamb in the Mage Quarter (beside the warlock trainers), wants two ingredients for a brew. Do it when your leveling takes you to Duskwood and the Wetlands.
level 25
accept 335
section Tear of Tilloa
tip Manor Mistmantle stands in the north-east of Duskwood, north of Darkshire. The Tear of Tilloa is a small white flower low in the grass of the fenced garden beside Stalvan's house: hard to see, so sweep the garden with your mouse. Fetid Corpses (level 29) wander the grounds and come quickly: at 25, send your voidwalker at the nearest one, grab the flower and leave. Stalvan Mistmantle (32) is inside the house; leave him alone.
objective 335.1 collect
section Musquash Root
tip The root grows at the water's edge in the pool below the small falls east of Dun Algaz, beside the Dark Iron cave below the Stonewrought Dam: a tall, spiky wooden root, not at the foot of the dam itself.
objective 335.2 collect
section A Noble Brew
tip Back to Zardeth. He brews the Black Claw Stout and gives it to you for Lord Baurles K. Wishock in the Hall of Petitioners, the first hall on the right inside Stormwind Keep.
turnin 335
accept 336
turnin 336
section You Have Served Us Well
tip Back to Zardeth once more: he offers warlocks a reward, which his imp Zggi, standing beside him, hands over.
accept 397
turnin 397]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/enchanted-gold-bloodrobe", title = "Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe", class = "Warlock", levels = "31-38", zone = "The Barrens", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/enchanted-gold-bloodrobe"] = [==[guide: Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe
id: forever/class/warlock/enchanted-gold-bloodrobe
level: 31-38
map: 1413
section In Search of Menara Voidrender (Stormwind)
tip At 31 Demisette Cloyce in the Slaughtered Lamb, in the Mage Quarter, sends you to Menara Voidrender in Ratchet. Buy a Robes of Arcana and a Gold Bar first (next steps) to save a trip.
level 31
accept 4738
section In Search of Menara Voidrender (Ironforge)
tip At 31 Briarthorn in Ironforge sends you to Menara Voidrender in Ratchet. Buy a Robes of Arcana and a Gold Bar first (next steps) to save a trip.
level 31
accept 4736
section In Search of Menara Voidrender (Orgrimmar)
tip At 31 Zevrost in the Cleft of Shadow sends you to Menara Voidrender in Ratchet. Buy a Robes of Arcana and a Gold Bar first (next steps) to save a trip.
level 31
accept 4737
section In Search of Menara Voidrender (Undercity)
tip At 31 Kaal Soulreaper in the Magic Quarter sends you to Menara Voidrender in Ratchet; the zeppelin from Tirisfal Glades flies to Durotar. Buy a Robes of Arcana and a Gold Bar first (next steps) to save a trip.
level 31
accept 4739
section Robes of Arcana and a Gold Bar
tip Tailors sew the Robes of Arcana from a rare pattern; miners smelt Gold Bars from Gold Ore. Everyone else buys both at the Auction House. If you wear the robe, take it off: Menara keeps it.
section Menara Voidrender
tip Menara Voidrender stands by Strahad Farsan's tower on the hill above Ratchet, behind the engineers' hut. She takes the robe, then sends the gold bar to Xizk Goodstitch in Booty Bay.
turnin 4738 only Human
turnin 4736 only Gnome
turnin 4737 only Orc,Troll
turnin 4739 only Undead
accept 1796
turnin 1796
accept 4781
section Xizk Goodstitch
tip The boat from Ratchet sails to Booty Bay. Xizk Goodstitch runs A Tailor to Cities on an upper level of the town. Give him the Gold Bar; he will spin the thread later.
turnin 4781
accept 4782
section Back to Menara
tip You need no thread yet: Menara wants demon parts from Desolace next.
turnin 4782
accept 4783
section Hatefury satyrs
tip The Hatefury satyrs (level 31-32) hold Sargeron in the far north-east of Desolace, past Nijel's Point: two kills in five give a vial, so plan on about 25.
objective 4783.1 collect
section Mannoroc Coven
tip The Lesser Infernals (36-37) and Demon Portal Guardians (38) of Mannoroc Coven, in the south of Desolace, drop the stone half the time. The guide waits for level 35 first: at 31 they are too strong to solo. They resist fire, so use Shadow Bolt and Corruption.
level 35
objective 4783.2 collect
section Menara again
turnin 4783
accept 4784
section Fine Gold Thread
tip Back to Xizk in Booty Bay: he offers Fine Gold Thread as a quest you hand straight back to him. He may show no quest marker; talk to him anyway.
turnin 4785
objective 4784.1 collect
section Smoldering Coal
tip The Burning Exiles (level 38-39), fire elementals at the Circle of West Binding in western Arathi Highlands, drop the coal about one time in three. The guide waits for level 37 first: below it they hit too hard to solo. They resist fire: Shadow Bolt and Corruption. The Cresting Charms from the Cresting Exiles near Hammerfall finish one off once you have hurt it. Make a Soul Shard with Drain Soul on the way.
level 37
objective 4784.2 collect
objective 4784.3 collect @ 24.9 30.5 map=1417
section The Completed Robe
tip Back to Menara with the thread, the coals and a Soul Shard. Then wait beside her while she works the robe (do not attack her: the quest log calls it a kill), and speak to her again.
turnin 4784
accept 4786
complete 4786 @ 62.5 35.4 map=1413
turnin 4786]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/felhunter-alliance", title = "Felhunter (Alliance)", faction = "Alliance", class = "Warlock", levels = "30-33", zone = "The Barrens", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/felhunter-alliance"] = [==[guide: Felhunter (Alliance)
id: forever/class/warlock/felhunter-alliance
level: 30-33
map: 1413
section Seeking Strahad (Stormwind)
tip At 30 Gakin the Darkbinder, in the cellar of the Slaughtered Lamb in the Mage Quarter, sends you to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.
level 30
accept 1798
section Seeking Strahad (Ironforge)
tip At 30 Lago Blackwrench, in the Forlorn Cavern, sends you to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.
level 30
accept 1798
section Strahad Farsan
tip Ratchet is a neutral goblin port on the Barrens coast: the boat from Booty Bay docks there. Strahad Farsan stands on the hill above the town, behind the engineers' hut, by his little tower; Menara Voidrender and two acolytes are with him. He sends you to Krom Stoutarm in Ironforge.
turnin 1798
accept 1758
section Krom Stoutarm
tip Krom Stoutarm is in the library of the Hall of Explorers. He wants two lost pieces of the Tome of the Cabal: one on the Hillsbrad coast, one in Thousand Needles.
turnin 1758
accept 1802
section Moldy Tome
tip The tome is a small grey-blue book lying in the sand of a murloc camp on the shore south-west of Southshore, near the water's edge. Six or seven murlocs guard it and more lurk underwater: they come in groups, so Fear one and keep your voidwalker on the rest. Walk down to the water to click it; from the hillside the crates block the cursor.
objective 1802.1 collect
section Tattered Manuscript
tip The centaur cave opens in the cliffs north of Freewind Post, a Horde town: keep clear of its guards. Inside, keep right at each fork, cross the pool by the small waterfall, and open the small dark box against the wall beside a larger chest: the larger one is the wrong one. You can open it only while on the quest. The centaurs respawn behind you on the way out.
objective 1802.2 collect
section Back to Krom
tip Krom pieces the tome together and gives you the Reconstructed Tome: keep it, Strahad takes it with the rods.
turnin 1802
accept 1804
section Rods of Channeling
tip The Dragonmaw hold Angerfang Encampment in the hills east of the road from Menethil Harbor to Dun Algaz. Only the casters drop the rods, four kills in five: the Bonewarders (level 27, with skeleton pets) and Shadowwarders (28). A steep path north of the central spirit healer leads up into the camp past most of the warriors.
objective 1804.1 collect
section The Binding
tip Back to Strahad in Ratchet. When you accept, he draws the summoning circle and his acolytes channel a greater circle over it: wait inside the tower until both are done. Then use the Tome of the Cabal on the circle. The felhunter (level 30, not elite) silences and eats mana, and it vanishes after two minutes: have your voidwalker out, open with your damage over time at once and let the voidwalker tank. If you die or it wins, abandon The Binding and take it again from Strahad. Keep the tome: Strahad takes it back.
turnin 1804
accept 1795
objective 1795.1 kill
turnin 1795]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/felhunter-horde", title = "Felhunter (Horde)", faction = "Horde", class = "Warlock", levels = "30-33", zone = "The Barrens", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/felhunter-horde"] = [==[guide: Felhunter (Horde)
id: forever/class/warlock/felhunter-horde
level: 30-33
map: 1413
section Seeking Strahad (Orgrimmar)
tip At 30 Gan'rul Bloodeye, in the Cleft of Shadow under the Valley of Strength, sends you to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.
level 30
accept 2996
section Seeking Strahad (Undercity)
tip At 30 Carendin Halgar, in the Magic Quarter, sends you to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet. The zeppelin from Tirisfal Glades flies to Durotar. Take only one Seeking Strahad: if Strahad offers nothing, drop the duplicate from your log.
level 30
accept 3001
section Strahad Farsan
tip Ratchet's flight point is a short flight from Orgrimmar's. Strahad Farsan stands on the hill above the town, behind the engineers' hut, by his little tower; Menara Voidrender and two acolytes are with him. He sends you to Jorah Annison in the Undercity.
turnin 2996 only Orc,Troll
turnin 3001 only Undead
accept 1801
section Jorah Annison
tip Jorah Annison is in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. He wants two lost pieces of the Tome of the Cabal: one on the Hillsbrad coast, one in Thousand Needles.
turnin 1801
accept 1803
section Moldy Tome
tip The tome is a small grey-blue book lying in the sand of a murloc camp on the shore south-west of Southshore, near the water's edge. Six or seven murlocs guard it and more lurk underwater: they come in groups, so Fear one and keep your voidwalker on the rest. Walk down to the water to click it; from the hillside the crates block the cursor.
objective 1803.1 collect
section Tattered Manuscript
tip The centaur cave opens in the cliffs north of Freewind Post. Inside, keep right at each fork, cross the pool by the small waterfall, and open the small dark box against the wall beside a larger chest: the larger one is the wrong one. You can open it only while on the quest. The centaurs respawn behind you on the way out.
objective 1803.2 collect
section Back to Jorah
tip Jorah pieces the tome together and gives you the Reconstructed Tome: keep it, Strahad takes it with the rods.
turnin 1803
accept 1805
section Rods of Channeling
tip The Dragonmaw hold Angerfang Encampment in the hills east of the road through the Wetlands, south of the Thandol Span you cross from Arathi Highlands. Only the casters drop the rods, four kills in five: the Bonewarders (level 27, with skeleton pets) and Shadowwarders (28). A steep path north of the central spirit healer leads up into the camp past most of the warriors.
objective 1805.1 collect
section The Binding
tip Back to Strahad in Ratchet. When you accept, he draws the summoning circle and his acolytes channel a greater circle over it: wait inside the tower until both are done. Then use the Tome of the Cabal on the circle. The felhunter (level 30, not elite) silences and eats mana, and it vanishes after two minutes: have your voidwalker out, open with your damage over time at once and let the voidwalker tank. If you die or it wins, abandon The Binding and take it again from Strahad. Keep the tome: Strahad takes it back.
turnin 1805
accept 1795
objective 1795.1 kill
