HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/imp-alliance", title = "Imp (Alliance)", faction = "Alliance", class = "Warlock", levels = "1-4", zone = "Elwynn Forest", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/imp-alliance"] = [==[guide: Imp (Alliance)
id: forever/class/warlock/imp-alliance
level: 1-4
map: 1429
section Drusilla La Salle (Humans)
tip Your first letter (Tainted Letter, from Marshal McBride after Kobold Camp Cleanup) points you to Drusilla La Salle, the warlock trainer in the little graveyard beside Northshire Abbey. She asks for a book the Defias stole.
accept 1598
section The Stolen Books
tip The Defias tent stands in the vineyard east of the Abbey. The book is small: it lies on the ground just right of the tent's opening, beside a blue jug. Three Defias Thugs (level 3-4) guard the tent; pull them one at a time, or step inside the tent and click the book, where they cannot reach you. The book respawns three minutes after someone takes it.
objective 1598.1 collect
section Summon Imp
tip Drusilla teaches you Summon Imp at the hand-in: summon it right away, it costs nothing and fights beside you.
turnin 1598
section Alamar Grimm (Gnomes)
tip Your first letter (Tainted Memorandum, from Sten Stoutarm after Dwarven Outfitters) points you to Alamar Grimm, the warlock trainer upstairs inside Anvilmar. He asks for three Feather Charms.
accept 1599
section Feather Charms
tip The Frostmane Novices (level 3-4) sit at the back of the troll cave south of Anvilmar, near Grek'nir the Cold by the icy pool: take the left tunnel past the entrance. Four kills in five drop a charm, but only two or three novices spawn, so you may wait out their three-minute respawn. They throw frostbolts from range; the Troll Whelps at the cave mouth jump anyone who passes. With the charms, your hearthstone takes you straight back: a new character's is set to Coldridge Valley.
objective 1599.1 collect
section Summon Imp
tip Alamar teaches you Summon Imp at the hand-in: summon it right away, it costs nothing and fights beside you.
turnin 1599]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/imp-horde", title = "Imp (Horde)", faction = "Horde", class = "Warlock", levels = "1-4", zone = "Durotar", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/imp-horde"] = [==[guide: Imp (Horde)
id: forever/class/warlock/imp-horde
level: 1-4
map: 1411
section Ruzan (Orcs and Trolls)
tip Your first letter (Tainted Parchment for Orcs, Tainted Tablet for Trolls, from Gornek after Cutting Teeth) points you to Nartok, the warlock trainer in the Den. Ruzan stands just outside the Den in the Valley of Trials and asks for six Vile Familiar Heads.
accept 1485
section Vile Familiars
tip The Vile Familiars (level 3-4) swarm the Burning Blade Coven, the cave north of the Den, inside and around its mouth. Almost every kill drops a head (80%), so about eight kills does it; they throw small fireballs, so pull them one at a time. They respawn in just over three minutes. Other classes hunt the same imps for their own Vile Familiars quest.
objective 1485.1 collect
section Summon Imp
tip Ruzan teaches you Summon Imp when you hand in the heads: summon it right away, it costs nothing and fights beside you. Then speak with Zureetha Fargaze a few steps away for a starter weapon.
turnin 1485
accept 1499
turnin 1499
section Venya Marthand (Undead)
tip Your first letter (Tainted Scroll, from Shadow Priest Sarvis after The Mindless Ones) points you to Maximillion, the warlock trainer in Deathknell. Venya Marthand waits inside the building beside him and asks for three Rattlecage Skulls.
accept 1470
section Rattlecage Skulls
tip The Rattlecage Skeletons (level 2-3) stand around the old smithy buildings just north of Deathknell, often right against the walls. Four kills in five drop a skull, so plan on about five; twenty of them spawn there and each comes back after five minutes.
objective 1470.1 collect
section Summon Imp
tip Venya teaches you Summon Imp when you hand in the skulls: summon it right away, it costs nothing and fights beside you.
turnin 1470]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/impsys-request", title = "An Imp's Request", class = "Warlock", levels = "50-54", zone = "Felwood", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/impsys-request"] = [==[guide: An Imp's Request
id: forever/class/warlock/impsys-request
level: 50-54
map: 1448
section An Imp's Request (Stormwind)
tip At 50 Demisette Cloyce in the Slaughtered Lamb, in the Mage Quarter, sends you to Impsy in Felwood with a piece of Felcloth.
level 50 when !zone "Felwood"
accept 8419 when !zone "Felwood"
section An Imp's Request (Ironforge)
tip At 50 Briarthorn in Ironforge sends you to Impsy in Felwood with a piece of Felcloth.
level 50 when !zone "Felwood"
accept 8419 when !zone "Felwood"
section An Imp's Request (Orgrimmar)
tip At 50 Zevrost in the Cleft of Shadow sends you to Impsy in Felwood with a piece of Felcloth.
level 50 when !zone "Felwood"
accept 8419 when !zone "Felwood"
section An Imp's Request (Undercity)
tip At 50 Kaal Soulreaper in the Magic Quarter sends you to Impsy in Felwood with a piece of Felcloth.
level 50 when !zone "Felwood"
accept 8419 when !zone "Felwood"
section Felcloth
tip One Felcloth: the Jadefire satyrs of Felwood drop it about one kill in fourteen, and so do the Legashi satyrs and the Felguard Sentries you hunt for Niby's essences. Quicker: buy one at the Auction House. You need it for the trainer's An Imp's Request or for Impsy's own Hot and Itchy, the same errand: whichever you hold.
section Impsy
tip Impsy waits beside Niby the Almighty on a rise just north-east of Bloodvenom Post: coming north over the Bloodvenom Falls bridge, they stand off the road to the east, past a few oozes. Hand him the trainer's An Imp's Request with the cloth. Next he wants ten Rotting Wood and four Bloodvenom Essence.
turnin 8419 when onquest 8419
section Impsy: Hot and Itchy
tip Impsy waits beside Niby the Almighty on a rise just north-east of Bloodvenom Post: coming north over the Bloodvenom Falls bridge, they stand off the road to the east, past a few oozes. Take his own Hot and Itchy and hand him the cloth at once. Next he wants ten Rotting Wood and four Bloodvenom Essence.
accept 8420 when !turnedin 8419
turnin 8420 when !turnedin 8419
section Rotting Wood and Bloodvenom
tip The Irontree treants (level 52) of Irontree Woods, in northern Felwood west of Talonbranch Glade, drop Rotting Wood one time in four; the big Withered Protector (55) often drops three at once but hits hard and dazes. The Tainted Oozes (51) around Impsy and along the Bloodvenom drop the essence one time in five.
accept 8421
objective 8421.1 collect
objective 8421.2 collect
section Impsy again
tip Impsy now wants six Voodoo Feathers from the Sunken Temple: a dungeon run.
turnin 8421
accept 8422
section The Sunken Temple
tip The Sunken Temple (Temple of Atal'Hakkar, level 50-56, a group of five) stands in the middle of the Pool of Tears: swim down into the temple and take the stairs to the entrance. The six troll guardians (level 51-52, elite) stand on the balconies around the central pit, each with adds; each drops his feather every time: Gasher and Zul'Lor the Amber, Hukku and Mijan the Blue, Zolo and Loro the Green. Not soloable at 52.
objective 8422.1 collect @ 69.0 54.0 map=1435
objective 8422.2 collect @ 69.0 54.0 map=1435
objective 8422.3 collect @ 69.0 54.0 map=1435
section Trolls of a Feather
tip Choose the Soul Harvester (staff), the Abyss Shard (off-hand) or the Robes of Servitude.
turnin 8422]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/incubus-alliance", title = "Succubus and Incubus (Alliance)", faction = "Alliance", class = "Warlock", levels = "20-25", zone = "Stormwind City", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/incubus-alliance"] = [==[guide: Succubus and Incubus (Alliance)
id: forever/class/warlock/incubus-alliance
level: 20-25
map: 1453
section Gakin's Summons (Gnomes)
tip At 20 Lago Blackwrench, the warlock trainer in Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern, sends you to Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind. Take the Deeprun Tram.
level 20
accept 1717
section Devourer of Souls
tip At 20 Gakin the Darkbinder, in the cellar of the Slaughtered Lamb in the Mage Quarter, sends you to Takar the Seer in the Barrens: a long trip for the Alliance. Take the boat from Menethil Harbor to Theramore and head west through Dustwallow Marsh, or the boat from Booty Bay to Ratchet.
level 20
turnin 1717 only Gnome
accept 1716
section Takar the Seer
tip Takar the Seer camps at a tent with a campfire just north-east of Camp Taurajo, by a fork in the road: Horde ground, so come in from the east and keep clear of the Taurajo guards. Doan Karhan beside him starts the Orb of Soran'ruk. Takar offers both branches: take both.
turnin 1716
accept 1738
accept 65602
section Heartswood
tip Ordil'Aran lies in north-west Ashenvale, north of Astranaar along the road toward Darkshore. About twenty Dark Strand cultists hold the ruins around the great tree: keep to the outer wall, and click the Heartswood from as far away as it lets you. It is turned in to Gakin, not to Takar.
objective 1738.1 collect
section The Wooden Figurine
tip The house stands alone in the trees of north-western Ashenvale, north-west of Ordil'Aran and well north of Maestra's Post: do it on the same trip as the Heartswood. Take the Unlit Torch from the table outside, light it at a campfire (a Basic Campfire of your own, or Talen's fire on Zoram Strand), and go straight back: the Burning Torch burns out after five minutes, so a fire of your own beside the house is quickest. Without it the figure in the house stops you. The figurine is upstairs.
objective 65602.1 collect
section The Binding: succubus
tip Back to Gakin with the Heartswood. He hands you the Heartswood Core: take the stairs behind him down to the crypt; part way along the lowest corridor a side stair on the left leads to the room with the purple circle. Stand on it and use the core. Summon your voidwalker first and keep the succubus (level 20, not elite) on the circle, or the guards may kill her and the kill does not count. If she wins, use the core again; keep it, Gakin takes it back.
turnin 1738
accept 1739
objective 1739.1 kill
turnin 1739
section The Binding: incubus
tip Give Gakin the figurine, then use the Wooden Figurine at the middle of the same circle and defeat the incubus it calls (level 20, not elite; it can charm you) with your voidwalker tanking. Keep the figurine: Gakin takes it back.
turnin 65602
accept 65603
objective 65603.1 kill
turnin 65603]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/incubus-horde", title = "Succubus and Incubus (Horde)", faction = "Horde", class = "Warlock", levels = "20-28", zone = "Orgrimmar", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/incubus-horde"] = [==[guide: Succubus and Incubus (Horde)
id: forever/class/warlock/incubus-horde
level: 20-28
map: 1454
section Devourer of Souls (Orgrimmar)
tip At 20 Gan'rul Bloodeye, in the Cleft of Shadow under the Valley of Strength, sends you to Cazul a few steps away. Two trainers start these demons, Gan'rul here and Carendin Halgar in the Undercity, and you can take only one; this guide follows whichever Devourer of Souls you took. Cazul offers both of Orgrimmar's branches: take both.
level 20
accept 1507
turnin 1507
accept 1508
accept 65601
section Zankaja
tip Zankaja lives in a hut up on the cliffs on the west side of the city, above the Valley of Strength: climb the wind rider tower, cross the bridge at its top to the west and turn right off it. She sends you to the Crossroads.
turnin 1508
accept 1509
section Magar
tip Magar keeps Magar's Cloth Goods on the main street east of the Cleft of Shadow. He asks you to look for his mate Krilge in Ashenvale.
turnin 65601
accept 65610
section Gazrog
tip Gazrog waits in front of the inn at the Crossroads. He sends you on to Ken'zigla at Malaka'jin, in Stonetalon Mountains.
turnin 1509
accept 1510
section Ken'zigla
tip Take the road west from the Crossroads into Stonetalon Mountains and, just past the border, the faint trail up to the left (south): Malaka'jin cannot be reached from the main road. Ken'zigla hands you her draught for Grunt Logmar.
turnin 1510
accept 1511
section Grunt Dogran
tip Grunt Logmar stands at Camp Taurajo, south down the road from the Crossroads. He sends you north to the quilboar camp where Dogran is held: the camp with two huts side by side, north-west of a decoy camp whose huts stand apart. A rare level 22 elite quilboar sometimes guards the huts: send your voidwalker in, sacrifice it if you must, and talk to Dogran. He gives you a pendant for Gan'rul. Keep it.
turnin 1511
accept 1515
turnin 1515
accept 1512
section The Binding: succubus (Orgrimmar)
tip Back to Gan'rul with the pendant. He hands you Dogran's Pendant: take it across the Cleft of Shadow to Neeru Fireblade's tent, stand on the purple circle and use it. Summon your voidwalker first and let it tank: the succubus (level 20, not elite) charms and lashes; keep your damage over time on her. If she wins, use the pendant again. Keep the pendant: Gan'rul takes it back.
turnin 1512
accept 1513
objective 1513.1 kill
turnin 1513
section Fallen Sky Lake
tip Fallen Sky Lake lies in southern Ashenvale, south-west of Splintertree Post. The Shadethicket Stone Movers and Bark Rippers (level 25-27) around the lake drop the Withered Scarf about one time in twenty, and the lone Shadethicket Oracle (30) can drop it too: plan on a good number of kills, so the guide waits for level 24 first (Forever made this quest level 27); with the succubus already bound you can leave it for your 20s leveling in Ashenvale. They respawn in five minutes.
level 24 when onquest 65610
objective 65610.1 collect when onquest 65610
section The Binding: incubus (Orgrimmar)
tip Back to Gan'rul with the scarf, then use the Withered Scarf on the same circle in Neeru's tent and defeat the incubus it calls (level 20, not elite) with your voidwalker tanking. Keep the scarf: Gan'rul takes it back.
turnin 65610
accept 65604
objective 65604.1 kill
turnin 65604
section Devourer of Souls (Undercity)
tip The Undercity's version, for warlocks who took Carendin Halgar's Devourer of Souls instead of Gan'rul's. At 20 Carendin, in the Magic Quarter, sends you to Godrick Farsan close by. Godrick shows you an image of each quarry and offers both branches: take both.
level 20
accept 1472
turnin 1472
accept 1476
accept 65593
section Silverpine hearts
tip Avelina Lilly (level 22) works as a tailor for the Dalaran wizards at Ambermill, in eastern Silverpine: the wizards around her are hostile. Dalin Forgewright (level 20, not elite) patrols near the Greymane Wall in the far south. Both are Alliance-friendly humans: attacking them can flag you for PvP. Each drops her or his heart.
objective 65593.1 collect
objective 1476.1 collect
section Corma Villard
tip Corma Villard (level 22, not elite; Comar in older records) wanders the north of the Wetlands just past the Thandol Span, to the right as you come off the bridge. From the Undercity head through Hillsbrad and Arathi Highlands, where the mobs are 30 and up. Attacking her flags you for PvP.
objective 1476.2 collect
section The Binding: succubus (Undercity)
tip Back to Carendin with Dalin's and Corma's hearts. He hands you the Pure Hearts: go down to the summoning circle below him, stand on it and use them. Summon your voidwalker first and keep the fight on the circle, or the guards may kill her and the kill does not count. If she wins, use the hearts again; keep them, Carendin takes them back.
turnin 1476
accept 1474
objective 1474.1 kill
turnin 1474
section Isaac Pearson
tip Isaac Pearson (level 22) works in Ratchet, on the Barrens coast, at one of two spots in town: take the zeppelin to Durotar and head south, or fly from Orgrimmar. He is an Alliance-friendly human: attacking him can flag you for PvP.
objective 65593.2 collect
section The Binding: incubus (Undercity)
tip Back to Carendin with the lovers' hearts, then place the Lovers' Hearts on the same circle and defeat the incubus they call (level 20, not elite; it can charm you). Keep the hearts: Carendin takes them back.
turnin 65593
accept 65597
objective 65597.1 kill
turnin 65597]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/orb-of-orahil", title = "Orb of Orahil", class = "Warlock", levels = "35-40", zone = "The Barrens", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/orb-of-orahil"] = [==[guide: Orb of Orahil
id: forever/class/warlock/orb-of-orahil
level: 35-40
map: 1413
section Knowledge of the Orb of Orahil (Stormwind)
tip At 35 Demisette Cloyce in the Slaughtered Lamb, in the Mage Quarter, sends you to Menara Voidrender in Ratchet.
level 35
accept 4968
section Knowledge of the Orb of Orahil (Ironforge)
tip At 35 Briarthorn in Ironforge sends you to Menara Voidrender in Ratchet.
level 35
accept 4965
section Knowledge of the Orb of Orahil (Orgrimmar)
tip At 35 Zevrost in the Cleft of Shadow sends you to Menara Voidrender in Ratchet.
level 35
accept 4967
section Knowledge of the Orb of Orahil (Undercity)
tip At 35 Kaal Soulreaper in the Magic Quarter sends you to Menara Voidrender in Ratchet. The zeppelin from Tirisfal Glades flies to Durotar.
level 35
accept 4969
section Menara Voidrender
tip Menara Voidrender and her two acolytes stand in Strahad Farsan's tower on the hill above Ratchet.
turnin 4968 only Human
turnin 4965 only Gnome
turnin 4967 only Orc,Troll
turnin 4969 only Undead
accept 1799
section Choose an acolyte
tip Pick one acolyte: you can take only one of their quests. Acolyte Wytula's felhound path ends with the Orb or Staff of Dar'Orahil, the shadow versions; Acolyte Magaz's infernal path with the Orb or Staff of Noh'Orahil, much the same items on the fire side. Most warlocks lean on shadow, but compare the four in their tooltips first. The guide follows the one you take. Keep the ruby or the emerald: it is handed back.
accept 4962
accept 4963
section Mannoroc Coven
tip Mannoroc Coven fills south-central Desolace, east of Shadowprey Village. The Burning Blade Summoners (level 38-39, warlocks with imps) carry the Infernal Orb every time. For the spirit, bring your demon to low health with your damage over time, then channel the ruby or the emerald on it and keep channelling while it dies, as with Drain Soul: the gem does no damage of its own. The ruby works on the coven's felhounds: the two Mana Eaters (37-38) in the north, and the Mage Hunters (38) and Ley Hunters (39) further south. The emerald works on the Lesser Infernals (36-37, sixteen of them, fire-resistant).
objective 1799.1 collect
objective 4962.1 collect
objective 4963.1 collect
section The demon's spirit
tip Back to Menara in the tower above Ratchet with the spirit and the gem first: her orb follows from it.
turnin 4962
turnin 4963
section Tabetha
tip Tabetha lives at her farm in the middle of Dustwallow Marsh, south of the road from the Barrens and south-west of Theramore; a spirit healer stands beside it. Deadmire, a level 45 crocolisk, patrols the creeks just north-east. Hand in the orb now; Cleansing waits for level 38. Before you accept it, clear the spiders and crocolisks around her paddock. Accepting starts a 3-minute timer: she walks to the paddock and lets the Demon of the Orb out. It is elite (level 40): grouping up is encouraged; a warlock of about 40 can solo it with Fear or Banish and damage over time, a level 38 one brings a friend. The timer keeps running after the kill, so hand in at once. If time runs out, abandon the quest and take it from Tabetha again.
turnin 1799
level 38
accept 4961
objective 4961.1 kill
turnin 4961
accept 4976
section The Orb of Dar'Orahil
tip Back to Menara in the tower above Ratchet with the cleansed orb. On the felhound path, accept her last quest and wait beside her while she completes the Orb of Dar'Orahil (do not attack her: the quest log calls it a kill), then speak to her again and pick the off-hand orb or the staff.
turnin 4976
accept 4964
complete 4964 @ 62.5 35.4 map=1413
turnin 4964
section The Orb of Noh'Orahil
tip On the infernal path, accept her last quest and wait beside Menara while she completes the Orb of Noh'Orahil, then speak to her again and pick the off-hand orb or the staff.
accept 4975
complete 4975 @ 62.5 35.4 map=1413
