HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/orb-of-soranruk", title = "Orb of Soran'ruk", class = "Warlock", levels = "22-30", zone = "The Barrens", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/orb-of-soranruk"] = [==[guide: Orb of Soran'ruk
id: forever/class/warlock/orb-of-soranruk
level: 22-30
map: 1413
section Doan Karhan
tip Doan Karhan camps beside Takar the Seer, at a tent just north-east of Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. Alliance warlocks reach him from Ratchet or Theramore; Horde ones head south from the Crossroads. He wants fragments from two dungeons: take the quest before your Blackfathom Deeps and Shadowfang Keep runs.
level 20
accept 1740
section Blackfathom Deeps
tip Blackfathom Deeps (level 24-32, a group of five) opens in the ruins on the north-west coast of Ashenvale, under the water at Zoram Strand. The Twilight Acolytes (level 24-25, elite, healers) stand in the last halls, around Twilight Lord Kelris and the altar before Aku'mai; each one drops a fragment, but only three spawn in a run and they do not come back for two hours, so one run covers one warlock: kill them first, before they heal the rest.
objective 1740.1 collect @ 14.5 14.2 map=1440
section Shadowfang Keep
tip Shadowfang Keep (level 22-30, a group of five) stands on the hill south of the Sepulcher. Free the prisoner in the cells right of the entrance and he opens the way into the courtyard. The Shadowfang Darksouls (level 20-21, elite) are not in the courtyard: they walk the halls past it, up the ramp that curves left and in the building after. About twelve stand in a run and one in five drops the Large Fragment, so clear every Darksoul and run it again if it does not drop.
objective 1740.2 collect @ 44.8 67.8 map=1421
section Back to Doan Karhan
tip Choose the off-hand Orb of Soran'ruk or the two-handed Staff of Soran'ruk.
turnin 1740]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/shard-of-the-green-flame", title = "Shard of the Green Flame", class = "Warlock", levels = "50-56", zone = "Felwood", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/shard-of-the-green-flame"] = [==[guide: Shard of the Green Flame
id: forever/class/warlock/shard-of-the-green-flame
level: 50-56
map: 1448
section Niby the Almighty
tip At 50 Niby the Almighty and his imp Impsy wait on a rise in central Felwood just north-east of Bloodvenom Post: coming north over the Bloodvenom Falls bridge, they stand off the road to the east, past a few oozes. Niby sends you to Impsy, beside him, who wants three Flawless Fel Essences from three places.
level 50
accept 7601
turnin 7601
accept 7602
section Azshara
tip The Legashi satyrs (level 51-53) hold the Legash Encampment on Azshara's northern coast. Every kind drops the essence three times in four; the satyrs burn mana and the Hellcallers rain fire, so pull them singly.
objective 7602.1 collect
section Jaedenar
tip Jaedenar lies just south of Bloodvenom Post, west of the road. The guide waits for level 53 first: its Legionnaires are 55. Of its two caves, Shadow Hold is the northern one, further up the hill; the other has no Legionnaires. Shadow Hold's tunnels run north under the hills, and the Jaedenar Legionnaires (level 55) stand in its deeper halls, from the first ramps on toward Lord Banehollow's chamber; they Uppercut anyone in melee. Three kills in four give the essence, but only about eleven spawn: clear your way in and wait out a five-minute respawn if you must. The cultists of Jaedenar and Shadow Hold are all hostile.
level 53
objective 7602.2 collect
section The Dark Portal
tip The Felguard Sentries (level 54) walk around the Dark Portal in the south of the Blasted Lands, each with a felhunter. Leave the level 57 Servants of Razelikh alone: they cannot be killed without their own quest.
objective 7602.3 collect
section Impsy
tip Back to Impsy. He hands you the Fel Fire: keep it, it wakes the infernal Kroshius.
turnin 7602
accept 7603
section Kroshius
tip Kroshius' remains lie in Shatter Scar Vale, the burnt crater north of Niby: follow the road north from his camp; the remains lie a little east of it. Use the Fel Fire beside them and wait for him to rise. Kroshius is elite (level 55): grouping up is encouraged; a warlock of 55 or more can solo him with Fear and damage over time, or with Enslave Demon, but fire spells do nothing to him and he knocks you back. If you die he heals to full; he rises again three minutes after he dies. An elite infernal patrols the pool south of the remains: pull Kroshius away from it. He always drops his core. Lost the Fel Fire? Abandon the quest and take it again from Impsy.
objective 7603.1 kill
objective 7603.2 collect
section Back to Niby
turnin 7603]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/tome-of-sacrifice", title = "Tome of Sacrifice", class = "Warlock", levels = "60-60", zone = "Blasted Lands", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/tome-of-sacrifice"] = [==[guide: Tome of Sacrifice
id: forever/class/warlock/tome-of-sacrifice
level: 60-60
map: 1419
section Daio the Decrepit
tip At 60 Daio the Decrepit waits in the Tainted Scar, the demon-filled hollow in the west of the Blasted Lands. The Scar is full of hard-hitting elites: Soulstone yourself first, then keep to the right-hand wall going in, or ride through mounted. Daio gives you two errands at once.
level 60
accept 7581
accept 7582
section Satyr Blood
tip The Wildspawn satyrs (level 55-57, elite) fill the Warpwood Quarter, Dire Maul's eastern wing: bring a group of five. Four in five drop a blood, but they do not come back for two hours and one full clear may come up short of fifteen; reset and run it again. The back door at Lariss Pavilion needs the Crescent Key, which drops inside this wing; until someone has it, go in by Dire Maul's main gate in central Feralas.
objective 7581.1 collect @ 59.2 45.1 map=1444
section Tears of the Hederine
tip The Hederine demons (level 57-60, elite) hold Darkwhisper Gorge in the far south of Winterspring: grouping up is encouraged. Two Slayers guard the gorge past the bridge; the western tunnel leads to more Initiates, the easiest of them (watch for their Dominate Mind). A warlock can solo them one at a time with Fear or Banish and damage over time, but slowly. Any of them can drop the Tears, four kills in five.
objective 7582.1 collect
section Suppression
tip Hand both in to Daio and take the Glowing Crystal Prison. Find a Doomguard Commander (level 61, elite) standing alone in the Tainted Scar, open from about 30 yards with your voidwalker on him, and channel the prison on him for about 20 seconds: he attacks you to break free, and his War Stomp can interrupt the channel, so sacrifice the voidwalker for its shield if you must. Grouping up is encouraged: a second player to tank makes it easy. When the channel finishes he becomes the Imprisoned Doomguard: click it. If the channel breaks, kill him or run, and try another.
turnin 7581
turnin 7582
accept 7583
objective 7583.1 use @ 34.5 63.7 map=1419
objective 7583.1 collect
section Back to Daio
turnin 7583]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/voidwalker-alliance", title = "Voidwalker (Alliance)", faction = "Alliance", class = "Warlock", levels = "10-12", zone = "Elwynn Forest", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/voidwalker-alliance"] = [==[guide: Voidwalker (Alliance)
id: forever/class/warlock/voidwalker-alliance
level: 10-12
map: 1429
section Gakin's Summons (Humans)
tip At 10 Remen Marcot, in the cellar of the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire (the stairs down are in the back room past the butcher's table), sends you to Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind.
level 10
accept 1685
section The Slaughtered Lamb (Gnomes)
tip At 10 Lago Blackwrench, the warlock trainer in Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern, sends you to Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind. Take the Deeprun Tram from Tinker Town. If Lago does not offer it, go to Gakin anyway: he still gives you the next quest.
level 10
accept 1715
section Gakin the Darkbinder
tip The Slaughtered Lamb is the tavern in the Mage Quarter; Gakin is in its cellar, down the stairs inside.
turnin 1685 only Human
turnin 1715 only Gnome
accept 1688
section Surena Caledon
tip Surena Caledon (level 9) is inside the farmhouse at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, south-east Elwynn near the Redridge road. Morgan the Collector (level 10) and a warrior stand with her and join the fight; Morgan gouges and goes for your imp, so keep him Feared. Put your damage over time on Surena first, Fear the others, and loot her choker before you finish them: it stays yours even if you die after. She throws fireballs from range and is back three minutes after she dies. Have the quest before you kill her, or the choker does not drop.
objective 1688.1 collect
section The Binding
tip Back to Gakin. He hands you the Bloodstone Choker. The circle is hard to find: take the stairs behind Gakin down; part way along the lowest corridor a side stair on the left leads into a room with a glowing purple circle in the middle. Stand on it and use the choker. The voidwalker (level 10, not elite) gets dangerous below 30% health: Curse of Agony, Corruption and Immolate with your imp on it, Fear when it gets close. If it beats you, use the choker again. Keep the choker: Gakin takes it back.
turnin 1688
accept 1689
objective 1689.1 kill
turnin 1689]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warlock/voidwalker-horde", title = "Voidwalker (Horde)", faction = "Horde", class = "Warlock", levels = "10-12", zone = "Durotar", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warlock/voidwalker-horde"] = [==[guide: Voidwalker (Horde)
id: forever/class/warlock/voidwalker-horde
level: 10-12
map: 1411
section Gan'rul's Summons (Orcs and Trolls)
tip At 10 Ophek sends you to Gan'rul Bloodeye. He stands outside at the back of Razor Hill's barracks, the big building on the east side of town (not the inn), a few steps from Dhugru Gorelust, the warlock trainer. Gan'rul stands with the senior warlocks in the Cleft of Shadow, the cavern under Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. An Orc or Troll leveling in Tirisfal Glades can take the Undercity version from Ageron Kargal in Brill instead (the Undercity steps below): you can do only one of the two.
level 10
accept 1506
turnin 1506
accept 1501
section Skull Rock
tip Skull Rock is the cave in the cliffs just east of Orgrimmar's gate. Inside, take the right-hand ramp up and follow it to the top: the Burning Blade Stash sits on that upper ledge, which cannot be reached from the lower floor. The cave is packed with Burning Blade Apprentices and Fanatics (level 9-11, many with voidwalkers) that respawn quickly, and Gazz'uz, a level 14 Burning Blade warlock, stands near the stash. Old notes call him elite; Forever's data lists him as normal. At 10 it is hard alone: pull one pack at a time and Fear the extra, wait for 11, or go with a friend. The stash always holds the tablet.
objective 1501.1 collect
section The Binding (Orgrimmar)
tip Back to Gan'rul. He hands you the Glyphs of Summoning: take them across the Cleft of Shadow to Neeru Fireblade's tent, stand on the purple circle on its floor and use them. The voidwalker (level 10, not elite) hits hard at 30% health and leaves after three minutes, so start at once: Curse of Agony, Corruption and Immolate, send your imp in, and Fear it when you need a breather. If it beats you or leaves, the glyphs are not used up: use them again on the circle. Keep the glyphs: Gan'rul takes them back.
turnin 1501
accept 1504
objective 1504.1 kill
turnin 1504
section Halgar's Summons (Undercity)
tip At 10 Ageron Kargal, upstairs in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, sends you to Carendin Halgar: the version for the Undead, and for Orcs and Trolls who level in Tirisfal Glades instead of taking Gan'rul's. Carendin stands in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, by the Temple of the Damned.
level 10
accept 1478
turnin 1478
accept 1473
section Perrine's Chest
tip The Scarlet tower stands in the fields west of the Undercity's ruins (not the tower near Deathknell). The grimoire is in the small chest on the ground floor, under the stairs; ignore the chest upstairs. Captain Perrine (level 9) and a Scarlet Zealot guard it: kill them, or Fear the zealot while you deal with Perrine. Scarlet Missionaries and Zealots (level 7-9) walk the fields around the tower. The chest is back three seconds after anyone opens it.
objective 1473.1 collect
section The Binding (Undercity)
tip Back to Carendin. He hands you the Runes of Summoning: go down the stairs from him to the summoning circle and use them while standing on it. Fight the voidwalker (level 10, not elite) on the circle: if it wanders off, the city guards may kill it and the kill does not count. Curse of Agony, Corruption and Immolate with your imp tanking bring it down; it hits harder below 30%. If you lose, use the runes again. Keep the runes: Carendin takes them back.
turnin 1473
accept 1471
objective 1471.1 kill
turnin 1471]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warrior/brutal-armor", title = "Brutal Armor", faction = "Horde", class = "Warrior", levels = "20-32", zone = "The Barrens", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warrior/brutal-armor"] = [==[guide: Brutal Armor
id: forever/class/warrior/brutal-armor
level: 20-32
map: 1413
section Speak with Ruga (Orgrimmar)
tip At 20, Sorek in the Valley of Honor sends you to Ruga Ragetotem in Camp Taurajo.
level 20
accept 1823
section Speak with Ruga (Thunder Bluff)
tip At 20, Torm Ragetotem, the warrior trainer of Thunder Bluff, sends you to Ruga Ragetotem in Camp Taurajo.
level 20
accept 1823
section Speak with Ruga (Undercity)
tip At 20, Baltus Fowler, a warrior trainer of the Undercity, sends you to Ruga Ragetotem in Camp Taurajo.
level 20
accept 1823
section Ruga Ragetotem
tip Fly to Camp Taurajo. Ruga stands in the hut with the leatherworking and tailoring trainers.
turnin 1823
accept 1824
section Trial at the Field of Giants
tip You have 30 minutes, and each Twitching Antenna rots 15 minutes after you loot it, so take the quest only when ready (logging out does not stop the clock). The Silithid Mounds dot the Field of Giants south of Camp Taurajo; every silithid drops an antenna. Creepers (level 20-21) and Grubs are the easiest: Swarmers (21-22) call small swarms and Creepers lay eggs that hatch adds. The eastern part of the field has plenty of Creepers. Ruga's Bulwark, a shield, is the reward.
objective 1824.1 collect
turnin 1824
accept 1825
section Thun'grim Firegaze
tip Thun'grim's hut sits on top of Thorn Hill, east of the Crossroads: climb the broad ridge on the north or east side. Brutal Armor is a level 30 quest; take it now and gather on the way. Thun'grim's Instructions list where each material comes from.
turnin 1825
accept 1838
section Windshear Mine
tip You need 15 Smoky Iron Ingots. The Windshear Mine lies at the east end of Windshear Crag, east of Sun Rock Retreat; every Windshear kobold (level 19-23) drops an ingot four kills in five. Stonecutters, Geomancers and Overlords run for help when low; Geomancers cast Frostbolt.
objective 1838.1 collect
section Hillsbrad Miners
tip You need 10 Powdered Azurite. The guide waits for level 25 first. The Hillsbrad Miners (level 26-27) work the mine in the hills west of Southshore and drop the azurite four kills in five; they fight in Defensive Stance, sunder your armor and run for help at 30% health. Fly to Tarren Mill and head south-west.
level 25
objective 1838.2 collect
section Roogug in Razorfen Kraul
tip Roogug is an elite quilboar (level 28) inside Razorfen Kraul, the dungeon at the south end of the Barrens; a five-player dungeon: needs a group of five, his guards come with him. The guide waits for level 26 first. Inside take the left path at the first fork, cross the vine bridge over the pig pens, go past the room with the big cauldron: he waits in the room on the right. He casts Lightning Bolt and calls Earth Rumblers. The vial always drops.
level 26
objective 1838.4 collect @ 42.9 90.2 map=1413
section Iron Bars
tip You need 10 Iron Bars. Miners smelt them from Iron Ore (one ore a bar, Smelt Iron at Mining 125); everyone else buys them at the auction house in Orgrimmar.
objective 1838.3 collect @ 55.9 62.7 map=1454
section Brutal Hauberk
tip Back to Thun'grim on Thorn Hill. Brutal Hauberk is the first piece; he then sends you to three crafters, one per piece: take all three.
turnin 1838
accept 1848
turnin 1848
accept 1839
accept 1840
accept 1841
section Ula'elek
tip Ula'elek is in Sen'jin Village on the Durotar coast. He wants 7 Uncloven Satyr Hooves.
turnin 1839
accept 1842
section Satyr Hooves
tip The satyrs of Satyrnaar, north-east of Splintertree Post (Xavian, level 28-30), and the Felmusk satyrs north-west of the post (25-27) drop a hoof four kills in five. A Xavian satyr at 15% health may cast Gift of the Xavian and heal to full: finish it fast or stun it. Hellcallers throw Fireballs from 40 yards; Felmusk satyrs reek in melee and run for help at 15%.
objective 1842.1 collect
section Brutal Gauntlets
turnin 1842
accept 1843
turnin 1843
section Orm Stonehoof
tip Orm Stonehoof works on Thunder Bluff's lowest level, close to the blacksmith.
turnin 1840
accept 1844
section Chimaeric Horn
tip The Chimaera Matriarch (level 28, not elite, larger than the young ones around her) roams the south edge of the Charred Vale in south-west Stonetalon, near the road to Desolace. She is the only one: she returns 5 minutes after dying and drops the Galvanized Horn four kills in five. She spits Corrosive Poison from 30 yards.
objective 1844.1 collect
section Brutal Helm
turnin 1844
accept 1845
turnin 1845
section Velora Nitely
tip Take the zeppelin from Orgrimmar to Tirisfal Glades; Velora Nitely works in the Undercity's Trade Quarter. She wants 8 Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbones.
turnin 1841
accept 1846
section Dragonmaw Shinbones
tip The Dragonmaw orcs (level 26-30) camp in the middle of the Wetlands; from Hammerfall in Arathi head south over the Thandol Span (Menethil Harbor is Alliance). With Dragonmaw Shinbones from Velora in your log, every Raider, Swamprunner, Centurion, Shadowwarder and Bonewarder drops a Dragonmaw Shinbone (without the quest they drop none): right-click it to test it, and about one in four comes out sturdy, the rest break, so expect 30 or more kills for 8. You can test while moving or fighting. The orcs run for help at 15%; Raiders net you, Centurions shield-bash, Shadowwarders cast Shadow Bolt, Bonewarders raise skeletons.
objective 1846.1 collect when onquest 1846
section Brutal Legguards
turnin 1846
accept 1847
turnin 1847]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warrior/fire-hardened-armor", title = "Fire Hardened Armor", faction = "Alliance", class = "Warrior", levels = "20-30", zone = "Redridge Mountains", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warrior/fire-hardened-armor"] = [==[guide: Fire Hardened Armor
id: forever/class/warrior/fire-hardened-armor
level: 20-30
map: 1433
section Yorus Barleybrew (Stormwind)
tip At 20, Wu Shen, beside Ilsa Corbin in the warrior trainers' building of Old Town, sends you to Yorus Barleybrew in Redridge.
level 20
accept 1698
section Yorus Barleybrew (Ironforge)
tip At 20, Kelv Sternhammer, the warrior trainer of Ironforge, sends you to Yorus Barleybrew in Redridge.
level 20
accept 1698
section Yorus Barleybrew (Darnassus)
tip At 20, Darnath Bladesinger, the warrior trainer of Darnassus, sends you to Yorus Barleybrew in Redridge.
level 20
accept 1698
section Yorus Barleybrew
tip Yorus Barleybrew sits in the inn at Lakeshire. His test is timed: before you take it, clear the Redridge gnolls on the path to the Rethban Caverns in the hills north-west of Lakeshire, including the two on the rock by the cave mouth (climb it from its right side).
turnin 1698
accept 1699
section The Rethban Gauntlet
tip You have one hour, and Yorus's Barleybrew Scalder leaves you drunk for 8-10 minutes. Run north-west into the Rethban Caverns, keeping close to the cliff wall to miss most gnoll packs, and go in as far as the first fork; then come back to Yorus (from the ridge you can jump down into Lakeshire). Dying and releasing your spirit fails the quest: abandon it and Yorus gives it again.
complete 1699
turnin 1699
accept 1702
section The Shieldsmith
tip Furen Longbeard works in the Dwarven District of Stormwind. He takes the Cask of Scalder (lost it? abandon the quest and Yorus gives a new one) and gives you Furen's Favor, a shield; Fire Hardened Mail is a level 28 quest, with Furen's Instructions listing what it needs.
turnin 1702
accept 1701
section Scorched Spider Fangs
tip You need 50 fangs. The Leech Stalkers and Cave Stalkers (level 21-22) crawl in the middle of the Wetlands, north of Dun Algaz; every one drops a fang. They poison; back in 5 minutes.
objective 1701.1 collect
section Charred and Galvanized Horns
tip The chimaeras live south-west of Sun Rock Retreat in the Charred Vale; the guide waits for level 26 first. You need 12 Charred Horns from the Fledgling (level 25-27) and Young Chimaeras (23-25), four kills in five, and the Galvanized Horn from the Chimaera Matriarch (28, the big one), also four in five. Only three Fledglings, two Young and one Matriarch live there, each back in 5 minutes, so expect to wait. Fledglings and the Matriarch spit Corrosive Poison, the Young cast Lightning Bolt. Alliance: fly to Stonetalon Peak and head south.
level 26
objective 1701.2 collect
objective 1701.3 collect
section Roogug in Razorfen Kraul
tip Roogug is an elite quilboar (level 28) inside Razorfen Kraul, the dungeon at the south end of the Barrens; a five-player dungeon: needs a group of five, and his guards come with him. Inside take the left path at the first fork, cross the root bridge, go past the big empty cauldron: he is in a dead end on the right, with about ten elites on the way. He casts Lightning Bolt and calls Earth Rumblers. The vial always drops.
objective 1701.4 collect @ 42.9 90.2 map=1413
section Furen's Armor
tip Back to Furen Longbeard in the Dwarven District for the hauberk. He then sends you to the smith of your race; the other two smiths' pieces are open to you as well: talk to them directly.
turnin 1701
accept 1782
turnin 1782
accept 1700 only Human
accept 1703 only NightElf
accept 1704 only Dwarf,Gnome
section Grimand Elmore
tip Grimand Elmore keeps the weapon shop in the north-west of the Dwarven District, a short walk from Furen. He wants 20 Burning Blood and the Burning Rock.
turnin 1700 only Human
accept 1705
section Burning Blood
tip The Nightbane worgen of Duskwood (Dark Runners, Vile Fangs, Shadow Weavers, Worgen and Tainted Ones, level 26-31) south and west of Darkshire drop the Burning Blood four kills in five. The Tainted Ones poison and howl; Vile Fangs cause Infected Wound.
objective 1705.1 collect
section Gutspill
tip Gutspill (level 32, not elite) carries the Burning Rock, four kills in five; the guide waits for level 30 first. He walks between the inside and the mouth of the Roland's Doom mine south-east of Darkshire, so wait at the entrance and pull him outside. He poisons and howls.
level 30
objective 1705.2 collect
section Grimand's Armor
turnin 1705
accept 1706
turnin 1706
section Mathiel
tip Mathiel works on the south side of the Warrior's Terrace in Darnassus. He wants 20 Sunscorched Shells.
turnin 1703
accept 1710
section Sunscorched Shells
tip The shells lie on the ground under the wyvern nests at Highperch in western Thousand Needles, deeper into the gorge. Only nine exist and each returns 3 minutes after you pick it, so you will wait; some shell-like things there cannot be looted. Highperch Wyverns (level 28-31) guard them and sometimes come several at once.
objective 1710.1 collect
section Mathiel's Armor
turnin 1710
accept 1711
turnin 1711
section Klockmort Spannerspan
tip Ride the Deeprun Tram from Stormwind to Ironforge. Klockmort Spannerspan, a gnome smith, works in Tinker Town near the engineering trainers. He wants 20 Searing Coral.
turnin 1704
accept 1708
section Iron Coral
tip The Iron Coral grows on the sea floor just south of Menethil Harbor, by the murloc huts and a wrecked boat: eight there and two south-east of the harbor, each back in 3 minutes, so you will wait for respawns to reach 20. The murlocs can net you underwater: watch your breath, and a Draught of Water Breathing removes the risk.
objective 1708.1 collect
section Klockmort's Creation
turnin 1708
accept 1709
turnin 1709]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warrior/haggards-weapons", title = "Defensive Stance and a Weapon (Alliance)", faction = "Alliance", class = "Warrior", levels = "10-11", zone = "Elwynn Forest", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warrior/haggards-weapons"] = [==[guide: Defensive Stance and a Weapon (Alliance)
id: forever/class/warrior/haggards-weapons
level: 10-11
map: 1429
section Seena Skybreaker in Valanaar
tip At 10, Seena Skybreaker stands with the trainers by Valanaar's west gate. A cultist, Zaal Stormshield, holds her family's shield at the Shrine of Akir.
level 10
accept 94003
section Zaal Stormshield
tip Head north-west from Valanaar to the Shrine of Akir. Zaal Stormshield stands west of the shrine's approach, among the cult's Guardians, Spiritcallers and Blademasters: pull them one at a time before you take him. He drops the Skybreaker Bulwark.
objective 94003.1 collect
section The Skybreaker Bulwark
tip Back to Seena in Valanaar. She teaches Defensive Stance and gives you the Stormforged Protector, a shield to use it with. Bartleby's road below still gives a weapon, once you reach Stormwind.
turnin 94003
section Muren Stormpike
tip At 10, Granis Swiftaxe, the warrior trainer in Kharanos, sends you to Muren Stormpike in Ironforge. Any Alliance warrior may take one of the three roads, never two: in Stormwind at 10 anyway? Ilsa Corbin's A Warrior's Training is the quickest stance (one fight in a tavern), with a Haggard's weapon after it.
level 10
accept 1679
section Muren Stormpike in Ironforge
tip Muren Stormpike stands in the Hall of Arms in the Military Ward.
turnin 1679
accept 1678
section Vejrek
tip Vejrek (level 11, a lone troll) waits at his hut on a hill south of Frostmane Hold, near the mountains at the top of a short ramp, with no other trolls around; the hut at the front of Frostmane Hold is the wrong one. He fights in Defensive Stance and sunders your armor; Thunder Clap slows him. His head always drops; he returns about 8 minutes after dying.
objective 1678.1 collect
section Tormus Deepforge
tip Back to Muren for Defensive Stance, then to Tormus Deepforge at the Great Forge in the middle of Ironforge.
turnin 1678
accept 1680
turnin 1680
accept 1681
section Ironband's Compound
tip Ironband's Compound lies in eastern Dun Morogh, below Helm's Bed Lake on its south side. Dark Iron Spies (level 8-10) stand along the way, far enough apart to pull one at a time. Ironband's Strongbox is in the basement of the southernmost house; Captain Beld (level 11) stands by it and charges on sight. The box always holds the ore and refills 15 minutes after opening.
objective 1681.1 collect
section Grey Iron Weapons
turnin 1681
accept 1682
turnin 1682
section Elanaria
tip At 10, Kyra Windblade, the warrior trainer in Dolanaar, or Moon Priestess Amara, who patrols the road west of Dolanaar, sends you to Elanaria on the Warrior's Terrace in Darnassus. Any Alliance warrior may take one of the three roads, never two: in Stormwind at 10 anyway? Ilsa Corbin's A Warrior's Training teaches the same stance after one fight in a tavern.
level 10
accept 1684
section Elanaria in Darnassus
tip Elanaria stands on the Warrior's Terrace.
turnin 1684
accept 1683
section Vorlus Vilehoof
tip Vorlus Vilehoof (level 10, a satyr) stands at a hidden moonwell up a hillside west of Dolanaar. The trail is hard to spot: it starts behind a Gnarlpine camp and climbs in switchbacks lined with lamp posts. The furbolgs below can come in groups. His horn always drops; he returns 5 minutes after dying.
objective 1683.1 collect
section The Shade of Elura
turnin 1683
accept 1686
section Elunite under Auberdine
tip Take the boat from Rut'theran Village to Auberdine. The wreck lies underwater just south of Auberdine's southern pier, where the Menethil boat docks. Open Crates of Elunite on the sea floor around the wreck, by a huge sunken turtle, toward the beach and under the pier until you have eight; every crate holds ore and comes back in 3-5 minutes. The grey Shade of Elura (level 11) drifts around the middle of the wreck and always drops the medallion: target it when you see it, so you can find it after surfacing for air. Watch your breath; Threshers can join in.
objective 1686.1 collect
objective 1686.2 collect
section Smith Mathiel
tip Back on the Warrior's Terrace: Elanaria hands you the Case of Elunite; Mathiel works on the far, south side of the same terrace, easy to miss.
turnin 1686
accept 1692
turnin 1692
accept 1693
turnin 1693
section A Warrior's Training
tip At 10, Lyria Du Lac, the warrior trainer by the inn in Goldshire, sends you to Harry Burlguard in Stormwind; Ilsa Corbin, the warrior trainer in Stormwind's Old Town, offers it too.
level 10
accept 1638
section Bartleby
tip Harry Burlguard and Bartleby are in the Pig and Whistle tavern in Old Town; Bartleby is the drunk at the far end of the bar. Bartleby (level 10) hits harder than his level, so start at full health; he gives up at low health instead of dying. If he wins, he disappears for about three minutes: keep the quest and talk to him again when he is back. A Dwarf, Gnome or Night Elf who took A Warrior's Training from Ilsa Corbin instead of their home road is led through Stormwind from here.
turnin 1638 when !turnedin 1684
accept 1639 when !turnedin 1684
turnin 1639 when !turnedin 1684
accept 1640 when !turnedin 1684
objective 1640.1 kill when !turnedin 1684
turnin 1640 when !turnedin 1684
accept 1665 when !turnedin 1684
turnin 1665 when !turnedin 1684
accept 1666 when !turnedin 1684
section Marshal Haggard
tip Marshal Haggard's manor stands at the south-east edge of the Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn, at the end of a short road that does not join the main one.
turnin 1666 when !turnedin 1684
accept 1667 when !turnedin 1684
section Dead-tooth Jack
tip Dead-Tooth Jack (level 11) camps in the far south-east of Elwynn. A guard stands beside him and Defias and wolves are spread around the camp (now and then a rarer guard too): clear them one at a time, then kill Jack. He always drops Dead-tooth's Key; open Dead-tooth's Strongbox in the crates by him for Marshal Haggard's Badge. Jack returns 3 minutes after dying, the box 1 minute after opening.
objective 1667.1 collect when !turnedin 1684
section Back to Marshal Haggard
turnin 1667 when !turnedin 1684]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warrior/heirloom-weapon", title = "Defensive Stance and a Weapon (Horde)", faction = "Horde", class = "Warrior", levels = "10-11", zone = "The Barrens", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warrior/heirloom-weapon"] = [==[guide: Defensive Stance and a Weapon (Horde)
id: forever/class/warrior/heirloom-weapon
level: 10-11
map: 1413
section Seena Skybreaker in Valanaar
tip At 10, Seena Skybreaker stands with the trainers by Valanaar's west gate. A cultist, Zaal Stormshield, holds her family's shield at the Shrine of Akir.
level 10
accept 94003
section Zaal Stormshield
tip Head north-west from Valanaar to the Shrine of Akir. Zaal Stormshield stands west of the shrine's approach, among the cult's Guardians, Spiritcallers and Blademasters: pull them one at a time before you take him. He drops the Skybreaker Bulwark.
objective 94003.1 collect
section The Skybreaker Bulwark
tip Back to Seena in Valanaar. She teaches Defensive Stance and gives you the Stormforged Protector, a shield to use it with. Uzzek's road below still gives a weapon later, once you reach Kalimdor.
turnin 94003
section Veteran Uzzek (Razor Hill)
tip At 10, Tarshaw Jaggedscar, the warrior trainer in the barracks of Razor Hill, sends you to Uzzek in the Barrens. Sorek in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor offers it too. Any Horde warrior may take one of the two roads, never both: heading to Tirisfal Glades at 10 anyway? Austil de Mon in Brill's inn offers the other: one fight by Brill's graveyard for the same stance, then the Agamand crypt for an heirloom weapon.
level 10
accept 1505
section Veteran Uzzek (Mulgore)
tip At 10, Krang Stonehoof, the warrior trainer of Bloodhoof Village, sends you to Uzzek in the Barrens. Torm Ragetotem in Thunder Bluff offers it too.
level 10
accept 1505
section Uzzek at Far Watch Post
tip Uzzek is easy to miss: he stands under a small canopy by a large tree just west of Far Watch Post, below the road's south side, with the post in sight to his east. Going straight south from the post does not lead to him. From Durotar cross the bridge west; from Mulgore head north past the Crossroads.
turnin 1505
accept 1498
section Singed Scales in Thunder Ridge
tip You need five Singed Scales. Thunder Lizards (level 9-10) and Lightning Hides (10-11) live down in the Thunder Ridge crevasse in north-west Durotar, south of Orgrimmar: from the Barrens bridge turn left and follow the river north into it. Both drop a scale about four kills in five; both cast Lizard Bolt.
objective 1498.1 collect
section Path of Defense
tip Back to Uzzek under his tree west of Far Watch Post.
turnin 1498
accept 1502
section Thun'grim Firegaze
tip Thun'grim's hut sits on top of Thorn Hill, east of the Crossroads. Most slopes are too steep: climb the broad ridge on the north or east side.
turnin 1502
accept 1503
section Forged Steel
tip The Stolen Iron Chest stands by a broken wagon in the Razormane camp north-west of Thun'grim, north-east of the Crossroads. Two Razormanes guard it and their hunters pull more quilboar: clear them one at a time, then open the chest (it refills within seconds, so a friend can loot it too).
objective 1503.1 collect
turnin 1503
section Speak with Dillinger
tip At 10, Austil de Mon, the warrior trainer inside the inn of Brill, sends you to Deathguard Dillinger by the graveyard on Brill's west edge. This road and Uzzek's exclude each other: drop Veteran Uzzek or Path of Defense from your log if you hold one.
level 10
accept 1818
section Deathguard Dillinger
tip Dillinger stands by the graveyard on Brill's west edge. An Orc, Troll, Tauren or Skyborne who took Speak with Dillinger from Austil de Mon instead of Uzzek's road is led through Brill from here.
turnin 1818 when !turnedin 1505
accept 1819 when !turnedin 1505
section Ulag the Cleaver
tip Ulag sleeps in the mausoleum in the graveyard just north of Dillinger. To wake him, click the flat skull plaque on the ground, left of the path to the mausoleum door; the seal lifts and Ulag (level 11, not elite) walks out. Start at full health.
objective 1819.1 kill when !turnedin 1505
turnin 1819 when !turnedin 1505
accept 1820 when !turnedin 1505
section Coleman Farthing
tip Coleman Farthing is in the Gallows' End Tavern, the inn on Brill's east side.
turnin 1820 when !turnedin 1505
accept 1821 when !turnedin 1505
section The Agamand Family Crypt
tip The four Agamand Weapon Racks are inside the Agamand Family Crypt at the north end of Agamand Mills, north of Brill, one rack per room: one in the lowest room, two in the pair of rooms up the stairs, one in the room above those. The axe rack stands in a dark corner. The crypt's undead come in packs of three or more and return quickly; the ones in the top room are not linked. The axe, dagger and mace racks take 15 minutes to refill after someone loots them.
objective 1821.1 collect when !turnedin 1505
objective 1821.2 collect when !turnedin 1505
objective 1821.3 collect when !turnedin 1505
objective 1821.4 collect when !turnedin 1505
section Back to Coleman Farthing
turnin 1821 when !turnedin 1505
accept 1822 when !turnedin 1505
turnin 1822 when !turnedin 1505]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warrior/quelserrar", title = "Quel'Serrar", class = "Warrior, Paladin", levels = "60-60", zone = "Feralas", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warrior/quelserrar"] = [==[guide: Quel'Serrar
id: forever/class/warrior/quelserrar
level: 60-60
map: 1444
section Nostro's Compendium of Dragon Slaying
tip The book is a rare random drop from the bosses of all three Dire Maul wings (Alzzin, Hydrospawn and the rest of the East, Tendris, Illyanna, Kalendris, Immol'thar and the West, King Gordok and the North's guards) and very rarely from the tribute chest; it can be traded, so the auction house may have one. Dire Maul is a five-player dungeon in the ruins of central Feralas: needs a group of five. Right-click the book to start the quest; it stays in your bags.
accept 7507
section Lorekeeper Lydros
tip Lorekeeper Lydros stands in the Athenaeum, the library at the far end of Dire Maul West, past the Court of the Highborne and the Prison of Immol'thar. The West door needs the Crescent Key, which Pusillin drops in Dire Maul East (he runs; chase him), or a rogue to pick it. Clearing to the library needs your group of five. He takes the book, hands you A Dull and Flat Elven Blade to give straight back, then the Unfired Ancient Blade. Keep that blade: lose it, and you must abandon the quest and take it again.
turnin 7507 @ 59.2 45.1 map=1444
accept 7508 @ 59.2 45.1 map=1444
turnin 7508 @ 59.2 45.1 map=1444
accept 7509 @ 59.2 45.1 map=1444
section Onyxia's breath
tip Onyxia is the 40-player raid boss of Onyxia's Lair, a cave in the Wyrmbog of southern Dustwallow Marsh; she returns once a week. Tell the raid first. Late in the fight (around 10-15% health, when she has landed again) use the Unfired Ancient Blade to plant it in the path of her fire breath, usually by the main tank's feet. When her breath has heated it, click the Ancient Heated Blade to take the Heated Ancient Blade: from then you have 20 minutes. Her breath can kill you while you plant or pick up the blade; if you die and nobody brings you back before she dies, wait for next week. Planted in the wrong place? Abandon the quest, take it again from Lydros for a new blade.
section Onyxia's corpse
tip Kill Onyxia, then target her corpse and use the Heated Ancient Blade on it before the 20 minutes run out. It becomes the Treated Ancient Blade, with no time limit.
objective 7509.1 use @ 52.1 75.8 map=1445
objective 7509.1 collect @ 52.1 75.8 map=1445
section The Forging of Quel'Serrar
tip Back to Lorekeeper Lydros in the Athenaeum of Dire Maul West: through the West door with the Crescent Key again, and a group to reach the library.
turnin 7509 @ 59.2 45.1 map=1444]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warrior/voodoo-feathers", title = "Voodoo Feathers", class = "Warrior", levels = "50-52", zone = "Swamp of Sorrows", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warrior/voodoo-feathers"] = [==[guide: Voodoo Feathers
id: forever/class/warrior/voodoo-feathers
level: 50-52
map: 1435
section A Troubled Spirit (Stormwind)
tip At 50, Wu Shen, beside Ilsa Corbin in the warrior trainers' building of Old Town, sends you to the Fallen Hero of the Horde in the Swamp of Sorrows.
level 50
accept 8417
section A Troubled Spirit (Ironforge)
tip At 50, Kelv Sternhammer, the warrior trainer of Ironforge, sends you to the Fallen Hero of the Horde in the Swamp of Sorrows.
level 50
accept 8417
section A Troubled Spirit (Darnassus)
tip At 50, Darnath Bladesinger, the warrior trainer of Darnassus, sends you to the Fallen Hero of the Horde in the Swamp of Sorrows.
level 50
accept 8417
section A Troubled Spirit (Orgrimmar)
tip At 50, Sorek in the Valley of Honor sends you to the Fallen Hero of the Horde in the Swamp of Sorrows.
level 50
accept 8417
section A Troubled Spirit (Thunder Bluff)
tip At 50, Torm Ragetotem, the warrior trainer of Thunder Bluff, sends you to the Fallen Hero of the Horde in the Swamp of Sorrows.
level 50
accept 8417
section A Troubled Spirit (Undercity)
tip At 50, Christoph Walker, a warrior trainer of the Undercity, sends you to the Fallen Hero of the Horde in the Swamp of Sorrows.
level 50
accept 8417
section The Fallen Hero of the Horde
tip The Fallen Hero of the Horde, a ghost, stands in the south-west of the Swamp of Sorrows, at the pass into the Blasted Lands, a short ride south-west of Stonard. Horde: fly to Stonard. Alliance: fly to Nethergarde Keep in the Blasted Lands and ride north through the pass. High-level beasts roam the way.
turnin 8417
accept 8423
section Helboars
tip Seven Helboars (level 52-53, not elite) roam the north-west of the Blasted Lands, south-west of Nethergarde Keep; some stand near the ogres on the mountainside by the road. They charge from 25 yards and cast Fire Nova. They share spawn points with the Felbeasts and scorpids: if no boars are around, kill those and boars may appear instead. Back in 5 minutes.
objective 8423.1 kill
section War on the Shadowsworn
turnin 8423
accept 8424
section Shadowsworn camps
tip The Shadowsworn camp around the mouth of the Serpent's Coil cave, south of Nethergarde Keep on the way to the Dark Portal. You need 20 Adepts (level 52-53, they leech blood and heal hurt allies: kill them first), 10 Cultists (51-52, they throw from range, so close in) and 20 Thugs (52-53, Thrash and Kick). Thugs can run short before the others: kill every Shadowsworn you pass.
objective 8424.1 kill
objective 8424.2 kill
objective 8424.3 kill
section Voodoo Feathers
turnin 8424
accept 8425
section The Sunken Temple
tip You need two feathers of each colour from the six Atal'ai troll guardians (level 51-52, elite) on the Sunken Temple's balcony, who hold the barrier in front of Jammal'an the Prophet: Gasher and Zul'Lor drop the amber, Hukku and Mijan the blue, Zolo and Loro the green, every kill; each player on the quest loots their own set. The Sunken Temple is a five-player dungeon: needs a group of five. It lies in the Pool of Tears in eastern Swamp of Sorrows: climb the temple's outer steps, dive into the flooded hall and follow the stairs down to the entrance. Inside, reach the balcony by the stairs or the path on the right, not the spiral stairs. Hukku calls guardians and casts Shadow Bolt Volley and Curse of Blood; Mijan heals the others (Renew, a Healing Ward, Healing Wave below half health): kill her or her ward fast; Zul'Lor cleaves.
objective 8425.1 collect @ 69.9 53.6 map=1435
objective 8425.2 collect @ 69.9 53.6 map=1435
objective 8425.3 collect @ 69.9 53.6 map=1435
section Back to the Fallen Hero
turnin 8425
tip In Classic the Fallen Hero let you choose the Diamond Flask, the Fury Visor or the Razorsteel Shoulders here. Forever's change notes say the choice is gone, though its quest page still lists three unnamed rewards: look at the reward window before you hand in.]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/class/warrior/whirlwind-weapon", title = "Whirlwind Weapon", class = "Warrior", levels = "30-40", zone = "The Barrens", category = "Class" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/class/warrior/whirlwind-weapon"] = [==[guide: Whirlwind Weapon
id: forever/class/warrior/whirlwind-weapon
level: 30-40
map: 1413
section The Islander (Stormwind)
tip At 30, Wu Shen, beside Ilsa Corbin in the warrior trainers' building of Old Town, sends you to Klannoc Macleod on Fray Island in the Barrens.
level 30
accept 1718
section The Islander (Ironforge)
tip At 30, Kelv Sternhammer, the warrior trainer of Ironforge, sends you to Klannoc Macleod on Fray Island in the Barrens.
level 30
accept 1718
section The Islander (Orgrimmar)
tip At 30, Sorek in the Valley of Honor sends you to Klannoc Macleod on Fray Island in the Barrens.
level 30
accept 1718
section The Islander (Thunder Bluff)
tip At 30, Torm Ragetotem, the warrior trainer of Thunder Bluff, sends you to Klannoc Macleod on Fray Island in the Barrens.
level 30
accept 1718
section The Islander (Undercity)
tip At 30, Baltus Fowler, a warrior trainer of the Undercity, sends you to Klannoc Macleod on Fray Island in the Barrens.
level 30
accept 1718
section Fray Island
tip Fly to Ratchet and go south along the Merchant Coast. Fray Island lies offshore to the south-east: wade across on the shallow sand bar; off it the water is deep and fatigue sets in. Klannoc Macleod stands by the arena.
turnin 1718
accept 1719
section The Affray
tip You have 10 minutes. Eat and drink to full, then step onto the grate in the middle of the crowd: Twiggy Flathead announces the challengers (level 26-27), who come one at a time, 15-20 seconds apart, and only while you stand near the grate. After each kill, step off the grate to eat or bandage; step back on when ready for the next. Six of them, then Big Will (level 33, not elite) walks out; he stays neutral until you attack him, so bandage or eat first. Do not use Demoralizing Shout: it sends the challengers running and more of them pile in at once. If nothing starts, step off and on the grate again, or abandon the quest and take it again.
objective 1719.1 kill @ 68.6 48.7 map=1413
turnin 1719
accept 1791
section Bath'rah the Windwatcher
tip Bath'rah the Windwatcher camps by ruins on the east bank of the river that runs past Tarren Mill, a short walk north-east of the town, just over the border in Alterac Mountains; his cauldron stands beside him. Horde: fly to Tarren Mill. Alliance: fly to Southshore and go north along the river; Tarren Mill's guards are level 42 elites, so keep away from the town. Accepting Cyclonian gives you Bath'rah's Parchment, the list of what he needs: 8 Liferoot, 30 Bloodscalp Tusks and the Essence of the Exile from his cauldron. The cauldron's Essence of the Exile is not a quest you take: it never shows in your quest log. Come back with its charms and hand them in at the cauldron.
turnin 1791
accept 1712
section Liferoot
tip You need 8 Liferoot. Herbalists pick it by rivers and lakes in the Wetlands, Arathi Highlands and Stranglethorn Vale; otherwise the auction house. Herb vendors keep only one at a time and restock every two hours: Bernard Gump and Maria Lumere in Stormwind, Antonio Perelli on the road in eastern Elwynn, Jeeda at Sun Rock Retreat in Stonetalon, Montarr in Thousand Needles. Kurzen Medicine Men in northern Stranglethorn drop one about one kill in twelve.
objective 1712.1 collect
section Bloodscalp Tusks
tip You need 30 tusks. Every Bloodscalp troll (level 33-37) of north-west Stranglethorn drops one about one kill in three, so plan on some 80 kills: the camps and ruins north and north-west of Grom'gol Base Camp and around the Bal'lal Ruins on the coast. They enrage below 30% health and the Warriors disarm; back in 5 minutes.
objective 1712.2 collect
section The exiles of Arathi
tip The cauldron wants 8 of each charm, 24 in all, and each exile drops its charm about one kill in three, so plan on some 70 kills. All are level 38-39, not elite: the guide waits for level 37 first, and a friend helps. Burning Exiles (fire) by the Circle of West Binding in the north-west, north-west of Refuge Pointe; Thundering Exiles (air) by the Circle of Outer Binding south-east of Refuge Pointe, casting Lightning Bolt from 40 yards; Cresting Exiles (water) by the Circle of East Binding, north-west of Hammerfall, with Frost Nova. About a dozen of each, back in under 7 minutes. The charms trade and sell on the auction house; using one banishes another kind of exile for a while (Burning on Thundering, Thundering on Cresting, Cresting on Burning).
level 37
section Essence of the Exile
tip Click Bath'rah's Cauldron with the 24 charms in your bags and Cyclonian in your log. Its window asks for the charms straight away, with nothing to accept: Continue, then Complete, and it hands you the Essence of the Exile.
turnin 1714
objective 1712.3 collect @ 80.5 66.9 map=1416
section The Summoning
tip Back to Bath'rah. Accepting The Summoning starts his ritual, and Cyclonian appears just north of his camp. Cyclonian is elite (level 40): grouping up is encouraged; it needs a group of two or three around level 40. It deals nature damage (a Nature Protection Potion soaks it), whirls, and Knock Away throws you far while it heals itself as you run back: fight with your back to a slope or rock. The Whirlwind Heart always drops. If the fight fails Bath'rah stops answering: abandon The Summoning and take it again for a new summon; the earlier items are not needed again.
turnin 1712
level 38
accept 1713
objective 1713.1 collect
turnin 1713
accept 1792
