accept 545
note Krusk now offers Gol'dir (level 36): leave it for the 38-39 visit.
turnin 515
section Elixir of Agony with a group
tip Lydon's next errand is a keg of Shindigger Stout from the cellar of Dun Garok, the elite dwarven keep south-east of Southshore: take it only if you go there with a group.
accept 517 when turnedin 515
section Battle of Hillsbrad with a group
tip Darthalia's last battle is at Dun Garok, the dwarven keep south-east of Southshore: every dwarf there is elite (28-32), Captain Ironhill too. Great XP if you have a group for it.
accept 541 when group 541
section Humbert's Sword with a group
tip Deathguard Humbert's sword drops from the same Dun Garok dwarves (about one in twelve).
accept 547 when group 547
section Dun Garok
tip Clear Dun Garok from the gate in; the dwarves run for help at 30% health.
objective 541.1 kill @ 71.2 79.0 map=1424 when onquest 541,547
objective 541.2 kill @ 71.0 78.3 map=1424 when onquest 541,547
objective 541.3 kill @ 71.6 79.2 map=1424 when onquest 541,547
objective 541.4 kill @ 72.2 79.8 map=1424 when onquest 541,547
objective 547.0 collect @ 71.2 79.0 map=1424 when onquest 541,547
section Tarren Mill
turnin 541 when onquest 541
accept 550 when onquest 541
section Deathguard Humbert
turnin 547 when onquest 547
section Shindigger keg
tip The Kegs of Shindigger Stout stand in the cellar of Dun Garok, the dwarven keep south-east of Southshore, beside Captain Ironhill (32); every dwarf there is elite (28-32).
objective 517.0 collect @ 72.0 80.5 map=1424 when onquest 517
section Back to Tarren Mill
tip Head back north to Tarren Mill.
turnin 517 when onquest 517
accept 524 when onquest 517
turnin 524 when onquest 517
section Arathi Highlands
goto 32.6 40.4 Boulderfist camp map=1417
section Boulderfist camp
tip Head east out of Tarren Mill through Thoradin's Wall and follow the road east. The Boulderfist Ogres and Enforcers (32-34) camp south of the road, south of Northfold Manor; the Enforcers stay in the cave there.
objective 676.1 kill
objective 676.2 kill
section Level 31
tip Hammerfall's quests are 32-36. Below 31? Keep killing the Boulderfist Ogres and Enforcers at this camp until level 31. Or, with a group, run the Scarlet Monastery dungeon (Graveyard) or the Blackfathom Deeps dungeon instead.
goto 31.2 48.0 Boulderfist camp map=1417 when level<31
level 31 when level<31
section Hammerfall
tip The orc stronghold at the eastern end of the road. Urda, the wind rider master, stands by the gate.
tip Rutherford Twing offers the Defiler's Basic Care Package only once you are Friendly with the Defilers (Arathi Basin): skip it if he doesn't offer it.
accept 655
getfp Hammerfall
turnin 8263
turnin 676
accept 677
turnin 655
accept 672
accept 671
accept 97539
section Witherbark Village
tip South of Hammerfall, the Witherbark trolls hold the village in the hills. Axe Throwers guard the outer huts; the Witch Doctors and Headhunters hold the heart of the village. Careful: All three troll types flee for help at 15% health, which can pull more trolls from the nearby camps.
objective 677.2 kill
objective 677.1 kill
objective 677.3 kill
section Highland raptors and Plains Creepers
tip On the way back north, Highland Striders roam the hills all around Hammerfall and drop the eyes, and south of it the Plains Creepers (32-33) spin their webs in the grass; they carry the spidersilk.
objective 672.0 collect
objective 97539.0 collect @ 69.5 50.5 map=1417
section Hammerfall
tip Back north to Hammerfall.
turnin 97539
turnin 672
accept 674
turnin 677
turnin 674
accept 675
turnin 675
note Tor'gan's Guile of the Raptor, Drum Fel's next Call to Arms and the doctor's Ward Restocking wait for the 38-39 visit.
section Fly to Undercity
goto 73.1 32.7 Hammerfall flight master map=1417
fly Undercity
section Varimathras
tip Varimathras stands beside Sylvanas in the Royal Quarter.
turnin 550 when onquest 550
section Undercity trainers
tip Train while you are in the Undercity: the trainers stand in the War Quarter, the Rogues' Quarter and the Magic Quarter (Paladins: Garen Largo).
train]==]
HawarysGuides.list[#HawarysGuides.list + 1] = { id = "forever/horde/30-40/02-thousand-needles", title = "Thousand Needles & Desolace", faction = "Horde", levels = "32-34", zone = "Thousand Needles", next = "forever/horde/30-40/03-stranglethorn-vale" }
HawarysGuides.text["forever/horde/30-40/02-thousand-needles"] = [==[guide: Thousand Needles & Desolace
id: forever/horde/30-40/02-thousand-needles
level: 32-34
map: 1441
section Zeppelin to Orgrimmar
goto 60.7 58.8 Zeppelin to Orgrimmar map=1420
section Alliance Relations
tip The zeppelin lands at the tower outside Orgrimmar's main gate. Craven Drok walks the Drag: if he isn't at the arrow, look along its streets to the south-west. Keldran stands in the Valley of Spirits on the west side of the city.
accept 1431
turnin 1431
accept 1432
section Orgrimmar trainers
tip Train while you are in the city.
train
section Searn Firewarder
tip Searn Firewarder stands in the Valley of Wisdom.
accept 1531
section Nogg
tip Nogg's workshop is in the Valley of Honor. Rig Wars is Gnomeregan's last boss: great XP if you run it with a group. Run it whenever your group is ready; hand it in on a later Orgrimmar stop.
accept 2841 when dungeon "Gnomeregan"
section Gnomeregan
note Run Gnomeregan with a group when it suits you: Mekgineer Thermaplugg at the end drops his Safe Combination; open his safe behind the northern bomb pillar for the Rig Blueprints. when dungeon "Gnomeregan"
section Orgrimmar flight master
goto 45.3 63.7 Orgrimmar flight master map=1454
section Thunder Bluff
tip Fly from Orgrimmar to Thunder Bluff and train with Turak Runetotem on Elder Rise; fly on to Freewind Post from there.
fly Thunder Bluff
train
section Islen Waterseer
tip Fly from Orgrimmar to Ratchet. Islen Waterseer camps on the coast a short walk south of the town; fly on to Freewind Post from Ratchet.
fly Ratchet
turnin 96
section Fly to Freewind Post
goto 46.7 49.9 Thunder Bluff flight master map=1456
fly Freewind Post
section Fly to Freewind Post
goto 63.1 37.1 Ratchet flight master map=1413
fly Freewind Post
section Fly to Freewind Post
fly Freewind Post
section Prate Cloudseer
tip Prate Cloudseer hides in a small cave in the canyon wall north-east of the post, on the way east.
turnin 1531
note Prate also starts Elemental Aid (Razorfen Kraul), the 33-40 chain to The Tempest's Weapons: forever/class/shaman/call-of-air-horde.
section Moktar Krin
tip Take the lift down and follow the canyon east. Moktar Krin camps on the north-western edge of the salt flats.
turnin 1146
accept 1147
section Mirage Raceway
tip The goblins and gnomes of the Mirage Raceway are neutral and give quests to both factions.
accept 1110
accept 5762
accept 1104
accept 1105
accept 1176
accept 1175
section The southern flats
tip South of the raceway, the Saltstone Crystalhides (32-33) and Gazers (34-35) roam the far end of the flats.
objective 1175.2 kill @ 78.4 87.9 map=1441
objective 1175.3 kill @ 77.1 88.4 map=1441
section The Rustmaul Dig Site
tip West of them the silithid swarm the dig site. Searchers and Hive Drones walk among the mounds; the Invaders (34-35) stay inside the hive cave. The first silithid you kill drops a Cracked Silithid Carapace: open it.
tip Careful: Hive Drones call for help when they fall to 20% health.
objective 1147.1 kill @ 69.8 83.3 map=1441
objective 1147.2 kill @ 68.0 85.7 map=1441
objective 1147.3 kill @ 64.8 86.0 map=1441
accept 1148
section Parts of the Swarm
tip Keep killing silithid at the dig site for the heart, the talons and the carapaces.
objective 1148.1 collect
objective 1148.2 collect
objective 1148.3 collect
section Moktar Krin
tip North from the dig to Moktar Krin's camp on the western edge of the flats.
turnin 1147
section Shimmering Flats: kill these as you meet them
tip East onto the flats. The Saltstone Basilisks (30-31) sun themselves north-west of it; the Sparkleshell tortoises crowd round a half-buried ship in the north-east, and the Salt Flats Scavengers and Vultures circle the eastern flats. Every vulture drops a bone, about one tortoise in three a shell.
tip Careful: Scavengers and Vultures use Execute when your health is low; the Snappers (34-35) hit hardest of the tortoises.
